S `eval`","locale":"en"},"5366":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-23","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"decide on CEL vs. custom evaluator before Phase 4 finishes; reject expressions until then","locale":"en"},"5367":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-24","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"Dynamic code","locale":"en"},"5368":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-25","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"Rust has no module registry; dylib unloading unsound","locale":"en"},"5369":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-26","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"static catalog first; WASM backend for real hot reload/sandboxing","locale":"en"},"5370":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-27","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"Type-level keys","locale":"en"},"5371":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-28","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"string keys can collide; `TypeId` unstable across dylibs","locale":"en"},"5372":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-29","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"`TypeId` check in-process; string + version tag for dynamic modules (paper §6.6)","locale":"en"},"5373":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-30","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"Error-message parity","locale":"en"},"5374":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-31","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"TS messages/columns (UTF-16)","locale":"en"},"5375":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-32","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"keep message wording where cheap; no UTF-16 parity","locale":"en"},"5376":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-33","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"How these were settled in the code:","locale":"en"},"5377":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-34","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"**Reentrancy:** critical sections queue `Action`s on the state (see Concurrency); values released under the lock are dropped after it.","locale":"en"},"5378":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-35","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"**Reference cycles:** there is no `Root` type or `shutdown()`. Disposing the root fiber, `root.fiber().dispose().await`, restarts it and reverts everything registered on it, which withdraws every binding.","locale":"en"},"5379":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-36","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"**Expressions:** decided as a side-effect-free JavaScript subset (`kardia_loader::expr`), not CEL; see Status and deviations.","locale":"en"},"5380":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-37","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"**Dynamic code:** the static catalog came first; the WASM, dylib and process backends followed (see Dynamic modules).","locale":"en"},"5381":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-38","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#risks","content":"**Type-level keys:** the in-process check is the downcast at access (`AccessError::TypeMismatch`). Guest services cross the module boundary as JSON values with JSON calls (`GuestService`), so no Rust type or `TypeId` crosses it.","locale":"en"},"5382":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-39","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#worked-example","content":"A provider and a consumer, written against the plugin API. The first tab is the example in today's API (it compiles and runs against the workspace once `connect` and its pool, placeholders for a real database client, are supplied); the second is the plan's original sketch of the then-future API.","locale":"en"},"5383":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-40","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#worked-example","content":"What changed between the sketch and the code:","locale":"en"},"5384":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-41","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#worked-example","content":"**Root:** `Context::new()` creates the root context; `root.fiber().dispose()` replaces `root.shutdown()`.","locale":"en"},"5385":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-42","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#worked-example","content":"**Errors:** `Result<()>` (`kardia_core::Result`) replaces `Result<(), PluginError>` and `anyhow::Result`.","locale":"en"},"5386":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-43","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#worked-example","content":"**Declarations:** `fn inject() -> Inject` (here `Inject::of::<(Database,)>()`) replaces `type Inject`, and `fn provide() -> Vec<Key>` replaces the `&'static [&'static str]` slice. `#[derive(Service)]` implements `Service` (the hand-written `impl Service for Database` also works). With the `#[plugin]` macro, a plugin is an `async fn` taking `Injected<(Database,)>`, which turns undeclared access into a compile error (see Plugins).","locale":"en"},"5387":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-44","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#worked-example","content":"**Boundaries:** `ctx.checkpoint()?` and `ctx.on_dispose(..)?` are synchronous and fallible.","locale":"en"},"5388":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-45","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#worked-example","content":"**Configuration:** `ctx.plugin::<P>(config)` requires `P::Config: Serialize` (the value is serialized and decoded like any other configuration), so a `Deserialize`-only config is passed as JSON with `plugin_value`. `db.update(value)?` validates at once and returns the future to await; `update_with(value, no_save)` takes the flag.","locale":"en"},"5389":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-46","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#worked-example","content":"**Settling:** `greeter.settled()` resolves as soon as no transition is in flight, so the example first waits for `db` to settle; the greeter's transitions start once the database is provided.","locale":"en"},"5390":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-47","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#worked-example","content":"**Logger:** `ctx.logger_named(\"greeter\")`, or `ctx.logger()`, which is named after the plugin.","locale":"en"},"5391":{"id":"/en/docs/development-risks-48","page_id":"/en/docs/development-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-risks#worked-example","content":"**Dependencies:** `#[derive(Deserialize)]` needs `serde` with the `derive` feature among the crate's own dependencies, even though `kardia::prelude` re-exports the derive.","locale":"en"},"5392":{"id":"/en/docs/development-status","page_id":"/en/docs/development-status","type":"page","content":"Status and deviations","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-status","locale":"en"},"5393":{"id":"/en/docs/development-status-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-status","content":"The implementation phases of kardia, their exit criteria, the implementation status, and every place where the implementation departs from the plan or from the TypeScript code.","locale":"en"},"5394":{"id":"/en/docs/development-status-1","page_id":"/en/docs/development-status","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-status#phases","content":"Implementation phases","locale":"en"},"5395":{"id":"/en/docs/development-status-2","page_id":"/en/docs/development-status","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-status#status","content":"Implementation status","locale":"en"},"5396":{"id":"/en/docs/development-status-3","page_id":"/en/docs/development-status","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-status#deviations","content":"Deviations","locale":"en"},"5397":{"id":"/en/docs/development-status-4","page_id":"/en/docs/development-status","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-status#errors","content":"Errors","locale":"en"},"5398":{"id":"/en/docs/development-status-5","page_id":"/en/docs/development-status","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-status#loader-hooks","content":"Loader hooks","locale":"en"},"5399":{"id":"/en/docs/development-status-6","page_id":"/en/docs/development-status","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-status#dynamic-modules","content":"Dynamic modules","locale":"en"},"5400":{"id":"/en/docs/development-status-7","page_id":"/en/docs/development-status","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-status#typescript","content":"The TypeScript side","locale":"en"},"5401":{"id":"/en/docs/development-status-8","page_id":"/en/docs/development-status","tags":[],"type":"text"