"},"6837":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"The identity matters when replacing a plugin: `root.registry().replace(&old, &new)` swaps the implementation behind every running instance of `old`, keeping their place in the tree and their configuration. This is what hot reload does; `provider_consumer` shows it.","locale":"en"},"6838":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"`Context::new()` creates a root context. Plugins started from a context become its children:","locale":"en"},"6839":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6840":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"Takes","locale":"en"},"6841":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"`ctx.plugin::<P>(config)`","locale":"en"},"6842":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"A typed configuration (`P::Config` must also be `Serialize`)","locale":"en"},"6843":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"`ctx.plugin_value::<P>(value)`","locale":"en"},"6844":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"A JSON configuration","locale":"en"},"6845":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"`ctx.plugin_def(&def, value)`","locale":"en"},"6846":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"A `PluginDef` and a JSON configuration","locale":"en"},"6847":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"`ctx.inject(inject, f)`","locale":"en"},"6848":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"Dependencies and a closure","locale":"en"},"6849":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"Each returns a `Fiber`, the handle to that running instance. Starting a plugin is itself an effect of the calling plugin, so a child stops when its parent stops. Stopping the root (`root.fiber().dispose().await`) reverts everything.","locale":"en"},"6850":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"The fiber handle offers:","locale":"en"},"6851":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6852":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Does","locale":"en"},"6853":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`state()`","locale":"en"},"6854":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`Pending` (waiting for dependencies), `Loading`, `Active`, `Unloading`, `Failed` or `Disposed`","locale":"en"},"6855":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`settled().await`","locale":"en"},"6856":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Waits until no transition is in flight; fails with the plugin's error","locale":"en"},"6857":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`update(value)?.await`","locale":"en"},"6858":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Replaces the configuration (below)","locale":"en"},"6859":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`update_with(value, no_save)`","locale":"en"},"6860":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"The same; `no_save: true` skips the write-back to a config file","locale":"en"},"6861":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`restart().await`","locale":"en"},"6862":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Unloads and loads the plugin again","locale":"en"},"6863":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`dispose().await`","locale":"en"},"6864":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Stops the plugin and removes it","locale":"en"},"6865":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`error()`","locale":"en"},"6866":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"The error of the last failed load","locale":"en"},"6867":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`context()`, `config()`, `name()`, `parent()`, `effects()`","locale":"en"},"6868":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Introspection","locale":"en"},"6869":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"A `Failed` plugin recovers only through `update`, `restart` or a replacement.","locale":"en"},"6870":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"The configuration enters as JSON (from a config file, `plugin_value` or `update`) and is decoded once per load into `Config`, with serde:","locale":"en"},"6871":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"A decoding error names the failing path, such as `invalid config: … (at items.1)`.","locale":"en"},"6872":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"Unknown fields are tolerated, unless the config type opts into `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]`.","locale":"en"},"6873":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"A missing configuration (`null`) is read as an empty object, so a config type whose fields all have defaults (`#[serde(default)]`) accepts it. `()` accepts anything.","locale":"en"},"6874":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"`fiber.update(value)` validates the new configuration first: a rejected configuration leaves the running instance untouched. The new configuration is then offered to the plugin's update hooks. If no hook takes it over, the plugin restarts.","locale":"en"},"6875":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"`ctx.on_update_with` does the same with a hook that returns the future `update` should wait for. A hook is an effect, so it goes away with the plugin.","locale":"en"},"6876":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#stopping-cleanly","content":"Everything a plugin registers through its context is an effect that is reverted when it stops: provided services, listeners, timers, child plugins, and plain disposers such as `ctx.on_dispose(…)`. Effects covers effects in full; two points matter while writing `apply`:","locale":"en"},"6877":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#stopping-cleanly","content":"**Register the inverse right after acquiring a resource**, so that nothing leaks if the plugin is stopped while starting.","locale":"en"},"6878":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#stopping-cleanly","content":"**`ctx.checkpoint()?`** is a point where a superseded load stops. It returns `Err(Interrupted)` when the plugin's target changed since the load began (it was updated, disposed or lost a dependency). Returning that error from `apply` is not a failure: the plugin unloads what it registered so far. kardia never cancels a running `apply` by itself.","locale":"en"},"6879":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"The loader resolves the `name` of each entry. To load your own plugins from a config file, register them in a `kardia::loader::Catalog` and pass it to `Loader::plugin`:","locale":"en"},"6880":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"`kardia::catalog()` holds every built-in plugin except `hmr` (which needs a module graph, see Hot reload), under its name and its TypeScript package name; `kardia::loader::builtins()` holds only `group`.","locale":"en"},"6881":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"An entry name that is not in the catalog fails with `ModuleNotFound`, located at the entry's `name`.","locale":"en"},"6882":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"`Loader::plugin` takes any `kardia::loader::Resolver`; `Catalog` is one. The `kardia` binary uses its own resolver that falls back to guest modules for names that are not built-in plugins: `crates/kardia/src/main.rs` shows the full setup, including `hmr`.","locale":"en"},"6883":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"<Card title=\"Services\" href=\"/docs/guide-services\" description=\"Caller attribution, interception, events and the logger.\" />","locale":"en"},"6884":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"<Card title=\"Effects\" href=\"/docs/guide-effects\" description=\"Effects, disposers, effect scopes and teardown.\" />","locale":"en"},"6885":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"<Card title=\"Loader\" href=\"/docs/guide-loader\" description=\"Entries, groups, isolation and include from Rust.\" />","locale":"en"},"6886":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"<Card title=\"API design\" href=\"/docs/development-design\" description=\"Why the plugin API looks the way it does.\" />","locale":"en"},"6887":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"page","content":"Services, events and logging","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services","locale":"en"},"6888":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services","content":"Provide and consume services, attribute calls to their caller, isolate and intercept services, dispatch events and log.","locale":"en"},"6889":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"Defining a service","locale":"en"},"6890":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"Providing a service","locale":"en"},"6891":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"Declaring dependencies","locale":"en"},"6892":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Accessing services","locale":"en"},"6893":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"Compile-time checked access","locale":"en"},"6894":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`Svc<T>` and the caller","locale":"en"},"6895":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"Interception metadata","locale":"en"},"6896":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"Isolation","locale":"en"},"6897":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"Events","locale":"en"},"6898":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"Listening","locale":"en"},"6899":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Dispatching","locale":"en"},"6900":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"Built-in events","locale":"en"},"6901":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"Hooks","locale":"en"},"6902":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"Logging","locale":"en"},"6903":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"Exporters","locale":"en"},"6904":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#example","content":"A complete example","locale":"en"},"6905":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services","content":"A **service** is a value that one plugin provides and other plugins depend on. The runtime tracks who provides what and who depends on what: a plugin that declares a service starts once the service is available, restarts when it is replaced, and stops when it goes away. This page shows how to define, provide and consume services, how calls are attributed to their caller, how isolation and interception change what a context sees, and how to use events and the logger.","locale":"en"},"6906":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services","content":"For the theory behind services see Reactive coeffects; for why the Rust API looks the way it does (string keys, `Svc<T>`, no `Proxy`) see API design; every place where kardia behaves differently from the TypeScript Cordis is listed on Status and deviations.","locale":"en"},"6907":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"A service is any `Send + Sync + 'static` type bound to a **key** through the `Service` trait:","locale":"en"},"6908":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"Keys are strings because configuration files name services (`inject: [database]`). The runtime stores each value together with its type, so a key reached with the wrong Rust type fails with `AccessError::TypeMismatch` instead of being misread.","locale":"en"},"6909":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"Usually you derive the trait:","locale":"en"},"6910":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"Without `name`, the key is the type name hyphenated: `Database` → `database`, `FooBar` → `foo-bar`. `#[service(crate = …)]` points the generated code at `::kardia`; without it, it refers to `::kardia_core`.","locale":"en"},"6911":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"**Associated services.** Cordis's `foo.bar` associated services and `ctx.mixin` are JavaScript-object conveniences. In kardia a service named `foo.bar` is just another key. To \"extend\" another plugin's type, use an extension trait (compile time, see `Svc<T>` and the caller) or a registry service built on `kardia_core::IdTable` (run time). No accessor or mixin layer is ported.","locale":"en"},"6912":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"Providing is an **effect** of the current fiber: it is reverted when the fiber unloads (see Revertible effects). Every method returns `Result<EffectHandle>`.","locale":"en"},"6913":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6914":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"Provides","locale":"en"},"6915":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide(value)`","locale":"en"},"6916":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"a `Service` under `S::NAME`","locale":"en"},"6917":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_arc(arc)`","locale":"en"},"6918":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"an `Arc<S>` you already hold","locale":"en"},"6919":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_as(key, value)`","locale":"en"},"6920":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"any `Send + Sync` value under an explicit key","locale":"en"},"6921":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_arc_as(key, arc)`","locale":"en"},"6922":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"the same, from an `Arc`","locale":"en"},"6923":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_checked(key, arc, check)`","locale":"en"},"6924":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"a value whose availability also depends on a predicate `check`, evaluated per consumer with the consumer's interception metadata. The predicate runs under the runtime lock and must not call into the runtime.","locale":"en"},"6925":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_serialized_as(key, value)`","locale":"en"},"6926":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"a `Serialize` value that also has a **JSON view**, readable with `ctx.view(key)`, by loader expressions and by guest plugins. A `serde_json::Value` provided under a key (`provide_as`, `provide_arc_as`, `provide_checked`) is its own JSON view.","locale":"en"},"6927":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"What providing does:","locale":"en"},"6928":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**One binding per key and realm.** A second provider in the same realm fails with `KardiaError::AlreadyProvided`, whose message is `service \"database\" has been registered at <db>` (the name of the providing plugin).","locale":"en"},"6929":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**Notification follows the provider's state.** Consumers are notified at once only if the providing fiber is `Active`; otherwise they are notified when it becomes `Active`. When the provider leaves `Active`, its consumers are notified before any of its inverses run.","locale":"en"},"6930":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**Withdrawal waits for consumers.** Reverting the provision removes the binding and notifies the realm, then waits until every consumer that committed to this binding has finished its own cleanup, and only then removes the provision.","locale":"en"},"6931":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**A retired provider frees its realm at once.** Disposing a provider unbinds its live provisions immediately, so a successor can provide in the same realm while the old consumers still drain (they keep reading the old binding through their committed views).","locale":"en"},"6932":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**A stale load cannot provide.** A retired fiber whose load is still in flight may still register inverses (so nothing it acquired leaks), but its `provide` calls fail with `KardiaError::InactiveEffect`.","locale":"en"},"6933":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**Removal is postponed during a drain.** While a provider is unloading, its withdrawn provisions stay reachable to its descendants until the drain ends, so they can use inherited services during their own cleanup.","locale":"en"},"6934":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`.provides([..])` on a `PluginDef` (or `provide = [..]` in `#[plugin]`, or `Plugin::provide()`) only **declares** what a plugin provides. The declaration is metadata for tooling and for the dependency-cycle check; a plugin can provide undeclared keys, which simply escape the check.","locale":"en"},"6935":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"There is no in-place overwrite of a bound value. To change what consumers see, provide a new value (withdraw and re-provide, restart or update the provider), so that the change is observed.","locale":"en"},"6936":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"A plugin lists the services it needs in its **inject** declaration, an `Inject`: ordered keys, each with optional interception metadata.","locale":"en"},"6937":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"Where the declaration goes:","locale":"en"},"6938":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"Plugin form","locale":"en"},"6939":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"Declaration","locale":"en"},"6940":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`impl Plugin for P`","locale":"en"},"6941":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`fn inject() -> Inject`","locale":"en"},"6942":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`#[plugin]` function","locale":"en"},"6943":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"the type of its context parameter, `Injected<(A, B)>`","locale":"en"},"6944":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`PluginDef::new` / `PluginDef::typed`","locale":"en"},"6945":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`.inject(..)`","locale":"en"},"6946":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"a closure plugin","locale":"en"},"6947":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`ctx.inject(deps, \\|ctx\\| async move { … })`","locale":"en"},"6948":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"a loader entry","locale":"en"},"6949":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"its `inject` field (see Configuration)","locale":"en"},"6950":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"The runtime keeps the fiber in step with its declaration:","locale":"en"},"6951":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"It stays `Pending` until every declared service is available, then loads.","locale":"en"},"6952":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"If a declared service is replaced by another binding, it unloads and loads again against the new one.","locale":"en"},"6953":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"If a declared service goes away, it unloads and waits in `Pending`.","locale":"en"},"6954":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"**Dependency cycles.** When a fiber is inserted, the runtime checks whether the declared `provide` and `inject` sets of the live fibers in its realm form a cycle through it. If they do, it logs a warning naming the cycle (`dependency cycle: a -> b -> a`) and the fiber stays `Pending`, instead of waiting silently.","locale":"en"},"6955":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6956":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Returns","locale":"en"},"6957":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Access","locale":"en"},"6958":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.get::<S>()`","locale":"en"},"6959":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Result<Svc<S>, AccessError>`","locale":"en"},"6960":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"checked, through committed views","locale":"en"},"6961":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.get_as::<T>(key)`","locale":"en"},"6962":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Result<Svc<T>, AccessError>`","locale":"en"},"6963":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"checked, by key, for any type","locale":"en"},"6964":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.view(key)`","locale":"en"},"6965":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Result<Value, AccessError>`","locale":"en"},"6966":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"checked, the service's JSON view","locale":"en"},"6967":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.deps::<(A, B)>()`","locale":"en"},"6968":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Result<(Svc<A>, Svc<B>), AccessError>`","locale":"en"},"6969":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"checked, a tuple of up to eight services","locale":"en"},"6970":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.live::<S>()`","locale":"en"},"6971":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Option<Svc<S>>`","locale":"en"},"6972":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"reflective: the live binding of the realm, if its provider is active; never fails for undeclared keys","locale":"en"},"6973":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.live_as::<T>(key)`","locale":"en"},"6974":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Option<Svc<T>>`","locale":"en"},"6975":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"the same, by key","locale":"en"},"6976":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"**Checked access** (the paper's Algorithm 6) resolves a key like this:","locale":"en"},"6977":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"A binding that a fiber on the way provides itself, in the same realm, is returned directly.","locale":"en"},"6978":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Otherwise the walk goes up through the fibers that derived the context.","locale":"en"},"6979":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"It stops at a context that isolates the key again (an isolation boundary): the key is undeclared.","locale":"en"},"6980":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"The first fiber that declares the key decides. It returns the binding that fiber **committed** to when it loaded; a fiber that declares the key but has no committed binding yields `Inactive`.","locale":"en"},"6981":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-93","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"The root context, which cannot declare `inject`, has **unchecked** access to the live store, as in Cordis.","locale":"en"},"6982":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-94","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Because checked access reads the committed view rather than the live store, a dependency stays readable while the consumer runs its own teardown, even if the provider is already gone from the store (Theorem 70 of the paper).","locale":"en"},"6983":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-95","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"The errors:","locale":"en"},"6984":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-96","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`AccessError`","locale":"en"},"6985":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-97","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Message","locale":"en"},"6986":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-98","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Undeclared { key }`","locale":"en"},"6987":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-99","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`cannot get property \"key\" without inject`","locale":"en"},"6988":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Inactive { key }`","locale":"en"},"6989":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`cannot get required service \"key\" in inactive context`","locale":"en"},"6990":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`TypeMismatch { key, expected }`","locale":"en"},"6991":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`service \"key\" is not of type …`","locale":"en"},"6992":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-104","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`Injected<D>` wraps a plugin context whose typed accesses are checked against its declared dependencies `D` at compile time. The `#[plugin]` macro reads `D` from the signature and generates both the declaration and the wrapper:","locale":"en"},"6993":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`Injected::get::<S, _>()`: the `_` is the inferred position of `S` in `D` (`kardia_core::index::I0` … `I7`); you never write it.","locale":"en"},"6994":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`Injected::deps()` returns all of `D` as a tuple of `Svc`s.","locale":"en"},"6995":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`Injected::context()` returns the underlying, unchecked `Context`, and `Injected<D>` dereferences to it, so every other `Context` method is available.","locale":"en"},"6996":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`#[plugin(name = \"…\", provide = [\"key\"], crate = path)]` takes an `async fn` whose first parameter is `Context` or `Injected<(..)>` and whose optional second parameter is `Arc<Config>`. It generates a plugin type named after the function in camel case (`greeter` → `Greeter`), with the hyphenated function name as plugin name unless `name` is given. Writing plugins is covered in Plugins.","locale":"en"},"6997":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Every access returns a `Svc<T>`: the service value together with the **caller**, the context that accessed it. Cordis attributes calls with a JavaScript `Proxy`; kardia makes the caller an explicit part of the handle.","locale":"en"},"6998":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6999":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Returns","locale":"en"},"7000":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`*svc` (`Deref`)","locale":"en"},"7001":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the service value","locale":"en"},"7002":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.caller()`","locale":"en"},"7003":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the accessing `Context`","locale":"en"},"7004":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.key()`","locale":"en"},"7005":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the key it was reached under","locale":"en"},"7006":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.impl_id()`","locale":"en"},"7007":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the identity of the binding (never reused, so a replacement by an equal value is observable)","locale":"en"},"7008":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.arc()`","locale":"en"},"7009":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the `Arc<T>`","locale":"en"},"7010":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.provider()`","locale":"en"},"7011":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the providing fiber (the service's definition site)","locale":"en"},"7012":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.logger()`","locale":"en"},"7013":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"a logger for work done on the caller's behalf: named by the caller's `logger` interception `name`, else after the providing plugin","locale":"en"},"7014":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.intercepts()`","locale":"en"},"7015":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the interception metadata of this access, outermost first","locale":"en"},"7016":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.meta()`","locale":"en"},"7017":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"that metadata merged with `S::merge_intercept`","locale":"en"},"7018":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"**Effects on the caller's behalf.** A service method that creates an effect for its caller registers it on `svc.caller()`. The effect then belongs to the caller's fiber and is reverted when the *caller* unloads, which is what Cordis's tracker achieves with `this.ctx`. Service crates expose such methods as **extension traits on `Svc<S>`**, which coherence allows because the trait is local. The timer service does this (simplified: the real `timeout` also reverts its effect once it has fired):","locale":"en"},"7019":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"So `timer.interval(..)` in `greeter` above stops when `greeter` unloads, not when the timer plugin does.","locale":"en"},"7020":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"**A service's own dependencies.** A service resolves its own dependencies through the `Context` it stored when it was constructed (its definition site), so no shadow contexts are needed. Two consequences differ from Cordis, where both follow the use site:","locale":"en"},"7021":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Interception metadata of the outer caller does not reach the services a service calls in turn; it stays on `Svc::caller()`.","locale":"en"},"7022":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Effects a service creates through its stored context belong to the service's fiber.","locale":"en"},"7023":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"Interception attaches metadata to a key along a context chain, so that a service can behave differently per caller (paper Def. 26–27). The usual example is the logger: `logger: { name: db, level: 3 }` renames and re-levels the logger of everything below.","locale":"en"},"7024":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"Where metadata comes from, outermost first:","locale":"en"},"7025":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"the metadata declared with the `inject` that admits the access (`Inject::with_meta`, or an entry's `inject: { key: meta }`);","locale":"en"},"7026":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"every `ctx.intercept(key, meta)` on the caller's derivation chain, outer to inner (a loader entry's `intercept` field adds one).","locale":"en"},"7027":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"`Svc::intercepts()` returns this list and `Svc::meta()` merges it with `S::merge_intercept`, by default `merge_shallow`: objects merged key by key, later values winning, like `Object.assign`. Override `merge_intercept` in your `Service` impl for another merge. On a context, `ctx.intercepts(key)` returns the chain's metadata and `ctx.intercept_meta::<T>(key)` merges and deserializes it (malformed metadata yields `T::default()`).","locale":"en"},"7028":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"Metadata also reaches availability predicates: `provide_checked` hands the predicate the consumer's metadata. The loader uses this for `inject: { loader: { await: true } }`, which makes `loader` available to an entry only once every entry has settled.","locale":"en"},"7029":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"Each key lives in a **realm**. By default all contexts share the key's root realm; isolating a key gives a context, and everything derived from it, a realm of its own:","locale":"en"},"7030":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"7031":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"Derives a context in which","locale":"en"},"7032":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`ctx.isolate(key)`","locale":"en"},"7033":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`key` lives in a fresh, private realm","locale":"en"},"7034":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`ctx.isolate_in(key, realm)`","locale":"en"},"7035":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`key` lives in a given realm (`RealmId::new()`), shared by every context isolated into it","locale":"en"},"7036":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`ctx.extend()`","locale":"en"},"7037":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"the context has its own mutable isolation and interception tables (an `Overlay`)","locale":"en"},"7038":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`ctx.extend_with(&overlay)`","locale":"en"},"7039":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"the context is backed by an existing `Overlay`, shared with other contexts","locale":"en"},"7040":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"A provider binds in the realm its context resolves the key to, and a consumer sees only the binding of its own realm. Checked access stops at a context that isolates the key again, so an isolated subtree cannot reach the outer binding through an outer declaration. Related queries: `ctx.realm(key)`, `ctx.has_isolation(key)`, `ctx.isolated_keys()`; and for tooling, `ctx.bindings(key)` and `ctx.binding_provider(key, realm)`.","locale":"en"},"7041":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"In configuration files, isolation is the entry field `isolate` (`{ db: true }` for a private realm, `{ db: shared }` for a realm shared under a label); see The loader.","locale":"en"},"7042":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"An event is a Rust type that implements `Event`. Listeners are registered per event type.","locale":"en"},"7043":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Output` is what each listener returns. `Bailable` decides whether a result stops a `bail` or `serial` dispatch, and whether it is a failure in `parallel`:","locale":"en"},"7044":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-156","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Output`","locale":"en"},"7045":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-157","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"Bails when","locale":"en"},"7046":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-158","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"Failure in `parallel`","locale":"en"},"7047":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-159","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`()`","locale":"en"},"7048":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-160","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"never","locale":"en"},"7049":{"id":