nt":"Section","locale":"en"},"7260":{"id":"/en/docs-25","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"**Theory**","locale":"en"},"7261":{"id":"/en/docs-26","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"What the paper defines, proves and prescribes","locale":"en"},"7262":{"id":"/en/docs-27","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"Concepts","locale":"en"},"7263":{"id":"/en/docs-28","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"**Implementation**","locale":"en"},"7264":{"id":"/en/docs-29","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"What the TypeScript code of Cordis actually does (Cordis v4, `cordis@4.0.0-rc.12`)","locale":"en"},"7265":{"id":"/en/docs-30","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"Cordis reference","locale":"en"},"7266":{"id":"/en/docs-31","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"**Proposal**","locale":"en"},"7267":{"id":"/en/docs-32","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"How kardia rebuilds it in Rust","locale":"en"},"7268":{"id":"/en/docs-33","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"Development","locale":"en"},"7269":{"id":"/en/docs-34","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs#how-this-documentation-is-organised","content":"Where the paper and the code differ, the difference is recorded in Paper vs. code. The Rust design says which side it follows at each such point, and Implementation status lists where kardia differs from the TypeScript impleme