ocs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#run-the-example","content":"Without an argument, the binary reads `kardia.yml` from the working directory. See Installation for the requirements.","locale":"en"},"7370":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-9","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#the-example-app","content":"`examples/kardia.yml` is a list of entries, one plugin each:","locale":"en"},"7371":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-10","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#the-example-app","content":"`timer` is the built-in timer service.","locale":"en"},"7372":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-11","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#the-example-app","content":"`hmr` reloads the guest modules below `plugins/` when their files change.","locale":"en"},"7373":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-12","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#the-example-app","content":"`plugins` is a group of two entries: the console logger, disabled for now, and `hello`, a WebAssembly guest plugin written by hand in WebAssembly text (`examples/plugins/hello.wat`).","locale":"en"},"7374":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-13","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#the-example-app","content":"The configuration file explains every field.","locale":"en"},"7375":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-14","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#things-to-try-while-it-runs","content":"**Change the config.** In `examples/kardia.yml`, set `disabled: false` on the `console` entry: the console logger starts. Set it back to `true` and it stops.","locale":"en"},"7376":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-15","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#things-to-try-while-it-runs","content":"**Hot-reload a plugin.** Edit the greeting in `examples/plugins/hello.wat`. The `hmr` entry reloads the WebAssembly plugin in place: the old instance logs its goodbye, then the new one logs your greeting.","locale":"en"},"7377":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-16","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#things-to-try-while-it-runs","content":"**Stop the app.** Press Ctrl-C. Shutting down does not write to the config file.","locale":"en"},"7378":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-17","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"The configuration file\" href=\"/docs/guide-configuration\" description=\"Entries, expressions, two-way sync and the built-in plugins.\" />","locale":"en"},"7379":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-18","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Writing plugins\" href=\"/docs/guide-plugins\" description=\"Services and plugins in Rust, and loading them from a config file.\" />","locale":"en"},"7380":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-19","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Hot reload\" href=\"/docs/guide-hot-reload\" description=\"Reloading guest modules as their files change.\" />","locale":"en"},"7381":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-20","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Guest plugins\" href=\"/docs/guide-guests\" description=\"WebAssembly, dynamic-library and process guests.\" />","locale":"en"},"7382":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"page","content":"Auxiliary packages","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","locale":"en"},"7383":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","content":"timer, logger-console, fs-node, package-manager, loader-utils and create: how ordinary Cordis services are built on the core primitives.","locale":"en"},"7384":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`@cordisjs/plugin-timer`","locale":"en"},"7385":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"`@cordisjs/plugin-logger-console`","locale":"en"},"7386":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"`@cordisjs/plugin-fs-node`","locale":"en"},"7387":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"`@cordisjs/plugin-package-manager`","locale":"en"},"7388":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#loader-utils","content":"`@cordisjs/loader-utils`","locale":"en"},"7389":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"`create-cordis`","locale":"en"},"7390":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#port","content":"Takeaways for a port","locale":"en"},"7391":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","content":"These packages are not described in the paper; they show how ordinary services are built on the core primitives.","locale":"en"},"7392":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","content":"**Common theme:** every resource is registered through `ctx.effect` on the *calling* fiber (found via the service tracker, see Services and traceability), so it is released when the caller unloads. There is no per-consumer bookkeeping in the service.","locale":"en"},"7393":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`timer/src/index.ts`. Service `timer`, mixed into the context as `ctx.timeout / interval / throttle / debounce / setTimeout / setInterval`.","locale":"en"},"7394":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"API","locale":"en"},"7395":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"Semantics","locale":"en"},"7396":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`timeout(cb, ms) → dispose`","locale":"en"},"7397":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"effect around `setTimeout`; when it fires it first disposes itself (removes the effect from the fiber), then calls `cb`","locale":"en"},"7398":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`timeout(ms) → Promise<void>`","locale":"en"},"7399":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"sleep; disposing the fiber rejects it with `Error('Context has been disposed')`; the effect is removed when the promise settles","locale":"en"},"7400":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`interval(cb, ms) → dispose`","locale":"en"},"7401":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"effect around `setInterval`","locale":"en"},"7402":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`interval(ms) → AsyncIterableIterator`","locale":"en"},"7403":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"each tick resolves only the oldest pending `next()`; ticks without a waiter are dropped; `return()`/`throw()` semantics of async iterators; fiber disposal rejects pending reads","locale":"en"},"7404":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`throttle(cb, ms, noTrailing?)`","locale":"en"},"7405":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"leading call, trailing call with latest args unless `noTrailing`; `.dispose()`","locale":"en"},"7406":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`debounce(cb, ms)`","locale":"en"},"7407":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"each call restarts the timer; `.dispose()`","locale":"en"},"7408":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"`shared.ts`, `index.ts`, `browser.ts`. A class plugin (`name = 'logger-console'`) whose constructor calls `ctx.logger.exporter(this)`, so the exporter lives exactly as long as the plugin (see Logger).","locale":"en"},"7409":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"Config: `colors` (Node default from `supports-color`), `maxLength`, per-name `levels`, `showDiff`, a `showTime` template, `label { width, margin, align }`.","locale":"en"},"7410":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"It renders a `[E]/[W]/[I]/[D]` prefix, a hashed-colour label, aligned continuation lines and an optional `+Nms` diff; `%o` uses `util.inspect`.","locale":"en"},"7411":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"The browser build delegates to `console.*`.","locale":"en"},"7412":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"`index.ts`, `watcher.ts`. Service `fs`, currently only `watch(path, { filter }) → Watcher`.","locale":"en"},"7413":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"Paths resolve relative to the **caller's** `ctx.baseUrl`; `file:` URLs are accepted; Windows drive-relative forms are rejected.","locale":"en"},"7414":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"A single file is watched **through its parent directory** (`depth: 0`), so atomic rename-based writes do not lose the watch.","locale":"en"},"7415":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"The `Watcher` is an async effect wrapping chokidar (`ignoreInitial`), registered after the initial scan. Only `change` events are forwarded; `ready` replays asynchronously to late listeners; dispatch uses a snapshot; listener errors go to `error` listeners (whose own errors are only logged).","locale":"en"},"7416":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"The filter consists of gitignore-like rules: **last match wins**, tested against the entry *or any ancestor*. A directory is still traversed if a later including rule's literal base is related; patterns leaving the root are rejected.","locale":"en"},"7417":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"`index.ts`, `agent.ts`, `manifest.ts`, `backup.ts`, `process.ts`, `state.ts`. Service `packageManager`: transactional dependency installs driving npm / pnpm / yarn classic / yarn berry (hoisted `node_modules` only).","locale":"en"},"7418":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"`install(changes, { signal })` is serialized:","locale":"en"},"7419":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Detect the agent from `package.json#packageManager` (exact version, verified by `--version`), require a lockfile, and check the layout.","locale":"en"},"7420":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Snapshot the install state and back up the manifest, lockfiles and rc files (mode- and symlink-preserving).","locale":"en"},"7421":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Edit `package.json` (preserving indentation, EOL and sort order).","locale":"en"},"7422":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Run the agent with an **inactivity timeout** and abort support.","locale":"en"},"7423":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Diff the install state (`added/removed/updated`, with real paths).","locale":"en"},"7424":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"On failure: restore the files and run a **non-cancellable recovery install**; if that fails too, throw an `AggregateError`.","locale":"en"},"7425":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Processes are spawned in their own process group (POSIX) and the whole tree is killed (SIGTERM → SIGKILL; `taskkill /T` on Windows). The environment is scrubbed of variables leaked by an outer `yarn run`.","locale":"en"},"7426":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Real paths use Node's JS `realpath` algorithm so that they match module URLs (intended to feed hmr roots; not wired up in the repository).","locale":"en"},"7427":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#loader-utils","content":"`index.ts`, `internal.ts`. `unwrapExports` (ESM/esbuild interop) and `ModuleLoader.fromInternal()`, which gives access to Node's internal cascaded ESM loader (its shape is detected by API presence across Node 22–24.12+). Pure Node glue; **no Rust counterpart**.","locale":"en"},"7428":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"`create/src/index.ts`, `bin.ts`. A standalone scaffolding CLI (it does not use core):","locale":"en"},"7429":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"prompt for a name and prepare the directory;","locale":"en"},"7430":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"fetch the template package (`@cordisjs/boilerplate`) tarball from the configured npm registry and extract it with `strip: 1`;","locale":"en"},"7431":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"optionally stage a pinned Yarn binary (five documented rules);","locale":"en"},"7432":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"rewrite `package.json`, optionally `git init`, install and start.","locale":"en"},"7433":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"Errors print a fixed message and `process.exit(1)` (the tests run it as a child process). The `--mirror` flag is parsed but unused.","locale":"en"},"7434":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#port","content":"timer, fs and the logger exporters are thin wrappers proving that **\"lifetime by effect\" + caller attribution** is enough to make arbitrary resources revertible: exactly the paper's §6.1 acquisition-inside-the-boundary pattern (see Discussion and related work).","locale":"en"},"7435":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#port","content":"package-manager and create are Node-ecosystem tools; for a Rust framework they are optional or must be retargeted (e.g. Cargo / WASM component packages).","locale":"en"},"7436":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"page","content":"Context and reflection","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context","locale":"en"},"7437":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context","content":"How Cordis core represents contexts, stores service bindings per realm, notifies dependents and resolves coeffects through a Proxy.","locale":"en"},"7438":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#context","content":"`Context`: the first-class context","locale":"en"},"7439":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"Construction","locale":"en"},"7440":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"Derivation with `extend()`","locale":"en"},"7441":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#realm-symbols","content":"Realm symbols","locale":"en"},"7442":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`ReflectService`","locale":"en"},"7443":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#impl","content":"`Impl`: a binding","locale":"en"},"7444":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"`provide(name, value?, check?)`: coeffect provision","locale":"en"},"7445":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#set","content":"`set(name, value)`","locale":"en"},"7446":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#get","content":"`get(name, strict = true)` and `_getImpl`","locale":"en"},"7447":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#notify","content":"`notify(names, filter?)`: reactive notification","locale":"en"},"7448":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`accessor` and `mixin`","locale":"en"},"7449":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"Property access through the Proxy","locale":"en"},"7450":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"`locate(ctx, name)`: the committed-view walk","locale":"en"},"7451":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"Interception","locale":"en"},"7452":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"Design observations","locale":"en"},"7453":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/context.ts`, `reflect.ts` and `utils.ts`. The paper counterparts are §3.2 (coeffects, see Reactive coeffects), §5.1.2 (Algorithms 2–3) and §5.1.4 (Algorithm 6), both in Implementation.","locale":"en"},"7454":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#context","content":"`context.ts` declares:","locale":"en"},"7455":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"`new Context()` builds the **root** (`context.ts:36-49`):","locale":"en"},"7456":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It creates empty `isolate`/`intercept` tables (`Object.create(null)`).","locale":"en"},"7457":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It wraps itself in a `Proxy` with `ReflectService.handler`. This proxy *is* the context everybody sees; `this[symbols.root] = self`.","locale":"en"},"7458":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It creates the **root fiber** `new Fiber(self, {}, {}, null, …)` (runtime `null` ⇒ root, uid 0, `ACTIVE`).","locale":"en"},"7459":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It instantiates the four built-in services on the root: `reflect`, `registry`, `events`, `logger`.","locale":"en"},"7460":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It calls `this.fiber._disposables.clear()`. The built-in mixins and accessors registered during construction are *not* part of the root fiber's revertible effects: they must survive `root.fiber.dispose()`.","locale":"en"},"7461":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"`context.ts:55-63`:","locale":"en"},"7462":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"Every derived context is a **prototype-chain child** of its parent. This realizes the paper's *derived realization* (Definition 23): the child overrides some slots and inherits everything else. Nothing needs to be undone; dropping the child object discards the adjustment.","locale":"en"},"7463":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"`isolate(name, label?)` (`context.ts:65`) creates `Object.create(this[symbols.isolate])`, sets `shadow[name] = label ?? Symbol(name)` and extends with it. A fresh symbol gives a private realm; a shared `label` gives a shared realm.","locale":"en"},"7464":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"`intercept(name, config)` (`context.ts:73`) follows the same pattern for the intercept table.","locale":"en"},"7465":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"A fiber's context is `parent.extend({ fiber: this })` (`fiber.ts:150`).","locale":"en"},"7466":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"**Key property:** the isolation and interception tables are *prototype chains*. A lookup (`table[name]`) sees the nearest override; `Object.hasOwn(table, name)` detects an isolation boundary introduced at exactly that level (used by `locate`).","locale":"en"},"7467":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#realm-symbols","content":"`ReflectService.provide` lazily assigns a root realm: `ctx[symbols.root][symbols.isolate][name] ??= Symbol(name)` (`reflect.ts:222`). Thus *every* service name has a realm symbol in the root table once it has been provided; isolated contexts override it. The **store is keyed by realm symbol**, which gives the two-layer `k → ρ(k) → σ(ρ(k))` resolution of Definition 24.","locale":"en"},"7468":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`reflect.ts` holds the shared, root-level tables:","locale":"en"},"7469":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"7470":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"Paper","locale":"en"},"7471":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"7472":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`store: Dict<Impl, symbol>`","locale":"en"},"7473":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"σ (`@@store`)","locale":"en"},"7474":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"realm symbol → current `Impl` (binding)","locale":"en"},"7475":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`props: Dict<Property>`","locale":"en"},"7476":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"–","locale":"en"},"7477":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"declared context properties: `{type:'service'}` or `{type:'accessor', get, set}`","locale":"en"},"7478":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`_implCounter`","locale":"en"},"7479":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"fresh names","locale":"en"},"7480":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"uid source for `Impl`s (never reused)","locale":"en"},"7481":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#impl","content":"`reflect.ts:65-75`:","locale":"en"},"7482":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"`reflect.ts:213-249`. `provide` is a `fiber.effect` (therefore tracked and revertible) whose callback:","locale":"en"},"7483":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"registers or validates `props[name]` as a service (an error if it is already an accessor);","locale":"en"},"7484":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"ensures a root realm symbol and computes `key = ctx[isolate][name]`;","locale":"en"},"7485":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"performs the **single-source check**: it throws `service \"x\" has been registered at <fiber>` if `store[key]` exists (O-Insert's disjointness, per realm);","locale":"en"},"7486":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"sets `store[key] = impl` and `fiber.provisions.add(impl)`;","locale":"en"},"7487":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"if the providing fiber is already `ACTIVE`, calls `notify([name])` immediately; otherwise notification happens when the fiber becomes `ACTIVE` (`Fiber._updateState`), matching \"only Active fibers provide\".","locale":"en"},"7488":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"Its **inverse** is async:","locale":"en"},"7489":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"delete the store entry (if it still holds this impl) and `notify` dependents in the impl's realm;","locale":"en"},"7490":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"the **provider-side guard**: `await` until `impl.dependents` is empty (`impl.release` is resolved by the last dependent's unload). It always yields at least once, so child cleanup can still access the inherited service;","locale":"en"},"7491":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"remove the impl from `fiber.provisions`.","locale":"en"},"7492":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-55","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#set","content":"`reflect.ts:200-211`. An in-place overwrite of the *own* binding (`impl.value = value`); an error if the name is not provided or is provided by another fiber. There is **no notification**: as the paper notes, an in-place overwrite is not observed by dependents.","locale":"en"},"7493":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-56","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#get","content":"`reflect.ts:188-198`. Resolves `ctx[isolate][name]` → `store[key]`. In `strict` mode it returns nothing unless `impl.ctx.fiber.state === ACTIVE` (**provider availability = Active**). It never throws.","locale":"en"},"7494":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-57","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#notify","content":"`reflect.ts:251-270`:","locale":"en"},"7495":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-58","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#notify","content":"This is Algorithm 3. The *filter* parameter exists so that the loader can replace the realm test during realm reassignment (Algorithm 7, see Managed realms).","locale":"en"},"7496":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-59","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`accessor(name, {get, set})` and `mixin(source, keys)` live at `reflect.ts:272-308`.","locale":"en"},"7497":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-60","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`accessor` declares a computed context property (as a revertible effect).","locale":"en"},"7498":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-61","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`mixin('events', ['on', 'emit', …])` exposes members of a service as context properties (`ctx.on` → `ctx.events.on`) bound to the accessing context. It is a generator effect that yields one accessor per key.","locale":"en"},"7499":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"The root wires (`reflect.ts:182-185`):","locale":"en"},"7500":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-63","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"Source","locale":"en"},"7501":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-64","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"Keys mixed into the context","locale":"en"},"7502":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-65","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`reflect`","locale":"en"},"7503":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-66","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`get`, `set`, `provide`, `accessor`, `mixin`","locale":"en"},"7504":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-67","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`fiber`","locale":"en"},"7505":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-68","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`runtime`, `effect`","locale":"en"},"7506":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-69","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`registry`","locale":"en"},"7507":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-70","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`inject`, `plugin`","locale":"en"},"7508":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-71","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`events`","locale":"en"},"7509":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-72","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`on`, `once`, `parallel`, `emit`, `serial`, `bail`, `waterfall`","locale":"en"},"7510":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-73","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"`ReflectService.handler` (`reflect.ts:105-170`) mediates `ctx.foo` in its `get` trap:","locale":"en"},"7511":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-74","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"*special* properties (symbols, `prototype`, `then`, numeric strings, names starting with `_`) bypass mediation;","locale":"en"},"7512":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-75","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"ordinary own or inherited properties are returned through `getTraceable` (see Services and traceability);","locale":"en"},"7513":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-76","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"a declared **accessor** → its getter;","locale":"en"},"7514":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-77","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"if the *def site* (the shadow, see Services and traceability) is the **root fiber** → unchecked `reflect.get(prop, false)` (root code cannot declare `inject`);","locale":"en"},"7515":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-78","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"otherwise a `waterfall('internal/get', …)` (which lets plugins hook access) around `locate(defSite, prop)`:","locale":"en"},"7516":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-79","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"impl found → its value (traced);","locale":"en"},"7517":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-80","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"the fiber declares the key but has no committed impl → `cannot get required service \"x\" in inactive context`;","locale":"en"},"7518":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-81","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"nobody declares it → `cannot get property \"x\" without inject`.","locale":"en"},"7519":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-82","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"The `set` trap: an undeclared property on a non-root fiber → the error `cannot set property without provide`; an accessor → its setter; a service → `waterfall('internal/set')` → `reflect.set`.","locale":"en"},"7520":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-83","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"Errors are created as cheap placeholders and only materialized with a trimmed stack when thrown (`createAccessError`/`enhanceAccessError`).","locale":"en"},"7521":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-84","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"`reflect.ts:83-102` implements Algorithm 6, extended with own provisions and isolation boundaries:","locale":"en"},"7522":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-85","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"Consequences, all covered by `tests/isolate.spec.ts` and `reflect.spec.ts`:","locale":"en"},"7523":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-86","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"a consumer reads the **committed** impl, not the live store, so it keeps seeing its dependency during its own teardown (Theorem 70);","locale":"en"},"7524":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-87","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"a child plugin *inherits* the injection of an ancestor (`inject` declared on an ancestor admits access in descendants);","locale":"en"},"7525":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-88","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"an isolation boundary stops inheritance (`does not inherit the injected view across isolation boundaries`).","locale":"en"},"7526":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-89","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"`Service[symbols.resolveIntercept]` (`service.ts:57-70`) resolves the metadata for a service named `name` at access time:","locale":"en"},"7527":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-90","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"walk the context's intercept prototype chain, collecting own values **outer → inner**;","locale":"en"},"7528":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-91","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"prepend the *component-declared* metadata `locate(caller, name).fiber.inject[name]` (the value given in `inject: { name: meta }` of the declaring fiber) at the lowest priority. There is none for own provisions, and the walk stops at an isolation boundary;","locale":"en"},"7529":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-92","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"merge with `service[symbols.mergeIntercept]` (default `Object.assign({}, ...values)`, so right-biased).","locale":"en"},"7530":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-93","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"This is exactly `σ(k)(d(k) ⊕ ι(k))` from Definition 27, with ⊕ = shallow object merge (customizable per service). The `logger` service uses it for `{ name, level }` (`logger.ts:213-224`).","locale":"en"},"7531":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-94","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"**Everything is in the root.** There is one `store`, one `props` and one `registry` per root; derived contexts differ only by their prototype-chained `isolate`/`intercept` tables and their `fiber`. This keeps \"is key k provided in realm r?\" a single map lookup.","locale":"en"},"7532":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-95","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"**Provider identity** is the `Impl.uid`, a fresh counter value. This implements the \"name, not value\" discipline of the committed and target views.","locale":"en"},"7533":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-96","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"**Isolation per realm symbol** implements the relaxed calculus \"disjoint within a realm\" (§4.4, see Metatheory).","locale":"en"},"7534":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-97","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"**No compile-time checking**: declared vs. accessed keys are checked only at runtime, by the proxy (paper §5.1.4 notes this could be static).","locale":"en"},"7535":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"page","content":"Effects","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects","locale":"en"},"7536":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects","content":"How Cordis core tracks revertible effects: accepted shapes, the execution engine, fiber.effect, ownership transfer and teardown order.","locale":"en"},"7537":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"Accepted effect shapes","locale":"en"},"7538":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"The engine `_execute(runner)`","locale":"en"},"7539":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`fiber.effect(execute, label)`: the tracked effect","locale":"en"},"7540":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#ownership","content":"Nesting and ownership transfer","locale":"en"},"7541":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`DisposableList`","locale":"en"},"7542":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#accumulator","content":"Fiber-level accumulator vs. the paper","locale":"en"},"7543":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"Error handling summary","locale":"en"},"7544":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"Tests documenting the semantics","locale":"en"},"7545":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/fiber.ts:60-363` and `utils.ts`. The paper counterpart is §3.1 and Algorithm 1; see Revertible effects.","locale":"en"},"7546":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"`fiber.ts:64-76`:","locale":"en"},"7547":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"An effect callback may therefore return:","locale":"en"},"7548":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"Callback returns","locale":"en"},"7549":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"Paper reading","locale":"en"},"7550":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"a function","locale":"en"},"7551":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"an effect function 𝔈Γ (the returned function is the inverse)","locale":"en"},"7552":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"`undefined`/`null`","locale":"en"},"7553":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"identity effect (nothing to undo)","locale":"en"},"7554":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"a `Promise<function>`","locale":"en"},"7555":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"async effect function","locale":"en"},"7556":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"a sync generator yielding disposers","locale":"en"},"7557":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"effect iterator ℑΓ, run to completion synchronously","locale":"en"},"7558":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"an async generator yielding disposers","locale":"en"},"7559":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"effect iterator with **iteration boundaries** that check a guard","locale":"en"},"7560":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"Anything else throws `TypeError('Invalid effect')`.","locale":"en"},"7561":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`fiber.ts:240-290`. `EffectRunner { epoch, execute, collect, getOuterStack }` abstracts the two users of the engine, a single `ctx.effect` call and a fiber's whole `apply`:","locale":"en"},"7562":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`execute()` produces the effect value;","locale":"en"},"7563":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`collect(dispose)` records a yielded inverse;","locale":"en"},"7564":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`epoch` is the **guard**. For async iterators the loop runs `while (runner.epoch === oldEpoch)`; when the epoch changes, the loop stops after the current iteration lands and `iter.return()` is called so the generator's `finally` blocks run (`fiber.ts:269-285`).","locale":"en"},"7565":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"**Sync iterators are not interruptible** (there is no guard check); they could not be interrupted anyway in a single-threaded host. Every `collect` is type-checked (`safeCollect`).","locale":"en"},"7566":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`composeError(…, getOuterStack)` stitches the error stack together with the stack captured where the effect or plugin was *created* (`buildOuterStack`). This produces long stack traces that point at the user's `ctx.plugin(...)`/`ctx.effect(...)` call site. It is pure DX and JS-specific.","locale":"en"},"7567":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`fiber.ts:292-357`. `ctx.effect` is `ctx.fiber.effect` (mixed in by `ReflectService`). Step by step:","locale":"en"},"7568":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`assertActive()`: a fiber whose `uid` is `null` (removed) cannot create effects (`CordisError('INACTIVE_EFFECT')`).","locale":"en"},"7569":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"A local list `disposables` and a local `dispose()` that runs them **in reverse order**. If one returns a promise, the remaining ones are chained after it (sequential LIFO, `fiber.ts:298-311`).","locale":"en"},"7570":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`EffectMeta { label, children }` for introspection (`fiber.getEffects()`, used by tooling).","locale":"en"},"7571":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"A runner whose `epoch` is a boolean (`armed` in Algorithm 1) and whose `collect`:","locale":"en"},"7572":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"pushes the disposer into the local list,","locale":"en"},"7573":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"**removes it from the fiber's top-level list** (`this._disposables.delete(dispose)`), an ownership transfer (see below),","locale":"en"},"7574":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"records child metadata.","locale":"en"},"7575":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"Execute. On a synchronous throw, dispose what was collected and rethrow.","locale":"en"},"7576":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"Async failures: `task.catch(dispose)`. A failing async effect rolls back what it collected, and errors are logged rather than left unhandled.","locale":"en"},"7577":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"Build the returned **wrapper** (the disposer):","locale":"en"},"7578":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"at-most-once (`epoch` flips to `false`), Theorem 7's soundness invariant;","locale":"en"},"7579":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"flipping `epoch` also stops an in-flight async iterator at its next boundary;","locale":"en"},"7580":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"if setup is still running, disposal waits for it first (`task.then(dispose)`).","locale":"en"},"7581":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`wrapper.then(...)` makes the disposer **awaitable**: `await ctx.effect(...)` waits for setup to finish and resolves to a disposer.","locale":"en"},"7582":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`disposables.push(this._disposables.push(wrapper))`: the wrapper is registered in the **fiber's** list, and the function that removes it from that list is the first local disposable (so disposing an effect manually also unregisters it from the fiber).","locale":"en"},"7583":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#ownership","content":"Calling `ctx.effect` inside another effect's callback first registers the inner wrapper in the fiber's list. If the outer callback **yields or returns** that wrapper, `collect` moves ownership: the wrapper leaves the fiber's list and becomes part of the outer effect. If it is not yielded, it stays a direct child of the fiber. This implements the paper's \"parent composition\" (`ctx.dispose ← dispose ∘ ctx.dispose`) *without* nesting effect scopes: the accumulator of a fiber is the `DisposableList` `fiber._disposables`.","locale":"en"},"7584":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`utils.ts:5-40`. An insertion-ordered `Map<number, T>` plus a `WeakMap<T, number>`:","locale":"en"},"7585":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`push(v)` returns a remover `() => map.delete(sn)`;","locale":"en"},"7586":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`delete(v)` removes by identity;","locale":"en"},"7587":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`clear()` returns the values **reversed** (LIFO) and empties the list.","locale":"en"},"7588":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"It is used for fiber disposables, runtime fiber lists and per-fiber hook lists. It is an instance of the \"insert with fresh id, remove by id\" commutative-key design from paper §3.4.2 (see The context paradigm).","locale":"en"},"7589":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#accumulator","content":"The fiber's accumulator is not one composed closure but the list `fiber._disposables`. On unload (`fiber.ts:488-498`):","locale":"en"},"7590":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#accumulator","content":"Disposers are **initiated in reverse order but run concurrently**; each starts after a microtask. Inside a single effect they are sequential LIFO. The paper acknowledges this (\"`fiber.dispose` initiates a fiber's effects concurrently\", §5.1.3), and it is sound under the independence results (Theorem 43: inverses of independent effects can run in any order; see Metatheory).","locale":"en"},"7591":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-55","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#accumulator","content":"Ordered teardown *within* one logical effect must therefore be expressed by grouping it in one `ctx.effect` (a generator).","locale":"en"},"7592":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-56","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"Situation","locale":"en"},"7593":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-57","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"Behaviour","locale":"en"},"7594":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-58","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"sync throw in effect callback","locale":"en"},"7595":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-59","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"collected disposers run, error rethrown to caller","locale":"en"},"7596":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-60","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"async rejection in effect","locale":"en"},"7597":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-61","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"collected disposers run, error logged","locale":"en"},"7598":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"invalid yielded value","locale":"en"},"7599":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-63","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"`TypeError('Invalid effect')`","locale":"en"},"7600":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-64","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"error in a disposer during fiber unload","locale":"en"},"7601":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-65","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"logged; other disposers still run (`tests/fiber.spec.ts: 'dispose error'`, `service-dispose.spec.ts: 'releases dependencies after a cleanup error'`)","locale":"en"},"7602":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-66","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"effect on removed fiber","locale":"en"},"7603":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-67","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"`CordisError INACTIVE_EFFECT`","locale":"en"},"7604":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-68","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`tests/dispose.spec.ts` covers:","locale":"en"},"7605":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-69","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`dispose by plugin`, `dispose manually`, `yield dispose`;","locale":"en"},"7606":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-70","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`async return 1/2`, `async yield 1`;","locale":"en"},"7607":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-71","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`async yield 2/3 (aborted)`: disposing during setup stops the generator and disposes only what was yielded;","locale":"en"},"7608":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-72","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`async yield (aborted, finally)`: `finally` runs;","locale":"en"},"7609":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-73","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`async yield 4 (await dispose)`;","locale":"en"},"7610":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-74","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`return/yield with error`, `async yield invalid effect`.","locale":"en"},"7611":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"page","content":"Events and logger","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events","locale":"en"},"7612":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events","content":"Cordis's EventsService (registration as an effect, dispatch modes, internal events) and its logger (name resolution, levels, ex