e_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"`on()`","locale":"en"},"7674":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"intercept listener registration","locale":"en"},"7675":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-63","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"`internal/dispatch`","locale":"en"},"7676":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-64","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"every public dispatch","locale":"en"},"7677":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-65","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"observation","locale":"en"},"7678":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-66","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"The constructor installs:","locale":"en"},"7679":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-67","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"the `internal/listener` handler that turns `ctx.on('internal/update', …)` into a per-fiber hook list (`fiber._hooks['internal/update']`, itself a tracked effect);","locale":"en"},"7680":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-68","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"the global `internal/update` dispatcher that chains those hooks;","locale":"en"},"7681":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-69","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"the `internal/config` validator.","locale":"en"},"7682":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-70","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"`logger.ts`:","locale":"en"},"7683":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-71","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"`LoggerService` is a callable, `noShadow` service: `ctx.logger(name?)` returns a `Logger`; `ctx.logger.info(...)` is shorthand for `ctx.logger().info(...)`.","locale":"en"},"7684":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-72","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"**Name resolution:** explicit argument → interception metadata `{ name }` → the hyphenated name of the *caller's* fiber (`fiber.name` walks up to the first named runtime, else `root`). Inside a service method the caller is the service's def site, so log lines are attributed to the service (`logger.spec.ts` regression tests).","locale":"en"},"7685":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-73","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"**Level:** `exporter.levels[name] ?? exporter.levels.default ?? logger.level ?? INFO`; the levels are `ERROR=0, WARN=1, INFO=2, DEBUG=3`.","locale":"en"},"7686":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-74","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"**Messages:** `{ sn, ts, name, type, level, args, fiber?: WeakRef<Fiber> }`. Errors with a `cause` log the cause; non-empty `AggregateError`s are flattened.","locale":"en"},"7687":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-75","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"**Exporters** are registered with `logger.exporter(exp)` as a tracked effect, so a console exporter plugin unregisters on unload. A built-in exporter keeps a ring buffer of the last 1000 messages (for late-attached consoles).","locale":"en"},"7688":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-76","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"`Logger.format` implements printf-style `%s %d %i %f %o %O %c %C` with exporter-overridable formatters, colour codes (16/256-colour palettes hashed from the logger name) and per-line truncation (`maxLength`, default 10240).","locale":"en"},"7689":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-77","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#port","content":"Events are just a service built on `ctx.effect`. Nothing in the lifecycle depends on them except the internal hooks (status, service, commit, update, config). A port can implement typed event channels and keep a small set of internal hook points.","locale":"en"},"7690":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-78","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#port","content":"`waterfall` doubles as the extension mechanism for core behaviour (`internal/get`, `internal/config`, `internal/update`). In Rust these are better expressed as explicit hook traits or registries than as stringly-typed events.","locale":"en"},"7691":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-79","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#port","content":"The logger maps naturally onto `tracing` (a span per fiber, the logger name as target), but the *exporter-as-effect* and buffer semantics must be kept if consoles attach at runtime.","locale":"en"},"7692":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-80","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#port","content":"How kardia does this is described in API design.","locale":"en"},"7693":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"page","content":"Fiber lifecycle and registry","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","locale":"en"},"7694":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","content":"How Cordis core instantiates plugins as fibers, computes their targets, and drives them through the load/unload state machine with inertia and guards.","locale":"en"},"7695":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#plugins","content":"Plugins (components) and runtimes","locale":"en"},"7696":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#ctx-plugin","content":"`ctx.plugin(plugin, config)`","locale":"en"},"7697":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#replace","content":"`registry.replace(old, new)`","locale":"en"},"7698":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber","content":"The `Fiber` data structure","locale":"en"},"7699":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"`FiberState` vs. the paper's θ","locale":"en"},"7700":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#instantiation","content":"Instantiation: O-Insert and O-Retire","locale":"en"},"7701":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#target","content":"Target computation: `_checkImpl` and `_refresh`","locale":"en"},"7702":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/e