:"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code-140","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code#rust","content":"Follow the **code's** HMR design (unit-wise commit, in-place replacement) over Algorithm 10.","locale":"en"},"8311":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code-141","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code#rust","content":"Fix the realm-GC early `return` in the port.","locale":"en"},"8312":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code-142","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code#rust","content":"How kardia carries these out is described in Lifecycle, API design, Loader, include and HMR and, with every deviation listed, Status.","locale":"en"},"8313":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","type":"page","content":"Services and traceability","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-services","locale":"en"},"8314":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services","content":"How Cordis attributes effects created inside service methods to the calling fiber, using the Service base class, trackers and traceable proxies.","locale":"en"},"8315":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-services#problem","content":"The problem it solves","locale":"en"},"8316":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-services#service","content":"The `Service` base class","locale":"en"},"8317":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-services#traceable-proxies","content