8362":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#associated-properties","content":"Covered by `tests/associate.spec.ts`. A service named `foo.bar` (or a property provided as `foo.bar`) is reachable as `ctx.foo.bar`. Objects created by a service (e.g. a `Session` with tracker `associate: 'session'`) expose mixins registered under `session.*` by *other* plugins (`ctx.mixin('bar', { answer: 'session.answer' })`). Visibility follows the declaring fiber (`'associated access follows the service fiber'`).","locale":"en"},"8363":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#associated-properties","content":"This is how independent plugins extend each other's types at runtime: the dynamic counterpart of TypeScript module augmentation (paper §6.4, see Discussion and related work).","locale":"en"},"8364":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"Concern","locale":"en"},"8365":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"JS mechanism","locale":"en"},"8366":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"Must be preserved as","locale":"en"},"8367":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"Effects attributed to the caller","locale":"en"},"8368":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"`service.ctx` returns use-site ctx via Proxy","locale":"en"},"8369