ugin-hmr 如何以单个事务、借助并查集提交单元原地替换发生变化的插件，以及它与论文算法 10 的区别。"],[3673,"@cordisjs/plugin-include 如何把 YAML/JSON 文件嫁接进条目树并保持文件与纤程的双向同步，以及 @cordisjs/plugin-group 是什么。"],[3756,"@cordisjs/plugin-loader 如何把声明式的条目树变为纤程并使两者保持同步：条目、表达式、协调、托管领域与校验。"],[2888,"@kardiajs npm 包：在 TypeScript 中使用同一套插件模型、把 TypeScript 运行时（如 Tauri webview）连接到 Rust kardia 应用的桥，以及 Vue 界面的扩展点。"],[4798,"**\\[Rust] note on RAII:** the paper explicitly positions Rust's ownership/RAII as *statically scoped* reversal: complementary, not a substitute. A Rust port should therefore *not* try to make a component's lifetime a lexical scope; component lifetime is dynamic and governed by the fiber state machine, while `Drop` remains useful for resources local to one effect."],[490,"**\\[Rust]** Rust 的 `TypeId`/以类型为键的服务*在单个二进制内*避免了冲突（一种键命名空间），但在动态加载的模块之间 `TypeId` 并不稳定，因此此时键必须是字符串加上一个 ABI/版本标签。"],[4752,"**\\[Rust]** Rust's `TypeId`/type-keyed services give collision-freedom *within one binary* (a form of key namespacing), but across dynamically loaded modules `TypeId` is not stable, so keys must then be strings plus an ABI/version tag."],[4726,"**\\[Rust]** The broker pattern is the recommended way to get many providers per key within the single-provider calculus."],[464,"**\\[Rust]** 在单一提供者的演算中，代理模式是让一个键拥有多个提供者的推荐方式。"],[7199,"**`<ExtensionSlot name>`** renders the components of a point, in order. Each one gets the context of the plugin that contributed it, so inside it `useContext()`, `usePlugin()` and `useService()` act as that plugin, and its effects stop with it. `props` go to every component, under each contribution's own; the default slot shows while there is nothing; the `item` slot (`{ item, owner }`) renders each contribution itself."],[2938,"**`<ExtensionSlot name>`** 按顺序渲染一个贡献点的组件。每个组件都获得贡献它的插件的上下文，因此在组件内部 `useContext()`、`usePlugin()` 和 `useService()` 都以该插件的身份工作，其效应也随该插件停止。`props` 传给每个组件，位于各贡献自身的 `props` 之下；没有内容时显示默认插槽；`item` 插槽（`{ item, owner }`）可自行渲染每个贡献。"],[5821,"**`config`** can be any value; the plugin decodes it. A group's `config` (`group: true`) must be a list of entries."],[1560,"**`config`** 可以是任意值，由插件自行解码。分组（`group: true`）的 `config` 必须是条目列表。"],[6610,"**`create(options, parent, position)`** validates the options deeply (including a group's members) before anything is committed, assigns an id if there is none, inserts the entry at `position` (clamped; `None` appends) in the group of entry `parent` (`None` for the root group) and starts it. A group entry creates its group when its plugin loads, so a `parent` that is still loading is awaited. (Entries that come from a file or a group update are validated shallowly instead, each group member when its group reconciles it; `kardia_loader::validate_options(&options, deep)` is the check.)"],[2349,"**`create(options, parent, position)`** 在提交任何内容之前深度校验选项（包括分组的成员），在没有 id 时分配一个，把条目插入到条目 `parent` 的分组（`None` 表示根分组）中的 `position` 处（会被截断到有效范围；`None` 表示追加到末尾），然后启动它。分组条目在其插件加载时才创建分组，所以仍在加载中的 `parent` 会被等待。（来自文件或分组更新的条目改为浅层校验，每个分组成员在其分组调和它时校验；校验函数是 `kardia_loader::validate_options(&options, deep)`。）"],[6878,"**`ctx.checkpoint()?`** is a point where a superseded load stops. It returns `Err(Interrupted)` when the plugin's target changed since the load began (it was updated, disposed or lost a dependency). Returning that error from `apply` is not a failure: the plugin unloads what it registered so far. kardia never cancels a running `apply` by itself."],[2617,"**`ctx.checkpoint()?`** 是过时的加载在此停止的位置。如果插件的目标在本次加载开始后发生了变化（被更新、被释放或失去了某个依赖），它返回 `Err(Interrupted)`。从 `apply` 返回这个错误并不算失败：插件会卸载它目前为止注册的内容。kardia 自身从不取消正在运行的 `apply`。"],[5531,"**`current_thread`** (`#[tokio::test]`)"],[1270,"**`current_thread`**（`#[tokio::test]`）"],[5823,"**`disabled`** is a boolean or an expression. On a group, it does not stop the group itself: it disables the entries inside it."],[1562,"**`disabled`** 是布尔值或表达式。用在分组上时，它不会停止分组本身，而是禁用分组内的条目。"],[6124,"**`dispose()`** retires the fiber: it is marked removed, its live provisions are unbound at once, it unloads and settles to `Disposed`. For the root fiber, `dispose()` restarts the root, reverting everything registered on it; this is how an app shuts down:"],[1863,"**`dispose()`** 让纤程退役：它被标为已移除，现存的提供立即解除绑定，然后卸载并稳定为 `Disposed`。对根纤程而言，`dispose()` 会重启根，撤销登记在其上的一切；应用就是这样关闭的："],[6123,"**`fail(error)`** fails the fiber from outside, as a load returning `error` would: it unloads, reverting its effects and provisions, and settles as `Failed` with that error until `update` or `registry.replace` clears it. A load in flight finishes first; a fiber that has already failed keeps its first error. It is how a host reports a failure that happens after `apply`, such as a guest process that exits."],[1862,"**`fail(error)`** 从外部使纤程失败，效果与加载返回 `error` 相同：纤程卸载，撤销其副作用和提供的服务，并以该错误停留在 `Failed`，直到 `update` 或 `registry.replace` 清除它。正在进行的加载会先完成；已经失败的纤程保留它的第一个错误。宿主用它报告 `apply` 之后发生的失败，例如退出的访客进程。"],[5822,"**`group`** is a boolean."],[1561,"**`group`** 是布尔值。"],[5819,"**`id`** is a string and must not contain `:` (the loader joins ids across included files with `:`). A missing id is generated when the file is read: eight hexadecimal digits. An anonymous entry that is unchanged on the next read keeps its id, so editing a neighbour does not restart it. Generated ids reach the file with the next write-back."],[1558,"**`id`** 是字符串，且不能包含 `:`（加载器（loader）用 `:` 连接跨 include（配置文件引入）文件的 id）。缺失的 id 在读取文件时生成：八位十六进制数字。在下一次读取时内容未变的匿名条目会保留其 id，因此编辑相邻条目不会让它重启。生成的 id 随下一次写回进入文件。"],[6661,"**`inject`** as a map attaches metadata to a declared dependency: `inject: { loader: { await: true } }`. The metadata may contain expressions, evaluated in the parent group's context; a failure disables the entry."],[5824,"**`inject`** is a list of service names, or a map from service name to interception metadata (`null` for none)."],[2400,"**`inject`** 写成映射时，可为声明的依赖附加元数据：`inject: { loader: { await: true } }`。元数据可以包含表达式，在父分组的上下文中求值；失败会禁用条目。"],[1563,"**`inject`** 是服务名列表，或从服务名到拦截元数据的映射（`null` 表示没有元数据）。"],[5825,"**`intercept`** is a map from service name to metadata. Changing it applies to the running plugin in place, without a restart."],[6660,"**`intercept`** is metadata for the services the entry's plugin uses, keyed by service: `intercept: { logger: { name: db, level: 3 } }`. It is evaluated (it may contain expressions) and swapped in place, so a running plugin sees new metadata without a restart. A failing `intercept` disables the entry."],[1564,"**`intercept`** 是从服务名到元数据的映射。修改它会原地作用于运行中的插件，无需重启。"],[2399,"**`intercept`** 是条目的插件所用服务的元数据，按服务分键：`intercept: { logger: { name: db, level: 3 } }`。它会被求值（可以包含表达式）并原地替换，所以运行中的插件无需重启就能看到新元数据。`intercept` 求值失败会禁用条目。"],[6655,"**`isolate`** gives the entry's services their own realm:"],[5826,"**`isolate`** is a map from service name to `true` (a scope private to the entry) or a label (a scope shared by every entry with that label)."],[1565,"**`isolate`** 是从服务名到 `true`（该条目私有的作用域）或标签（所有带该标签的条目共享的作用域）的映射。"],[2394,"**`isolate`** 给条目的服务一个自己的领域（realm）："],[6390,"**`kardia-guest/2`** sends the same messages, each with an `id`: an export carries a new `id`, and every message about it carries the same one (`{\"id\":3,\"call\":\"view\",\"key\":\"db\"}`, `{\"id\":3,\"result\":…}`, `{\"id\":3,\"output\":…}`, `{\"id\":3,\"done\":0}`). The host calls one export at a time. Two more messages need no running export:"],[2129,"**`kardia-guest/2`** 发送相同的消息，但每条都带有 `id`：每次导出带一个新的 `id`，与它有关的每条消息都带同一个 `id`（`{\"id\":3,\"call\":\"view\",\"key\":\"db\"}`、`{\"id\":3,\"result\":…}`、`{\"id\":3,\"output\":…}`、`{\"id\":3,\"done\":0}`）。宿主一次只调用一个导出。另有两条消息不需要正在运行的导出："],[5311,"**`loader` await barrier**"],[1050,"**`loader` 等待屏障**"],[1274,"**`multi_thread`**"],[5535,"**`multi_thread`**"],[5820,"**`name`** is required. A name that is not a built-in plugin is a guest module path, relative to the config file: `.wasm` or `.wat` for WebAssembly, anything else a dynamic library. See Guest plugins."],[1559,"**`name`** 必填。不是内置插件名的名字是访客模块路径，相对于配置文件：`.wasm` 或 `.wat` 表示 WebAssembly，其他扩展名表示动态库。见访客插件。"],[6615,"**`remove(id)`** disposes the entry and removes it from its group."],[2354,"**`remove(id)`** 释放条目，并把它从所在分组中移除。"],[6122,"**`restart()`** bumps the fiber's revision, so it unloads and loads again with the same configuration. It fails on a retired fiber, and it does not recover a `Failed` fiber: the failure stays (and `settled()` keeps returning it) until `update` or `registry.replace` clears it."],[1861,"**`restart()`** 递增纤程的修订号，使它以相同配置卸载并重新加载。对已退役的纤程会失败；它也不能恢复 `Failed` 的纤程：在 `update` 或 `registry.replace` 清除错误之前，失败一直保留（`settled()` 也一直返回它）。"],[6116,"**`update(config)`**:"],[1855,"**`update(config)`**："],[6611,"**`update(id, patch, parent, position)`** merges `patch` into the options (`null` deletes a key), validates the result and applies it. `parent: None` leaves the entry where it is; `Some(None)` moves it to the root group and `Some(Some(id))` into the group of entry `id`, also across trees: a move into another tree takes the entry's group members along and fails if one of their ids already exists there."],[2350,"**`update(id, patch, parent, position)`** 把 `patch` 合并进选项（`null` 删除一个键），校验结果并应用。`parent: None` 表示条目留在原处；`Some(None)` 把它移到根分组，`Some(Some(id))` 把它移入条目 `id` 的分组，也可以跨树移动：移入另一棵树时，条目的分组成员会一起移动；若其中某个 id 在目标树中已存在，则移动失败。"],[3057,"**`wasm32-unknown-unknown` 目标**，仅在构建 WebAssembly 访客插件（guest plugin）或运行完整测试套件时需要："],[5405,"**0. Scaffold**"],[1144,"**0. 脚手架**"],[5408,"**1. Effects & store**"],[1147,"**1. 效应与存储**"],[5411,"**2. Fibers & lifecycle**"],[1150,"**2. 纤程与生命周期**"],[5414,"**3. Services & built-ins**"],[1153,"**3. 服务与内置服务**"],[5417,"**4. Loader**"],[1156,"**4. 加载器**"],[5420,"**5. Include & fs**"],[1159,"**5. Include 与 fs**"],[5423,"**6. Ergonomics**"],[1162,"**6. 易用性**"],[5426,"**7. Dynamic modules (optional)**"],[1165,"**7. 动态模块（可选）**"],[4900,"**A calculus of dynamic composition** (§4): a component is a triple `(d, p, e)` (dependencies, provisions, effect iterator); its instantiations are **fibers**; nine rules (3 orchestration, 6 lifecycle) move fibers through `Inactive → Reloading → Active → Unloading`. The metatheory proves preservation, recovery exactness, ordering, resolution coherence, progress (no deadlock and termination) and **confluence** (the quiescent state equals a from-scratch static load of the final configuration)."],[7307,"**A contributor** to kardia"],[7305,"**A plugin author** writing plugins in Rust or as guest modules"],[7309,"**A researcher** interested in the theory"],[6931,"**A retired provider frees its realm at once.** Disposing a provider unbinds its live provisions immediately, so a successor can provide in the same realm while the old consumers still drain (they keep reading the old binding through their committed views)."],[7020,"**A service's own dependencies.** A service resolves its own dependencies through the `Context` it stored when it was constructed (its definition site), so no shadow contexts are needed. Two consequences differ from Cordis, where both follow the use site:"],[6932,"**A stale load cannot provide.** A retired fiber whose load is still in flight may still register inverses (so nothing it acquired leaks), but its `provide` calls fail with `KardiaError::InactiveEffect`."],[7303,"**A user** running an app from a config file"],[7896,"**Abort/commit**: units with any failed import are aborted and their modules restored. Orphaned evicted modules are restored with the aborted units they overlap (unless they reach a committed unit). Stage-1-loaded modules linked against restored modules are evicted."],[6467,"**Accept.** The changed modules and every module that imports an accepted one (except host modules) are accepted."],[4720,"**Acquisition vs. emission.** Reaching outside happens in two stages: *acquisition* installs a record inside the boundary (`open` → descriptor, `malloc` → block, `fork` → child), which is revertible; *emission* pushes data through that channel (`write`, `send`) and crosses outside, which is not revertible."],[7232,"**Adding a TypeScript side, such as a Tauri webview:** TypeScript and Tauri."],[4894,"**Agent harnesses**: a harness that rewrites its own components continuously cannot afford a restart per modification, and naive code replacement silently breaks dependents."],[4566,"**Algorithm 7 – realm reassignment with delimiters.** There is one delimiter symbol `δ_k` per key; each context stores a tag under `δ_k`, inherited by descendants and redrawn on each reassignment, so that `γ′[δ_k] = d₁ ⇔ γ′` derives from the entry's context."],[5002,"**Alternative considered:** a `!Send` design (`Rc<RefCell<..>>` on a `LocalSet`) mirrors JS most literally and was recommended by one analysis pass for the loader. It is rejected for the core because it would force every plugin and service in the ecosystem to be `!Send`-compatible (no `tokio::spawn`, awkward with most async libraries), while the lock-plus-actions discipline above preserves the same atomicity with comparable complexity. If profiling later shows lock contention on the access hot path, committed views (immutable per episode) can be published through `arc-swap` without changing semantics."],[7890,"**Analyze**: reverse edges (excluding edges from host modules). `accepted` = the changed modules plus everything that transitively imports them; `declined` = host ∪ the rest. *(The paper's Algorithm 8 is a fixed point over forward imports with cycles defaulting to declined; the code is a simpler reverse-reachability worklist.)*"],[6676,"**Anonymous entries.** Entries the file leaves without an id get one before the loader sees them, and the id is written back. An anonymous entry that looks exactly like one from the previous read keeps that id (unless the file now names it explicitly), so editing a neighbour does not restart it."],[5856,"**App → file.** Changes made at runtime, through the loader API or by a plugin updating or disposing itself, are written back to whoever owns them: the file, or a patch in the configuration of the `include` that loaded it (see `include`). Generated ids are written along with them."],[4472,"**application frameworks**, for example Koishi (§5.3)."],[6911,"**Associated services.** Cordis's `foo.bar` associated services and `ctx.mixin` are JavaScript-object conveniences. In kardia a service named `foo.bar` is just another key. To \"extend\" another plugin's type, use an extension trait (compile time, see `Svc<T>` and the caller) or a registry service built on `kardia_core::IdTable` (run time). No accessor or mixin layer is ported."],[6008,"**Asynchronous:** `ctx.effect(label, |scope| async move { … })` spawns the body. It is never dropped half-way: disposal waits for it to reach its end or an iteration boundary. A failure disposes what the body collected, is logged, and is reported by `EffectHandle::ready()`. Returning `Interrupted` (see below) is not a failure."],[5328,"**Atomic writes:** temp file in the same directory, stale-content check before every rename, bounded retry on `PermissionDenied`/`ResourceBusy`, read-only → keep journal in memory."],[6687,"**Atomic writes.** The include writes a temp file in the same directory (`.<name>.<pid>.<seq>.tmp`) and renames it over the file, so no reader sees a truncated file."],[7893,"**Backup and evict** every evicted URL (the whole multi-slot ESM entry + the CJS module)."],[5607,"**Behavioural parity with Cordis core** where the paper is silent (epoch with revision, two-level guard, concurrent fiber-level disposal, `update` veto, `replace`), using the TypeScript test suite as the acceptance specification."],[7809,"**Binding-level** (`provide`'s inverse, see `provide`): withdrawing one binding waits for that binding's dependents only. This lets one provider withdraw binding A without waiting for consumers of binding B (`service-dispose.spec.ts: 'withdraws one binding without waiting for another binding from the same provider'`), and lets a binding be replaced during a consumer's initialization."],[8035,"**Bootstrap** (`core/bin.js`): create a root `Context`, set `baseUrl` to the cwd, `await ctx.plugin(Loader)`, then `ctx.loader.create({ name: '@cordisjs/plugin-include', config: { path: './cordis.yml' } })`."],[5387,"**Boundaries:** `ctx.checkpoint()?` and `ctx.on_dispose(..)?` are synchronous and fallible."],[7230,"**Building your own host around the loader:** Loader."],[7177,"**Calls are asynchronous** in both directions. A call into the other side fails with `unavailable` when that side is gone, and with `timeout` when it does not answer."],[4728,"**Capability-based access control.** Proxy-mediated access only allows declared dependencies (an undeclared access is an error). `inject` acts as a capability request, the context proxy as a capability mediator. Because declarations are static, the orchestrator can review them at load time."],[5319,"**Catalog:** `Catalog::register::<P>()`, `register_def(name, def)` and `alias(alias, name)` (not `register_alias`); `kardia_loader::builtins()` registers `group` and aliases `@cordisjs/plugin-group` to it, and `kardia::catalog()` adds the other built-in plugins under their names and their JavaScript package names."],[5305,"**Catalog**"],[7375,"**Change the config.** In `examples/kardia.yml`, set `disabled: false` on the `console` entry: the console logger starts. Set it back to `true` and it stops."],[6976,"**Checked access** (the paper's Algorithm 6) resolves a key like this:"],[5320,"**Checkpoint:** synchronous, `ctx.checkpoint()?`."],[6185,"**Child processes.** `ProcessSource` runs each plugin instance as its own process, speaking the guest ABI as JSON lines over stdin and stdout (see Process transport). A guest whose process ends fails only its own plugin; one that breaks the protocol or outlives a call's deadline is killed. Process guests covers arguments, spawners, timeouts and exit reports. Replace an executable by renaming a new file over it: a running executable cannot be written to, and one held open for writing cannot be started."],[4895,"**Coarse-grained workaround**: OS processes give temporal composability per process; container orchestrators give spatial composability per service. Both discard in-process state on restart and cannot express in-address-space dependencies; the granularity is wrong."],[8263,"**Code:** `_runner.epoch` = `\"<revision>:<uid>:<uid>…\"` or `'__INACTIVE__'`. The **revision** counter folds configuration revisions into the target: `restart()`, `update()` and `registry.replace()` bump it, forcing an unload→reload chain without retiring the fiber. This realizes the §4.4 *Configuration* revision more cheaply than retire → remove → reinsert at the same name."],[8269,"**Code:** explicit reverse references `Impl.dependents: Set<Fiber>`, populated at commit time and removed at the end of the dependent's unload, plus wake-up resolvers (`impl.release`, `fiber._release`). Two guards exist: the **fiber-level** guard (no disposer of the provider runs until *all* its provisions are free) and the **binding-level** guard inside `provide`'s inverse. This gives the paper's per-binding semantics (`relied_n`) while letting a provider withdraw one binding without waiting for another."],[8272,"**Code:** fiber-level disposers are *initiated* in reverse order but run **concurrently** (`Promise.all`), each after one microtask; errors are logged and do not stop the others. Sequential LIFO holds only *inside* one `ctx.effect`. The paper acknowledges the concurrency (§5.1.3) and it is justified by Theorem 43 (independent inverses commute), but it means ordering-sensitive teardown must be grouped into one effect."],[8277,"**Code:** it iterates all runtimes' fibers, filters by declared key and **realm symbol** (or a custom filter during realm moves), recomputes only the affected keys (`_checkImpl`), then calls `_refresh`. It also emits `internal/service`. Notifications for a fiber's provisions are issued from `_updateState` only on transitions into or out of `ACTIVE`."],[8275,"**Code:** only **async** iterators are interruptible; sync iterators and plain functions run to completion (they cannot be interrupted in a single-threaded host anyway). Async iterators take the *landing* alternative (an inertial host) and are closed with `iter.return()` so `finally` blocks run. `_reload` also yields one microtask before executing, so superseded loads never start."],[8266,"**Code:** the instantiation effect's inverse sets `uid = null` (removed from the runtime immediately), forces the target to ⊥, then awaits the transition chain; the final state is `DISPOSED`. There is no persistent registry of retired entries. Re-enabling an entry creates a **fresh fiber** (as the paper prescribes)."],[4719,"**Coeffects move the boundary** by reifying an external location behind operations that each have an inverse. The boundary is drawn *per location*, not per medium (a private scratch file is inside; a shared path is outside)."],[4937,"**Coeffects.** Judgments `Γ @ coeffect ⊢ t : T` annotate the *context*. Comonads `(D, ε, δ)` (Uustalu and Vene) structure context-dependent computation; Petricek et al. propose coeffects as a unified static analysis; graded coeffects use a pre-ordered semiring to quantify usage."],[7392,"**Common theme:** every resource is registered through `ctx.effect` on the *calling* fiber (found via the service tracker, see Services and traceability), so it is released when the caller unloads. There is no per-consumer bookkeeping in the service."],[6186,"**Common to all three.** `GuestService::call` blocks its caller until the guest answers; `call_async` runs the call off the async workers, as the bridge does with `apply` and `dispose`. A deadline stops a process guest (it is killed) and a WASM guest with a time limit (it traps); a dylib guest runs on the caller's thread and cannot be stopped. There is no separate broker service: each fiber's `GuestService` is the RPC endpoint. The backends are cargo features of `kardia-hmr` (`wasm`, `dylib`, `process`, all on by default), beside `preserve-order` (on by default), which turns on `serde_json/preserve_order` through `kardia-loader`; leave it off to keep serde_json's default maps in your application (Key order)."],[7201,"**Composables:** `useContext()`; `usePlugin(plugin, config)` runs a plugin for the lifetime of a component; `useService(key)` is a ref that follows a service (`undefined` while none is provided); `useContributions(key)` is a computed list for custom rendering, such as a navigation menu; `useFiberState(fiber)` follows a fiber."],[5388,"**Configuration:** `ctx.plugin::<P>(config)` requires `P::Config: Serialize` (the value is serialized and decoded like any other configuration), so a `Deserialize`-only config is passed as JSON with `plugin_value`. `db.update(value)?` validates at once and returns the future to await; `update_with(value, no_save)` takes the flag."],[6691,"**Conflicts: the file wins.** When the file changes while runtime changes are pending, the include merges three ways. Conflicting runtime changes are dropped so that the tree follows the file, and each drop is logged as `config conflict in <path>: entry <id> <reason>; file wins`, with one of these reasons:"],[5857,"**Conflicts:** when the file and the app both changed, the file wins."],[5574,"**Confluence**"],[7198,"**Contribution points** are `Contributions<T>` services (`defineContributions(key)` provides one). `register(item)` is an effect of the calling plugin; items are ordered by `order`, an `id` is unique, and `items` / `entries` are Vue-reactive."],[4901,"**Cordis** (§5): a TypeScript meta-framework, made of a core library (effect tracking and coeffect resolution) and a declarative loader with configuration reconciliation and hot module replacement. Case study: **Koishi**, a chatbot framework with more than 4000 community plugins (Koishi uses Cordis v3; the paper describes v4)."],[7254,"**Cordis** is the meta-framework of spatiotemporal composability described in the paper *A Programming Paradigm for Spatiotemporal Composability* (Shi, Zhang & Cui, arXiv:2608.25512). Its reference implementation is written in TypeScript."],[2993,"**Cordis** 是论文 *A Programming Paradigm for Spatiotemporal Composability*（Shi、Zhang 与 Cui，arXiv:2608.25512）所描述的时空可组合性元框架，其参考实现用 TypeScript 编写。"],[640,"**Cordis**（§5）：一个 TypeScript 元框架，由核心库（效应追踪与余效应解析）和一个带配置协调与模块热替换的声明式加载器组成。案例研究：**Koishi**，一个拥有超过 4000 个社区插件的聊天机器人框架（Koishi 使用 Cordis v3；论文描述的是 v4）。"],[4609,"**Corollary 69 (Terminal recovery)**: after an episode closes, the state equals \"other fibers only\"; in particular `σ_n = ∅` (which is O-Remove's premise)."],[5318,"**Data model:** `EntryOptions` is a typed view read from options already accepted by `validate_options` (`EntryOptions::read`); the JSON object stays the source of truth, so unknown keys survive write-back without a `flatten` map. `IsolateLabel::{Private, Shared(String)}` and `Disabled::{Bool(bool), Expr(String)}` are as planned."],[5297,"**Data model**"],[5386,"**Declarations:** `fn inject() -> Inject` (here `Inject::of::<(Database,)>()`) replaces `type Inject`, and `fn provide() -> Vec<Key>` replaces the `&'static [&'static str]` slice. `#[derive(Service)]` implements `Service` (the hand-written `impl Service for Database` also works). With the `#[plugin]` macro, a plugin is an `async fn` taking `Injected<(Database,)>`, which turns undeclared access into a compile error (see Plugins)."],[8328,"**def site**"],[4413,"**Definition 31 – tests / indistinguishability.** A *test* over `𝒜` is a finite word of forward maps and yielded inverses of operations; `v ≈_𝒜 v′` when every test is defined at both or at neither and yields equal outcomes. `≃_k := ≈_{𝒜_k}`."],[4415,"**Definition 33**: states related at key set `S` have the same domain on `S` and related values at each key. `≃` (`S = K`) is the finest; `≃_S` forgets keys outside `S`. Related states agree on satisfaction and on `notify_d`, so *reactivity is a property of `Σ/≃`*."],[4416,"**Definition 34**: the logical-relation extension of `≃` to functions, products and `Maybe`, read coinductively for iterators. A map *respects* `≃` when it is related to itself."],[4422,"**Definition 40**: `reach(i)` is the set of iterators reachable by continuation; the transformation monoid `𝔐(i)` is generated by all forward maps and yielded inverses in `reach(i)`; `len(i)` is the longest continuation chain."],[4424,"**Definition 42 – independent iterators** `i, j`:"],[4428,"**Definition 44**: operations `a, a′` are independent when their lifts are independent effect functions *and* neither disturbs the other's outcome. A key is **commutative** when any two of its operations (including an operation with itself) are independent."],[4430,"**Definition 46 – witnessed coeffect**: a coeffect carries, as a third constituent, a proof that its key is commutative. As with the effect witness, *the obligation falls on the component providing the key*, not on consumers. From here on every coeffect is assumed witnessed."],[4321,"**Definition 54 – relied upon:** `relied_n(γ) := ∃m ≠ n, k ∈ d_m. installed_m(γ) ∧ ω_m(k) = n`"],[4329,"**Definition 55 – confined to `n`.** A map is confined to `n` if it (1) *writes* only `σ_n` and the values other tables hold at keys of `d_n` (a consumer operating on a coeffect writes the provider's table at that key), never control fields or the registry domain; and (2) *reads* only `σ_n` and `σ_m|_{d_n}`. Instantiation is the one exception (it writes a fresh entry; its inverse writes one `τ`)."],[4330,"**Definition 56 – context-mediated iterators for `n`.** The least set containing the unit and three iteration forms: the lift of an operation stage at a key of `d_n ∪ p_n`; the lift of a provision stage at a key of `p_n` (landing in `σ_n`); an instantiation. **Every fiber's effect function must lie in this set.**"],[4602,"**Definition 63 – well-formed registry:** (1) parents exist (or are `root`); (2) provisions are pairwise disjoint; (3) an installed fiber's `ω` is total on `d_n` and names existing fibers; (4) every fiber an installed `ω` names is installed."],[4604,"**Definition 65**: fibers `m, n` are *entangled* when one's provision meets the other's declarations. A run is *pairwise independent* when every pair of fibers is independent, or entangled with only commutative shared keys."],[4615,"**Definition 72**: precedence `n ≺ m := p_n ∩ d_m ≠ ∅` (`n` may provide a key `m` declares). Acyclicity of `≺` is an **assumption** (a component that declares a key it provides itself violates it)."],[4620,"**Definition 74 – support set A**: `n ∈ A ⇔ ¬τ_n ∧ (π_n = root ∨ π_n ∈ A) ∧ ∀k ∈ d_n. ∃m ∈ A. k ∈ p_m`, a function of `τ, π, d, p` only. **Lemma 75**: the support relation is well-founded and `A` is unique."],[4621,"**Definition 76 – total on its provision**: a finished activation has installed every key of `p`. **Lemma 77**: at quiescence (with totality), `A` is the set of Active fibers."],[4551,"**Definition 81 – entry:** `id` (stable reconciliation key), `url` (component module), `isolate`, `intercept`, `config`, `disabled`. An entry is a faithful specification because it records exactly what the support set reads: `disabled` → `τ`, tree parent → `π`, `url` → `(d, p)`. Entries form a **configuration tree**; `@cordisjs/group` loads a list of child entries; `@cordisjs/include` grafts an external YAML or JSON file. Binding is **bidirectional**: a component that revises its own config or disables itself has the change written back."],[4418,"**Definitions 36/37**: effect functions and iterators *witnessed up to `≃_S`*: `g(δ) ≃_S γ` instead of equality."],[5391,"**Dependencies:** `#[derive(Deserialize)]` needs `serde` with the `derive` feature among the crate's own dependencies, even though `kardia::prelude` re-exports the derive."],[6954,"**Dependency cycles.** When a fiber is inserted, the runtime checks whether the declared `provide` and `inject` sets of the live fibers in its realm form a cycle through it. If they do, it logs a warning naming the cycle (`dependency cycle: a -> b -> a`) and the fiber stays `Pending`, instead of waiting silently."],[4683,"**Derived**: leave the input intact and return a *fresh context deriving from it* with the identity inverse; recovery discards the derived context."],[7891,"**Discover**: for accepted modules, unwrap the exports and keep those that are registered plugins; **group them by runtime** (several modules can export the same plugin)."],[1077,"**dylib（`libloading`）**：仅用于开发期：相同的工具链，每个版本从一个唯一的复制路径加载，**永不卸载**（由于 TLS 析构函数和泄漏的 `'static` 引用，卸载 Rust dylib 是不可靠的），C-ABI 入口点。"],[5338,"**dylibs (`libloading`):** development-time only: same toolchain, each version loaded from a unique copied path, **never unloaded** (unloading Rust dylibs is unsound with TLS destructors and leaked `'static` references), C-ABI entry point."],[5380,"**Dynamic code:** the static catalog came first; the WASM, dylib and process backends followed (see Dynamic modules)."],[6184,"**Dynamic libraries.** `DylibSource` speaks a C ABI instead of passing Rust types: a `cdylib` carries its own copies of `kardia-core` and tokio, with separate statics and no runtime context. Each load copies the library to a fresh path (in a `kardia-dylib-<pid>` directory under the temp directory), because the platform loader hands out the library it already loaded for a known path. Libraries are never unloaded: unloading Rust code is unsound once it registered thread-local destructors or handed out `'static` references."],[7175,"**Effects never cross.** Each side reverts its own."],[7018,"**Effects on the caller's behalf.** A service method that creates an effect for its caller registers it on `svc.caller()`. The effect then belongs to the caller's fiber and is reverted when the *caller* unloads, which is what Cordis's tracker achieves with `this.ctx`. Service crates expose such methods as **extension traits on `Svc<S>`**, which coherence allows because the trait is local. The timer service does this (simplified: the real `timeout` also reverts its effect once it has fired):"],[7183,"**Effects:** `ctx.effect(scope => ...)` collects inverses with `scope.defer` or returns one. An asynchronous body is never cancelled: `scope.checkpoint()` ends it once the effect is disposed."],[7245,"**Effects:** everything a plugin sets up (listeners, timers, services, child plugins) is tracked and reverted when the plugin stops."],[4936,"**Effects.** Judgments `Γ ⊢ t : T ! effect`. Monadic effects (Moggi, Wadler) encapsulate effectful computation in `T(A)` with unit `η` and multiplication `μ`. Algebraic effects (Plotkin and Power) declare operation signatures; effect handlers (Plotkin and Pretnar) interpret them with delimited continuations (Koka, Eff, OCaml 5)."],[6715,"**Entry errors** the loader logs (option and config validation, `ModuleNotFound`, expression failures) are located through the tree backend's `locate` / `locate_expr`. Each issue gets `(at <path>, file:line:col)`, an expression failure an `at <path> (file:line:col)` frame, and the entry and each ancestor that has a position an `at <id> (file:line:col)` frame:"],[5301,"**Entry state machine**"],[5385,"**Errors:** `Result<()>` (`kardia_core::Result`) replaces `Result<(), PluginError>` and `anyhow::Result`."],[5329,"**Errors:** structured `ConfigFrame { id, file, line, col }` chains instead of rewritten stack strings."],[7185,"**Events** are named: `ctx.on`, `emit`, `bail`, `serial`, `parallel`. The runtime reports `internal/plugin-inserted`, `internal/plugin-removed`, `internal/status`, `internal/service`, `internal/commit` and `internal/replace`."],[7178,"**Events** go from the host to every client, named."],[7531,"**Everything is in the root.** There is one `store`, one `props` and one `registry` per root; derived contexts differ only by their prototype-chained `isolate`/`intercept` tables and their `fiber`. This keeps \"is key k provided in realm r?\" a single map lookup."],[4723,"**Exclusive binding**: at most one is bound at a time; switching unloads one provider and loads another, perturbing every consumer."],[7687,"**Exporters** are registered with `logger.exporter(exp)` as a tracked effect, so a console exporter plugin unregisters on unload. A built-in exporter keeps a ring buffer of the last 1000 messages (for late-attached consoles)."],[6334,"**Exports** (status `0` is success; on failure the guest `write`s the error):"],[5379,"**Expressions:** decided as a side-effect-free JavaScript subset (`kardia_loader::expr`), not CEL; see Status and deviations."],[5323,"**Expressions:** implemented as a side-effect-free JavaScript subset (`kardia_loader::expr`) instead of CEL; identifiers resolve through the JSON views of services (`ctx.view(name)`, provided with `provide_serialized_as`), not through an `ExprValue` trait; see Expressions."],[5315,"**Expressions** (`!!js`)"],[7200,"**Failing contributions** are contained: a contribution that throws (in setup, render, a hook, a watcher or a handler) is replaced by the `error` slot (`{ error, item, owner, retry }`), or by nothing without one, while the other contributions keep rendering and the error does not reach the app. `retry()` mounts it again. `@error` (`{ error, item, owner }`) reports the failure, for example to show which plugin failed; without it, the failure is logged by the owner's logger. The owner's plugin keeps running: a broken view is one contribution of the plugin, and stopping the plugin would also remove its services and its other contributions. To stop it, call `owner.fiber.dispose()` from `@error`."],[7808,"**Fiber-level** (the `_unload` loop): a provider fiber does not run *any* disposer until no provision has dependents."],[5855,"**File → app.** When the file changes, the new entries are reconciled with the running ones by `id`: a changed entry is updated in place, a new one starts, a removed one stops."],[6674,"**File edits → tree.** Each read is reconciled into the subtree; only the latest intended tree is applied, older ones are skipped. A file that fails to parse mid-edit (an empty or truncated file is routine while editing) is logged as a warning, the running tree stays as it was, and nothing is written until a later read succeeds."],[4729,"**Fine-grained policy through interception**: for example, a filesystem dependency carrying metadata about readable and writable paths, checked by the provider. It is adjustable from the context without modifying the provider; it affects how a dependency is used, not whether it is satisfied, so it can change at runtime without a reload."],[5105,"**First CI release.** Bump and tag as above. When it has published, set each package's *Publishing access* to \"Require two-factor authentication and disallow tokens\", so only the trusted publisher (and maintainers with 2FA) can publish."],[7299,"**For the ideas:** Overview → The calculus → Implementation in the paper."],[7300,"**For the port:** Fibers and lifecycle → Paper vs. code → the Rust design."],[4938,"**Gap.** Both are static instruments over lexically fixed scopes. No fixed lexical scope delimits a plugin loaded after deployment, and no compile-time context anticipates dependencies arising from runtime configuration. The paper therefore *reifies* the structures, so that a runtime can operate on them and establish dynamically what these systems guarantee statically."],[5103,"**GitHub, environment.** In the repository's *Settings → Environments*, create `npm`. Optionally restrict its deployments to `js-v*` tags and add required reviewers: the publish job waits for them."],[842,"**GitHub，环境。** 在仓库的 *Settings → Environments* 中创建 `npm`。可以选择把它的部署限制为 `js-v*` 标签，并添加必需的审核人：发布任务会等待他们批准。"],[6151,"**Guest plugins** are separate modules that the `hmr` plugin can reload in place, unlike plugins compiled into the binary, whose code changes need a restart. In a config file loaded by the `kardia` binary, any entry name that is not a built-in plugin is a guest module path, relative to the config file:"],[6364,"**Handshake.** The host's first line offers version 2 as an export: `{\"export\":\"hello\",\"input\":{\"protocol\":\"kardia-guest/2\"}}`. A version 2 guest answers `{\"ready\":\"kardia-guest/2\"}`. A version 1 guest answers `{\"done\":1}`, as it does to any export it does not know, and the host serves it version 1, so either starts without a delay, and a version 2 guest still runs on a host that never offers it. A guest that does not answer within the handshake timeout is killed."],[6354,"**Host functions** (WASM imports from module `cordis` or `kardia`; for a dylib, function pointers in the `host` struct `{ host, read, write, log, provide, view, invoke }`, each taking `host.host` first). Pointers are guest addresses, lengths are byte counts:"],[7376,"**Hot-reload a plugin.** Edit the greeting in `examples/plugins/hello.wat`. The `hmr` entry reloads the WebAssembly plugin in place: the old instance logs its goodbye, then the new one logs your greeting."],[5299,"**Id-addressed documents instead of object identity**"],[2278,"**id** 在一棵树内唯一。没有 id 的条目会得到一个随机的八位十六进制 id。在嵌套的树之间，条目有一个**复合 id**：各层树所有者的 id 和它自己的 id 用 `:`（`kardia_loader::SEP`）连接，如 `include:hmr`；因此 `id` 不得包含 `:`。"],[5836,"**Identifiers:** a name reads the JSON value of the service with that name. The entry must declare that service in `inject`. Only services that have a JSON view can be read this way (see Writing plugins)."],[5608,"**Idiomatic Rust**: typed service keys, explicit caller attribution instead of `Proxy`, `Send + Sync` handles usable from a multi-threaded tokio runtime, no `unsafe` in the core."],[6539,"**Ids** are unique within a tree. Entries without one get a random eight-hex-digit id. Across nested trees an entry has a **composite id**, its tree owners' ids and its own joined by `:` (`kardia_loader::SEP`), such as `include:hmr`; an `id` must therefore not contain `:`."],[7263,"**Implementation**"],[4872,"**In kardia:** `ctx.effect(label, |scope| async { .. })` and `ctx.effect_sync(..)` return an `EffectHandle` registered on the current fiber's accumulator; `scope.adopt(handle)` moves a nested effect under an enclosing one. A `Disposer` wraps an `FnOnce`, so \"at most once\" is enforced by the type system. See Effects and API design."],[4456,"**In kardia:** `kardia_core::IdTable<T>` is this registry: `insert` returns a fresh, never-reused id, `remove` takes that id, and entries stay in insertion order. Service authors should build their registries (routes, listeners, commands) on it. See Services and API design."],[4736,"**In kardia:** `kardia-hmr` loads guest modules through three backends, each running a guest plugin through a bridge plugin that instantiates the guest once per fiber and drops the instance when the fiber is disposed. `WasmSource` runs core WebAssembly modules on Wasmtime (sandboxed, one store per fiber). `DylibSource` loads dynamic libraries but never unloads them (no `dlclose`): unloading Rust code is unsound once it has registered thread-local destructors or handed out `'static` references, so each version is loaded from a fresh copy of the file. `ProcessSource` runs one child process per fiber and kills it after `dispose`. See Guest plugins and Hot reload."],[4629,"**In kardia:** a failed fiber is in `FiberState::Failed` and keeps its error (`Fiber::error()`); only `update`, `restart` or `replace` recover it. See Lifecycle."],[4328,"**In kardia:** a fiber's target is `Target::Inactive` (`⊥`) or `Target::Epoch { revision, providers }`, the `ImplId`s of its providers in `inject` order; `ImplId` and `FiberId` are never reused. The committed view (`ω`) is a key → `ImplId` map fixed for the episode, and each binding keeps the set of fibers whose committed view names it (`relied_n`), which the guard waits on. In a plugin's `apply`, `ctx.checkpoint()` is an iteration boundary: it returns `Err(Interrupted)` once the load has been superseded or the fiber retired, which is L-Divert's abort alternative. See Lifecycle."],[4705,"**In kardia:** a key is the string `Service::NAME` bound to a Rust type through the `Service` trait. `ctx.provide(value)` is a tracked effect returning an `EffectHandle`, and providing a key twice in one realm fails with `KardiaError::AlreadyProvided`. `ctx.isolate(key)` (a fresh private realm), `ctx.isolate_in(key, realm)` (a shared realm) and `ctx.intercept(key, meta)` return a derived `Context`. Declared metadata comes from `Inject::with_meta`, and `Service::merge_intercept` merges it with the context's, outermost first, by default a right-biased shallow merge of JSON objects. See Services."],[4799,"**In kardia:** an `EffectHandle` does not dispose its effect on `Drop`; an effect lives until its fiber unloads or it is disposed explicitly, so a component's lifetime is never tied to a Rust scope. Inside an effect, ordinary `Drop` types still clean up local resources. See Effects and Lifecycle."],[4855,"**In kardia:** an effect body receives an `EffectScope`. `scope.defer(..)` collects an inverse without a boundary; `scope.yield_(disposer)` collects one and marks an iteration boundary, and `scope.checkpoint()` marks a boundary alone. Both return `Err(Interrupted)` once the effect has been disposed, so `?` ends the body at the boundary, keeping only the inverses collected so far. See Effects."],[4654,"**In kardia:** dependency cycles are reported when a fiber is inserted. The registry searches the declared `provide`/`inject` of live fibers for a cycle through the new fiber and logs a warning naming it (`dependency cycle: a -> b -> a`); the fiber stays `Pending`. Declared `provide` is metadata only, so a plugin that provides undeclared keys escapes the check. See Lifecycle."],[4753,"**In kardia:** keys are strings (`Service::NAME`) everywhere, because configuration names services. A binding holds its value as `dyn Any`, and a typed access downcasts it, failing with `AccessError::TypeMismatch`, which detects collisions between unrelated types within one binary. Guest modules do not share Rust types with the host: they provide and read services by string key, as JSON views with JSON calls, through the JSON guest ABI. That ABI carries no version tag. See Services and Guest plugins."],[4727,"**In kardia:** one key has one provider per realm (a second `ctx.provide` fails with `KardiaError::AlreadyProvided`). A broker is an ordinary service whose registry is an `IdTable`; a backing provider registers with it through an effect created on its own fiber (`svc.caller().effect(..)`), so the registration is withdrawn when that provider unloads. kardia has no separate broker service for guests: each guest fiber's `GuestService` is its own RPC endpoint, and its calls are synchronous rather than the asynchronous contract above, so a hung guest blocks its caller. See Services and Guest plugins."],[4573,"**In kardia:** Rust has no module registry, so `kardia-hmr` keeps its own `ModuleGraph`, loaded from a `ModuleSource` (WebAssembly, dynamic libraries or child processes), and replaces the plugins a changed module exports through `registry.replace`. Changed host modules are reported for a restart instead of being applied. A failed import aborts only its own unit (the plugins whose modules it shares), whose cache entries are restored, while the other units are applied. See Hot reload and Loader internals."],[4593,"**In kardia:** several of these theorems are property tests. `crates/kardia-core/tests/model.rs` runs random orchestration sequences of synthetic components (writes to a shared table, each with an exact inverse) under real tokio schedules with random delays. It checks ordering (Theorem 70) during every run, and preservation (Theorem 64), recovery exactness (Theorem 68 / Corollary 69) and confluence (the Active fibers are exactly the support set, Theorem 80) at quiescence. See Testing."],[4741,"**In kardia:** the `Service` trait binds a type to its key (`#[derive(Service)]`), and a service crate extends what a consumer can do with an extension trait on `Svc<S>` (for example `TimerExt` for `Svc<Timer>`), which coherence allows because the trait is local. Access is mediated at runtime by `ctx.get::<S>()` against the committed view, without a proxy. The `#[plugin]` macro supplies the compile-time half: a plugin function taking `Injected<(A, B)>` declares `A` and `B`, and accessing anything else through it does not compile. See Plugins, Services and API design."],[4568,"**In kardia:** the declarative loader is the `kardia-loader` crate (entries, groups, realms and a plugin `Catalog`), and file-backed include with two-way sync is `kardia-include`. See Loader and Loader internals."],[4743,"**In kardia:** the registry reports a cycle when a fiber is inserted: it searches the declared `provide`/`inject` of live fibers and logs a warning naming the cycle; the fiber stays `Pending`. See Lifecycle."],[4550,"**In kardia:** there is no proxy. `ctx.get::<S>()` performs Algorithm 6 against committed views and fails with `AccessError::Undeclared`, `AccessError::Inactive` or `AccessError::TypeMismatch`; `ctx.live::<S>()` is the reflective read of the live store, which never fails for an undeclared key. The compile-time check is there too: a `#[plugin]` function taking `Injected<(A, B)>` declares `A` and `B`, and `get::<S, _>()` on it does not compile for an undeclared `S`. See Services and Plugins."],[4543,"**In kardia:** transitions and asynchronous effect bodies are spawned as tokio tasks, so they progress without being polled by the caller, and they are never dropped half-way. All lifecycle bookkeeping happens in short critical sections under one state lock per root; no user code runs while the lock is held. See Concurrency."],[4627,"**In kardia:** transitions are inertial. An effect body or a plugin's `apply` is spawned and never dropped half-way; disposal waits for it to reach its end or an iteration boundary (`ctx.checkpoint()`, `scope.checkpoint()`, `scope.yield_(..)`), where it can stop with `Interrupted`. See Concurrency and Lifecycle."],[4682,"**In-place**: mutate the context and return a non-trivial inverse; recovery runs the inverse."],[7806,"**Inertia:** a stale target does not abort an in-flight `apply`. The load lands and the fiber unloads afterwards (async hosts take the *landing* alternative of L-Divert). The microtask yield before executing lets a burst of `update()` calls skip superseded loads entirely (`update.spec.ts: 'skips superseded loads before executing the plugin'`)."],[4745,"**interface drift**: the provider changes the interface behind `k` between versions;"],[8073,"**interpolate expressions** in `config` before validation (skipped for groups) in the inner fiber's context"],[5326,"**IO loop:** one task driven by `dirty_read/dirty_write` flags + `Notify`; latest-wins tree application; `flush()`."],[1065,"**IO 循环**：一个由 `dirty_read/dirty_write` 标志加 `Notify` 驱动的任务；树的应用以最新者为准；`flush()`。"],[7186,"**Isolation and interception:** `ctx.isolate(key, realm?)`, `ctx.intercept(key, meta)`, `ctx.interceptMeta(key)`."],[7533,"**Isolation per realm symbol** implements the relaxed calculus \"disjoint within a realm\" (§4.4, see Metatheory)."],[7255,"**kardia** rebuilds it in Rust. It is published on crates.io as `kardia` and nine `kardia-*` crates, with API docs on docs.rs. The source is on GitHub."],[2994,"**kardia** 用 Rust 重新构建了它。它以 `kardia` 和九个 `kardia-*` crate 的形式发布在 crates.io 上，API 文档见 docs.rs，源代码在 GitHub 上。"],[4746,"**key collision**: unrelated providers choose the same key name."],[4748,"**key namespacing** `K × P` (by package; eliminates collisions, couples to a registry);"],[5324,"**Key order:** options are `serde_json` maps, and `sort_keys` gives write-backs their stable order (`id`, `name`, the others alphabetically, `config` last) only with the `preserve-order` feature, which turns on `serde_json/preserve_order` and is on by default. Cargo unifies that feature into every `serde_json::Map` of a build, so it is optional: without it, maps and write-backs list their keys alphabetically. `kardia-include` and the `kardia` facade turn it on; `kardia-hmr` passes it through as a default feature, so an application that turns off `kardia-hmr`'s (and `kardia-loader`'s) default features keeps serde_json's default maps."],[7466,"**Key property:** the isolation and interception tables are *prototype chains*. A lookup (`table[name]`) sees the nearest override; `Object.hasOwn(table, name)` detects an isolation boundary introduced at exactly that level (used by `locate`)."],[4322,"**L-Divert** may fall between any two iterations; it routes into Unloading with the inverses accumulated so far (not through Active, which would let dependents activate against a leaving component). The *abort* alternative needs an iteration boundary; the *landing* alternative lets the in-flight iteration complete (needed for asynchronous hosts, §4.4)."],[56,"**L-Divert** 可以发生在任意两次迭代之间；它带着迄今为止累加的逆操作进入 Unloading（而不经过 Active，否则依赖者会针对一个即将离开的组件激活）。*中止*选项需要一个迭代边界；*落地*选项让正在进行的迭代完成（异步宿主需要它，§4.4）。"],[4323,"**L-Leave** records the decision only: the fiber stops providing (its table leaves `σ_γ`) while its own committed view and everybody else's stay intact."],[57,"**L-Leave** 只记录决定：纤程停止提供（其表离开 `σ_γ`），而它自己的已提交视图和其他所有纤程的已提交视图都保持不变。"],[4324,"**L-Unload** is the *only* rule that applies an accumulator; it discards the committed view last. Its premise `¬relied_n` is **the guard**: a provider's withdrawal waits until every consumer that resolved a key to it has gone."],[58,"**L-Unload** 是*唯一*应用累加器的规则；它最后才丢弃已提交视图。它的前提 `¬relied_n` 就是**守卫**：提供者的撤回要等到每个把某个键解析到它的消费者都离开之后。"],[4754,"**Languages:** make the context implicit again (for ergonomics, and to prevent a component from reaching another component's context through a closure or a global, which would leak effects out of its lifecycle); give the compiler syntax for effects (compile an effect iterator into one state machine holding the inverses in its frame instead of a closure per step); admit the coeffect specification into the type system (report cycles at compile time; structural dependency comparison à la row types)."],[4414,"**Lemma 32**: `≃_k` is an equivalence respected by all operations of `𝒜_k`, and the *coarsest* such relation (proof principle: exhibit any respected equivalence containing the pair)."],[4417,"**Lemma 35**: on maps and iterators `≃_S` is a partial equivalence."],[4419,"**Lemma 38**: all equalities of §3.1 hold with `=` replaced by `≃`."],[4420,"**Lemma 39**: a context-mediated iterator lies in `ℑ^S_Σ` for any `S` containing the keys its stages touch."],[4423,"**Lemma 41**: commutation is settled on generators; `⋄` does not enlarge the monoid."],[4331,"**Lemma 57**: its members are confined to `n` and witnessed at `≃_{d_n ∪ p_n}`."],[4595,"**Lemma 59 (lookups in Table 1):**"],[4601,"**Lemma 60 (≃-invariance)**: the rules cannot distinguish `≃`-related states. **Lemma 61 (equivariance)**: results hold up to renaming fiber names. **Lemma 62 (vestigial entries)**: a retired, Inactive, empty, childless entry is invisible to all rules."],[4605,"**Lemma 66**: every run is pairwise independent (supplied by witnessed coeffects and Theorem 47, see The context paradigm)."],[4606,"**Lemma 67 (entangled steps)**: while `n`'s episode is open, a provider `m` of `n` takes only identity state maps (the guard blocks its L-Unload); a consumer's steps commute with `g_n`; while `n` is Reloading, entangled fibers take only identity maps."],[4622,"**Lemma 78 (Transposition)** and **Lemma 79 (Deletion)**: adjacent independent steps can be swapped, and a closed episode (with its instantiations) can be deleted without changing the endpoint."],[7685,"**Level:** `exporter.levels[name] ?? exporter.levels.default ?? logger.level ?? INFO`; the levels are `ERROR=0, WARN=1, INFO=2, DEBUG=3`."],[7129,"**Level:** the `level` of the `logger` interception metadata, if any. `logger.with_level(level)` sets it on a copy."],[6362,"**Lifecycle of a module.** Loading a module instantiates it once to read its metadata (`meta`, then `dispose`); dependencies in `deps` are loaded first. Each fiber running the plugin then gets a fresh instance: `apply` with `{ config, imports }`, any number of `call`s, and `dispose` when the fiber is disposed, after which the instance is dropped. A non-zero status with no written output fails with `guest failed with status <n>`."],[7184,"**Lifecycle:** fibers move through `pending`, `loading`, `active`, `unloading`, `failed` and `disposed`, as in Rust. A plugin restarts when a dependency is replaced, waits when one leaves, and its provider keeps running until its consumers have cleaned up. `fiber.update(config)`, `restart()`, `ctx.onUpdate(...)` and `ctx.registry.replace(old, new)` (hot replacement, for Vite HMR) behave as in Rust."],[8157,"**Likely bug (verified in source):** in the realm GC listener (`config/isolate.ts:150-153`) the inner loop uses `return` when an entry still references the realm. That exits the whole listener and skips GC for the remaining names of the same `legacy.isolate`; `continue` (of the outer loop) was almost certainly intended. Effect: a stale global realm may survive until a later partial-dispose."],[4452,"**Limit:** binding every shared location at a key is a *discipline*, not a property of the construction. A location the system cannot reify as a coeffect lies outside the theorem (see the system boundary, §6.1, on Discussion and related work)."],[7247,"**Live changes:** you can reconfigure, replace or hot-reload any plugin while the app runs, and the rest of the app follows."],[4679,"**Local spatial composability**: a component activates only at a state satisfying its specification (it never reads an absent binding), and every context change is classified against the specification (loss of satisfaction is detected where it happens). Two things are left to the global form (§4.3.3, see Metatheory): withdrawing a binding only *after* the deactivations it causes have finished, and keeping the bindings an activation reads unmoved while it runs."],[5390,"**Logger:** `ctx.logger_named(\"greeter\")`, or `ctx.logger()`, which is named after the plugin."],[1922,"**macOS 上的陷阱处理**。在 macOS 上，wasmtime 默认通过 Mach 异常端口处理 WASM 陷阱。它的陷阱处理器是进程级的：wasmtime 在创建第一个引擎时安装它，之后的引擎若要求另一种设置，wasmtime 会 panic。`kardia::hmr::set_macos_mach_ports(false)` 让 kardia-hmr 创建的每个引擎改用 Unix 信号。请在创建第一个 `WasmSource` 或 `WasmGuest` 之前调用它：此后再要求另一种设置会返回错误，且不改变任何东西。应用自己用 wasmtime 创建的引擎必须使用相同的设置。在 macOS 以外的平台上，这个调用不改变任何东西。"],[5321,"**Managed realms:** the delimiter test is `Context::is_within(..)` on contexts whose entry tables are tagged `Overlay` nodes; the realm-GC fix is in (`collect_realms` uses `continue`)."],[4565,"**Managed realms.** `isolate: true` gives a *local* realm private to the entry, tagged by its id and carried along when the entry moves; `isolate: \"name\"` gives a *global* realm shared by every entry naming that string. A realm is discarded once no entry names it."],[5307,"**Managed realms**"],[6466,"**Match.** Changed modules are the loaded modules at or below the reported roots; host modules among them are only reported."],[7889,"**Match**: loaded modules whose path has a root as an ancestor (whole-segment match). Host modules and native addons → `skippedHostModules` (reported only)."],[7686,"**Messages:** `{ sn, ts, name, type, level, args, fiber?: WeakRef<Fiber> }`. Errors with a `cause` log the cause; non-empty `AggregateError`s are flattened."],[4740,"**Metaprogramming** supplies both together: *compile-time metaprogramming (for example **Rust procedural macros**, Scala macros, Zig comptime) emits, for each dependency, a typed declaration together with an accessor, dispensing with a general-purpose interception primitive.*"],[8154,"**migrate** a binding whose provider is inside the entry (tags equal) to the new symbol if it is free. The provider keeps the same `Impl` (same uid) and **does not restart**. If the target is occupied the move is *blocked*, and `Impl.isolate` keeps tracking where the binding really lives;"],[7684,"**Name resolution:** explicit argument → interception metadata `{ name }` → the hyphenated name of the *caller's* fiber (`fiber.name` walks up to the first named runtime, else `root`). Inside a service method the caller is the service's def site, so log lines are attributed to the service (`logger.spec.ts` regression tests)."],[7128,"**Name:** the `name` of the context's `logger` interception metadata if there is one; otherwise the plugin name of the fiber (or of its nearest named ancestor, else `root`), hyphenated (`fooBar` → `foo-bar`, `snake_case` → `snake-case`)."],[6353,"**Names.** Each export and dylib symbol may also be named `kardia_*` instead of `cordis_*` (`kardia_meta`, `kardia_new`, …). The host looks each one up as `kardia_*` first and falls back to `cordis_*`, so a guest may export either set, mix them, or export both: when both are present the host calls the `kardia_*` one. WASM host functions are offered under both import modules, `kardia` and `cordis`, and a module may import from either or both. Hosts up to kardia-hmr 0.2.0 know only `cordis_*` and `cordis`, so `kardia-guest` (like pykardia's exporter) exports every entry under both names and imports the host functions from `cordis`: its guests load on old and new hosts alike."],[4733,"**native code: explicit dynamic linking and unlinking** (`dlopen`/`dlclose`, `LoadLibrary`/`FreeLibrary`);"],[7534,"**No compile-time checking**: declared vs. accessed keys are checked only at runtime, by the proxy (paper §5.1.4 notes this could be static)."],[4617,"**No deadlock**: a non-quiescent state always admits some lifecycle rule (the chain of Unloading fibers blocked by relied-upon consumers is `≺`-increasing, hence finite, and ends at an unblocked one)."],[4441,"**No**"],[4536,"**Not checked:** the witness (that the inverse really reverts) and the coeffect commutativity witness. These are author and provider obligations."],[8296,"**not detected**: a dependency cycle leaves fibers PENDING silently; the paper (§6.5) says a runtime *can* report it at load time, but Cordis does not"],[6929,"**Notification follows the provider's state.** Consumers are notified at once only if the providing fiber is `Active`; otherwise they are notified when it becomes `Active`. When the provider leaves `Active`, its consumers are notified before any of its inverses run."],[5102,"**npmjs.com, first publish.** npm configures a trusted publisher in a package's settings, so each package must exist first. From a machine logged in with `npm login`: `cd js && bun install && bun run build`, then `npm publish --access public` in `packages/core`, `timer`, `bridge`, `tauri` and `vue`, in that order. This publishes the first version without provenance; later versions come from CI. A package added later, such as `@kardiajs/vue`, needs this step, and its own trusted publisher, before its first CI release."],[5101,"**npmjs.com, organization.** Create the free organization `kardiajs` (the `kardia` package name and the `@kardia` scope belong to others), and add the maintainers' accounts. Enable two-factor authentication on them."],[5104,"**npmjs.com, trusted publishers.** In each package's *Settings → Trusted publishing*, add a GitHub Actions publisher: organization or user `licyk`, repository `kardia`, workflow `npm-release.yml`, environment `npm`. The fields are case-sensitive and npm checks them only at publish time. A new trusted publisher must publish within two days, or it expires and has to be recreated, so release a version (step 5) right after."],[843,"**npmjs.com，可信发布者。** 在每个包的 *Settings → Trusted publishing* 中添加一个 GitHub Actions 发布者：组织或用户 `licyk`，仓库 `kardia`，工作流 `npm-release.yml`，环境 `npm`。这些字段区分大小写，npm 只在发布时检查它们。新建的可信发布者必须在两天内完成一次发布，否则会过期并需要重新创建，因此请紧接着发布一个版本（第 5 步）。"],[840,"**npmjs.com，组织。** 创建免费组织 `kardiajs`（`kardia` 包名和 `@kardia` 作用域属于他人），并加入维护者的账户。为这些账户启用双因素认证。"],[841,"**npmjs.com，首次发布。** npm 在包的设置中配置可信发布者，因此每个包必须先存在。在用 `npm login` 登录的机器上：`cd js && bun install && bun run build`，然后按顺序在 `packages/core`、`timer`、`bridge`、`tauri` 和 `vue` 中执行 `npm publish --access public`。这样发布的首个版本不带来源证明；之后的版本都由 CI 发布。之后新增的包（如 `@kardiajs/vue`）在首次 CI 发布之前，同样需要这一步和它自己的可信发布者。"],[6928,"**One binding per key and realm.** A second provider in the same realm fails with `KardiaError::AlreadyProvided`, whose message is `service \"database\" has been registered at <db>` (the name of the providing plugin)."],[4755,"**Operating systems:** make the declared coeffect specification the whole of what a component can reach (like WASM imports), provide isolation and interception natively, and provide OS resources (memory, file descriptors) as coeffects so that acquisitions are recorded once by the party that hands them out; transactional or copy-on-write storage can make some emissions revertible."],[4408,"**operation stage**: perform `a ∈ 𝒜_k` for `k ∈ S`, and choose the continuation by the outcome;"],[7368,"**Or install the binary from crates.io** and point it at your own config file:"],[5565,"**Ordering**"],[5339,"**Out-of-process plugins** (respawn = reload) via the service-broker/RPC pattern of paper §6.2."],[8268,"**Paper (Algorithm 5):** `unload` awaits the `notify(...)`'d dependents' `await()`."],[8262,"**Paper:** `fiber.target` is a hash of `target(γ, n)` (key → provider uid tuple), ⊥ when unsatisfied."],[8276,"**Paper:** `notify` iterates all fibers and calls `refresh`."],[8265,"**Paper:** O-Retire (set τ) and O-Remove (drop the entry) are separate rules; a retired entry may linger (vestigial)."],[8271,"**Paper:** the accumulator is a LIFO composite; Algorithm 5 runs `fiber.dispose()` once."],[8274,"**Paper:** the guard is checked before each iteration; L-Divert may abort or land."],[5327,"**Parsing:** a YAML parser with spans and custom tags (`saphyr` family): `!!js` → `Value::Expr`; errors **and** warnings fatal; JSON via `serde_json` plus a spanned pass for locations."],[7895,"**Partition into units** with union-find: two attempts join a unit if their **old ∪ new** closures share an evicted module (two plugins sharing a changed dependency must not end up with different instances of it)."],[5533,"**Paused time** (`start_paused = true`)"],[4749,"**peer dependencies** with semver ranges through the package manager (Cordis's current approach; relies on semver discipline and one version per package);"],[4570,"**Phase 1 – classification (Algorithm 8).** The inputs are `stashed` (the changed files) and `externals` (non-replaceable modules, whose change needs a full restart). A fixed point over `get_imports`: a pending module is *accepted* if one of its imports is accepted, and *declined* if all its imports are declined; leftovers (cycles) default to declined."],[4571,"**Phase 2 – stale-entry detection (Algorithm 9).** For each entry, collect the transitive imports of `entry.url`, stopping at declined modules; if the tree meets `accepted`, the entry is stale and its tree is folded into `accepted`."],[4572,"**Phase 3 – transactional reload (Algorithm 10).** Invalidate the caches of accepted modules (backing them up), re-import each stale entry and swap in a fresh fiber; on any error, restore the caches and rebuild every stale entry from the backup, then rethrow. The system never enters a half-reloaded state. (On Node.js both the ESM and the CJS caches are cleared.)"],[7181,"**Plugins** are functions, classes or objects with `apply`, each with optional `name`, `inject`, `provide` and `Config` (any Standard Schema validator). `apply` may return a promise, or a function that runs when the plugin stops."],[4996,"**Porting rule:** every synchronous segment of the TS code becomes **one critical section** on `State`. Nothing awaits while holding the lock, and **no user code is called while holding the lock** (plugin `apply`, disposers, event listeners, availability checks)."],[4672,"**Preconditions:** a dependency may not be provided twice (`k ∉ dom(σ)` for extension) nor revoked if absent (`k ∈ dom(σ)` for restriction). A violated precondition is *signalled as an error and produces no transition* (equivalently, compose in the `Maybe` monad)."],[5559,"**Preservation**"],[5571,"**Progress**"],[7266,"**Proposal**"],[7532,"**Provider identity** is the `Impl.uid`, a fresh counter value. This implements the \"name, not value\" discipline of the committed and target views."],[4409,"**provision stage**: `set(k, v)` for `k ∈ P` (a key no operation can create)."],[5325,"**Pure modules**, ported almost verbatim and unit-tested in isolation: `journal` (record, merge, flatten, apply, three-way `reconcile`; file wins), `patch` (insert/override patches, `PatchIndex` ownership, `route_journal`), anonymous id assignment."],[4898,"**Reactive coeffects** (§3.2): a component declares the keys it requires (a *specification*); every context change is classified against it as *activating*, *deactivating* or *neutral*, which drives activation and deactivation. This gives *local spatial composability*."],[6690,"**Read-only or missing files.** Changes are kept in memory, with a warning: `config file <path> is read-only, N pending change(s) kept in memory` (or `is missing`). A failed write logs `failed to write config file <path>, N pending change(s) kept in memory`."],[6713,"**Read, parse and validation errors** of a file are a `ConfigFileError { stage, path, cause, issues }`:"],[5537,"**Real time**"],[4552,"**Reconciliation** is incremental, justified by Theorem 80 (the endpoint is a function of the final config), Theorem 73 (it quiesces), Corollary 69 (rebuilding one entry leaves its neighbours untouched) and Theorem 70 (entries can be instantiated together, and a fiber waits at L-Begin, so **modules are loaded concurrently**). Changes are dispatched per field:"],[5562,"**Recovery exactness**"],[5377,"**Reentrancy:** critical sections queue `Action`s on the state (see Concurrency); values released under the lock are dropped after it."],[5378,"**Reference cycles:** there is no `Root` type or `shutdown()`. Disposing the root fiber, `root.fiber().dispose().await`, restarts it and reverts everything registered on it, which withdraws every binding."],[6877,"**Register the inverse right after acquiring a resource**, so that nothing leaks if the plugin is stopped while starting."],[6933,"**Removal is postponed during a drain.** While a provider is unloading, its withdrawn provisions stay reachable to its descendants until the drain ends, so they can use inherited services during their own cleanup."],[7573,"**removes it from the fiber's top-level list** (`this._disposables.delete(dispose)`), an ownership transfer (see below),"],[5568,"**Resolution coherence**"],[6519,"**Resolving names.** The loader turns an entry's `name` into a `PluginDef` through a `Resolver`, the analogue of a module import. Resolution may be asynchronous:"],[4897,"**Revertible effects** (§3.1): every context transformation is paired with an inverse that the runtime holds. Tracking and recovery are monoid homomorphisms, so the context is recovered upon removal, which gives *local temporal composability*."],[5384,"**Root:** `Context::new()` creates the root context; `root.fiber().dispose()` replaces `root.shutdown()`."],[7887,"**Roots**: `await callback()` → absolute paths (validated)."],[7202,"**Routes:** `addRoute(ctx, router, route)` adds a vue-router route as an effect: it is removed when the plugin stops."],[7367,"**Run it from a clone of the repository.**"],[7228,"**Running an app from a config file:** The configuration file, then Hot reload."],[4739,"**runtime level**: access must be dynamically mediated (a JavaScript `Proxy`, Python descriptors, or reflection at the cost of type safety)."],[7317,"**Rust 1.85 or newer.**"],[3056,"**Rust 1.85 或更新版本。**"],[7203,"**Rust-only extensions** cannot ship Vue code, but a Rust plugin can expose a value describing its UI (a settings schema, say) and a TypeScript plugin can register a generic component for it."],[4730,"**Sandboxing** untrusted code needs an execution boundary beyond the language (SFI, a separate runtime, a sandboxed process, a container); the untrusted component reaches host dependencies through a *bridge*, itself an ordinary fiber whose capabilities can be attenuated."],[4675,"**Satisfaction predicate**: `σ ⊧ d := ∀k ∈ d. k ∈ dom(σ)`, decidable because `dom(σ)` is finite."],[5309,"**Self-dispose / self-update write-back**"],[5322,"**Self-dispose:** `DisposeReason` was not introduced. The loader sets a per-entry `disposing` flag around its own `fiber.dispose()` call (`entry.rs`, `dispose_fiber`), the same pattern as the TS `_disposing` flag."],[5606,"**Semantic fidelity to the calculus** (paper §4): fibers, target vs. committed views, the guard on unload, inertia, failure outcomes, single source per (key, realm), confluence."],[7176,"**Service availability crosses.** A service the host exposes appears on the client exactly while it is exposed, so a client plugin that injects it runs exactly then, and restarts when it is exposed anew."],[4724,"**Service broker**: a central service is injected by both the backing providers and the consumers; providers *register with the broker* through revertible effects; consumers see no change when a backing provider changes."],[7246,"**Services:** plugins provide services and declare the services they depend on. A plugin starts once its dependencies are available, restarts when one is replaced, and stops when one goes away."],[7182,"**Services** are keyed by string. `ctx.get(key)` is checked access: it fails for a service the plugin did not declare. `ctx.live(key)` reads the live store without a check. A `Service` comes back as a view whose `caller` is the accessing context, Kardia's `Svc::caller`."],[5389,"**Settling:** `greeter.settled()` resolves as soon as no transition is in flight, so the example first waits for `db` to settle; the greeter's transitions start once the database is provided."],[5858,"**Shutting down** (Ctrl-C) does not write to the file."],[4890,"**Spatial composability**"],[4737,"**Spatial requirements:** a dependency-injection mechanism at two levels:"],[7894,"**Stage 1, import**, sequentially per stale plugin: re-import and check that the exports are a valid plugin (`registry.resolve`). *All fallible validation happens here, while only the module cache has been mutated*, so later stages need no rollback. No cache entry is restored before every plugin has been imported."],[6469,"**Stage 1: import.** The stale plugins' modules are evicted and every stale plugin is imported again. This is the only fallible step; validity is checked here, where only the module cache has changed, so the later stages need no rollback. Nothing is restored before every plugin has been imported, so no new module links against an evicted old one. Import errors are logged."],[7897,"**Stage 2, replace (synchronous)**: `ctx.registry.replace(oldPlugin, newPlugin)` per committed attempt. `replace` aliases the old plugin key to the new one (later `ctx.plugin(old)` instantiates the new code) and calls `fiber._replace(newRuntime, newInject)` on each fiber: re-check injections, clear errors, bump the revision ⇒ **the same fiber object unloads and reloads in place** (identity, parent, config and loader entry preserved)."],[6471,"**Stage 2: replace.** Each committed plugin is replaced in place through `registry.replace`, logged as `reload plugin at <module>`."],[7898,"**Stage 3, settle (concurrent)**: `await Promise.all(fibers.map(f => f.await().catch(noop)))`. There is **no rollback**: a plugin whose new `apply` throws stays FAILED (as on a cold start) and is retried on the next change."],[6472,"**Stage 3: settle.** The replaced fibers settle concurrently. There is no rollback: a plugin that fails to apply stays failed, as on a cold start."],[6468,"**Stale plugins.** Every registered plugin whose module closure reaches an accepted module is stale. A plugin exported by several modules (a module re-exporting it, for example) takes its replacement from the outermost exporter, the one no other exporter imports."],[7892,"**Stale plugins**: per runtime, the closure of its exporters through accepted modules. The module to re-import is the **outermost exporter** (which keeps the entry module's `inject`/`Config` metadata)."],[6688,"**Stale-content check.** Before every rename, it checks that the file still holds the content it last read. If someone else wrote the file meanwhile, it reads and merges first, then writes again."],[6673,"**Starting.** The include reads the file. If the file is missing and `initial` is set, it writes `initial` (with ids assigned) and reads that; without `initial` it fails with `config file not found: <path>`. Any other read, parse or validation failure fails the plugin, as does an unsupported extension (`extension \"toml\" not supported`). A file must be a top-level array of objects."],[7377,"**Stop the app.** Press Ctrl-C. Shutting down does not write to the config file."],[4750,"**structural compatibility** predicates (width subtyping is easy; behavioural contracts are hard; bounded quantification is undecidable)."],[7888,"**Sweep**: evict *failed* ModuleJobs from the cache (Node keeps them and rethrows on every import), per type slot."],[7565,"**Sync iterators are not interruptible** (there is no guard check); they could not be interrupted anyway in a single-threaded host. Every `collect` is type-checked (`safeCollect`)."],[6007,"**Synchronous:** `ctx.effect_sync(label, |scope| { … })` runs the body at once. If the body fails (or panics), whatever it collected is disposed and the error is returned."],[5829,"**Syntax:** a side-effect-free subset of JavaScript:"],[4887,"**Temporal composability**"],[4731,"**Temporal requirements:** closures (an inverse is a captured value), plus a way to introduce and retract a component's code at runtime:"],[4618,"**Termination**: each fiber takes at most `(K + 3)(V(n) + 1)` steps, where `V(n)`, the number of target turns, is finite."],[7318,"**The `wasm32-unknown-unknown` target**, only needed to build WebAssembly guest plugins, or to run the full test suite:"],[4899,"**The context paradigm** (§3.3): the effect context and the coeffect context are unified into one context type `Γ∞`, and *every* effect and coeffect is mediated through it. This induces an **observational equivalence `≃`** under which the effects of distinct components become **independent** (§3.4)."],[7864,"**The implementation differs substantially from the paper's Algorithm 10** (see Paper vs. code)."],[4841,"**Theorem 10**: `(𝔈Γ, ⋄)` is a monoid with unit `η(γ) = (γ, id)`; `(f,g) ↦ γ ↦ (f(γ), g)` is a homomorphism `𝔗Γ → 𝔈Γ`."],[4842,"**Theorem 11**: `𝔈Γ*` is a submonoid (witnessing survives composition), and uniform inverses land in it."],[4844,"**Theorem 13**: `effect(f) ⋄ effect(g) = effect(f ⋄ g)`."],[4845,"**Theorem 14**: projections commute: the lifted forward and inverse maps act on the state exactly as `f` and `g`."],[4846,"**Theorem 15**: for a witnessed `e`: `g′(Δ) = (γ, φ ∘ g ∘ f)`. The *state* is recovered exactly; the *accumulator* is restored if and only if `g ∘ f = id`; in every case `(φ ∘ g ∘ f)(γ) = φ(γ)`, so the soundness invariant is preserved. Hence `effect` does **not** carry `𝔈Γ*` into `𝔈*∂Γ` in general, but reverting never moves the recovery target."],[4848,"**Theorem 16**: applying `e₁…eₙ ∈ 𝔈Γ*` from `(γ₀, id)` and reverting in **reverse order**, every revert recovers the state its application ran against, and every intermediate state satisfies the soundness invariant. LIFO needs nothing more."],[4829,"**Theorem 4**: tracking leaves the forward behaviour untouched: `pr₁ ∘ track(f,g) = f ∘ pr₁`."],[4427,"**Theorem 43**: for pairwise independent `e₁…eₙ`, applying the yielded inverses **in any permutation** reaches `γ₀`. Each inverse withdraws its own contribution and nothing else, whatever the order."],[4429,"**Theorem 45**: operations at **distinct keys** are always independent (key-local maps commute)."],[4450,"**Theorem 47**: two context-mediated iterators with `P₁ ∩ S₂ = P₂ ∩ S₁ = ∅` (neither provides a key the other touches) and commutative shared keys are independent. With every coeffect witnessed, only that disjointness remains to check, and §4 (the calculus) reads it off the declarations."],[4830,"**Theorem 5**: `track` is a monoid homomorphism `𝔗Γ → (∂Γ → ∂Γ)`: tracking pairs one at a time equals tracking their twisted composite."],[4603,"**Theorem 64**: every rule preserves well-formedness. The guard on L-Unload is what carries clauses (3) and (4): no committed view ever names a removed fiber. Consequences: a name freed by O-Remove may be reissued (there are no stale views), and a fiber can be removed as soon as it is Inactive without a separate dependency check."],[4607,"**Theorem 68 (Recovery exactness)**: applying `n`'s accumulator at any point of its episode leaves every table where the *other* fibers' steps alone would have left it from the episode start:"],[4832,"**Theorem 7**: for `g(f(γ)) = γ`: `recover(track(f,g)(γ,φ)) = recover(γ,φ)`. A tracked step whose inverse reverts it does not move the recovery target. The **soundness invariant** of a state is `φ(γ) = γ₀`; every state reached from `(γ₀, id)` by such steps satisfies it, and `recover` carries it back to `(γ₀, id)`."],[4611,"**Theorem 70 (Ordering)**"],[4614,"**Theorem 71 (Resolution coherence)**: every iteration of a transition runs against the one committed resolution `ω`. When the fiber leaves Reloading, either L-Finish lands it Active against `ω`, or L-Divert takes it out and its episode closes with exact recovery. A transition never straddles two resolutions of its coeffects (no glitch *within* a transition; Cordis has no global \"turn\" as FRP has)."],[4616,"**Theorem 73 (Progress)**: assume `≺` is acyclic, iterator length is at most `K`, and there are finitely many names. Then:"],[4623,"**Theorem 80 (Confluence)**: any run reaching a quiescent state can be reduced to a **canonical** run: the same orchestration steps, then one episode per supported fiber in an order linearising support. Two runs with the same orchestration inputs reach `≃`-related states (up to renaming). *The lifecycle relation has unique normal forms.*"],[7260,"**Theory**"],[4577,"**Threats to validity:** a single ecosystem, a single language, observational evidence; measuring overhead and productivity is future work."],[6689,"**Transient failures.** A rename that fails with `PermissionDenied` or `ResourceBusy` (such as a virus scanner holding the file) is retried up to 10 times, waiting 20 ms longer each time."],[6183,"**Trap handling on macOS**. wasmtime handles WASM traps on macOS through Mach exception ports by default. Its trap handler is process-wide: wasmtime installs it with the first engine, and panics when a later engine asks for the other setting. `kardia::hmr::set_macos_mach_ports(false)` has every engine kardia-hmr makes use Unix signals instead. Call it before the first `WasmSource` or `WasmGuest` is made: after that, asking for the other setting returns an error and changes nothing. An engine the application makes with wasmtime itself must use the same setting. Elsewhere than macOS the call changes nothing."],[6675,"**Tree changes → file.** Runtime changes of the subtree (API edits, plugin self-updates and self-disposals) are recorded in a journal and written back to whoever owns them: the file, or a patch in the include's own configuration, which is persisted through the include's own entry in the parent tree. Shutting down does not write to the file."],[6541,"**Two fibers per entry with `inject`.** An entry that declares `inject` runs an outer fiber (tagged `loader:outer`, `kardia_loader::OUTER_TAG`) that holds the dependencies, resolves the plugin, passes a `ctx.checkpoint()?`, and then starts the inner fiber that runs the plugin. Without `inject`, the entry has only the inner fiber."],[5303,"**Two fibers per entry with `inject`**"],[4738,"**type level**: a well-typed dependency access; the context type must record each key's coeffect. *Typeclasses (Haskell) and **traits (Rust)** let a provider extend the context type from its own module through an instance/`impl`*; TypeScript uses module augmentation."],[5381,"**Type-level keys:** the in-process check is the downcast at access (`AccessError::TypeMismatch`). Guest services cross the module boundary as JSON values with JSON calls (`GuestService`), so no Rust type or `TypeId` crosses it."],[6540,"**Typed view.** `EntryOptions::read(&options)` reads validated options into a typed view (`id`, `name`, `config`, `group`, `disabled: Option<Disabled>` with `Disabled::{Bool, Expr}`, `inject`, `intercept`, `isolate: Vec<(String, IsolateLabel)>` with `IsolateLabel::{Private, Shared(label)}`); the JSON object stays the source of truth."],[6470,"**Units.** Plugins whose closures (in the old or the new graph) share an evicted module form a **unit** that commits or aborts together. A unit with a failed import is aborted: nothing in it is applied, and its modules' cache entries are restored; the other units are not affected."],[8325,"**use site**"],[5313,"**Validation**"],[6365,"**Version 1:**"],[4893,"**VSCode**: extensions cannot be unloaded individually (87 of the top 100 contain code and require an extension-host restart); `deactivate` is only a shutdown hook and separates disposal from creation. `extensionDependencies` is barely used (7 of the top 100), and inter-extension APIs are untyped (`exports: any`)."],[632,"**VSCode**：扩展无法单独卸载（排名前 100 的扩展中有 87 个包含代码，需要重启扩展宿主）；`deactivate` 只是一个关闭钩子，把释放与创建割裂开来。`extensionDependencies` 几乎没人使用（前 100 中只有 7 个），扩展间的 API 是无类型的（`exports: any`）。"],[5337,"**WASM components (wasmtime):** old and new instances coexist safely, dropping is sound, natural sandbox (paper §6.3 bridge fibers). Cost: services cross a WIT boundary."],[1076,"**WASM 组件（wasmtime）**：新旧实例可以安全共存，丢弃是可靠的，天然沙箱（论文 §6.3 的桥接纤程）。代价：服务需要跨越 WIT 边界。"],[6180,"**WebAssembly.** `WasmSource` runs core WebAssembly modules on wasmtime rather than WIT components, so guests need no component toolchain (the tests are written in WAT). A module compiles once per version and instantiates in its own store per fiber. `WasmSource::with_limits` bounds each instance:"],[1919,"**WebAssembly。** `WasmSource` 在 wasmtime 上运行核心 WebAssembly 模块，而不是 WIT 组件，因此访客不需要组件工具链（测试用 WAT 编写）。模块每个版本编译一次，并为每个纤程在各自的 store 中实例化。`WasmSource::with_limits` 为每个实例设置上限："],[4734,"**WebAssembly**: an instance is released when a native embedder (for example **Wasmtime**) drops it."],[472,"**WebAssembly**：当原生嵌入者（例如 **Wasmtime**）丢弃实例时，该实例被释放。"],[6050,"**When a fiber unloads**, the runtime:"],[6542,"**When an entry runs.** A literal `disabled: true` or a disabled ancestor group blocks the entry. A `disabled` expression is evaluated in the outer fiber's context (which sees the entry's `inject`); if it fails, the entry is disabled and the failure reported. The entry's `intercept` is evaluated next; a plugin does not run with an `intercept` that cannot be evaluated. Expressions in `config` are interpolated in the plugin's context on every load, while the source keeps the expressions; a group's `config` is its entry list and is not interpolated."],[6930,"**Withdrawal waits for consumers.** Reverting the provision removes the binding and notifies the realm, then waits until every consumer that committed to this binding has finished its own cleanup, and only then removes the provision."],[4721,"**Withholding and compensation.** Recovering an emission requires either withholding it until the producing state is certain (the output-commit problem) or compensation (delete the created file, refund the charge) up to an application-supplied, coarser equivalence. Compensations compose LIFO like inverses, but the commutation metatheory (Metatheory) must be re-established against the coarser relation."],[6046,"**Within one effect** (an `effect_sync` body, an `effect` body, or the inverses a scope adopted), inverses run **sequentially, newest first**:"],[6616,"**Write-back.** Changes a plugin makes to itself reach its entry:"],[7229,"**Writing plugins compiled into your app:** Writing plugins, Services and Effects."],[7231,"**Writing plugins that reload without restarting the app:** Guest plugins."],[4435,"**Yes**"],[3270,"**一切都在根上。** 每个根只有一个 `store`、一个 `props` 和一个 `registry`；派生上下文之间的区别只在于原型链上的 `isolate`/`intercept` 表及其 `fiber`。这让“键 k 是否在领域 r 中被提供？”保持为一次映射查找。"],[1925,"**三者的共同点。** `GuestService::call` 会阻塞调用者直到访客应答；`call_async` 则在异步工作线程之外执行调用，桥接插件执行 `apply` 和 `dispose` 时也是如此。截止时间可以终止进程访客（将其杀死）和设置了时间上限的 WASM 访客（触发陷阱）；dylib 访客运行在调用者的线程上，无法被终止。没有单独的代理（broker）服务：每个纤程的 `GuestService` 就是 RPC 端点。这些后端是 `kardia-hmr` 的 cargo 特性（`wasm`、`dylib`、`process`，默认全部开启）；另有 `preserve-order`（默认开启），它通过 `kardia-loader` 开启 `serde_json/preserve_order`，关闭它可让应用保留 serde_json 的默认映射（键顺序）。"],[638,"**上下文范式**（§3.3）：效应上下文与余效应上下文被统一为一个上下文类型 `Γ∞`，*所有*效应与余效应都经由它中介。这诱导出一个**观察等价 `≃`**，在它之下，不同组件的效应变得**独立**（§3.4）。"],[271,"**不检查**：见证（逆操作确实能撤销）和余效应交换性的见证。这些是作者和提供者的义务。"],[4035,"**不检测**：依赖环会让纤程静默地停留在 PENDING；论文（§6.5）说运行时*可以*在加载时报告它，但 Cordis 没有这样做"],[3635,"**中止/提交**：存在任何导入失败的单元被中止，其模块被恢复。孤立的被逐出模块随与之重叠的中止单元一起恢复（除非它们能到达某个已提交单元）。与已恢复模块链接的第 1 阶段加载模块会被逐出。"],[3038,"**了解思想**：概述 → 演算 → 论文中的实现。"],[3039,"**了解移植**：纤程与生命周期 → 论文与代码 → Rust 设计。"],[2917,"**事件**从宿主发往每个客户端，以名称区分。"],[2924,"**事件**以名称区分：`ctx.on`、`emit`、`bail`、`serial`、`parallel`。运行时会报告 `internal/plugin-inserted`、`internal/plugin-removed`、`internal/status`、`internal/service`、`internal/commit` 和 `internal/replace`。"],[4002,"**代码：** `_runner.epoch` = `\"<revision>:<uid>:<uid>…\"` 或 `'__INACTIVE__'`。**修订**计数器把配置修订折叠进目标：`restart()`、`update()` 与 `registry.replace()` 会递增它，从而在不使纤程（fiber）退役的情况下强制一条卸载→重新加载链。这比“退役 → 移除 → 以同一名称重新插入”更廉价地实现了 §4.4 *Configuration* 的修订。"],[4014,"**代码：** 只有**异步**迭代器可中断；同步迭代器与普通函数运行至结束（在单线程宿主中它们本来也无法被中断）。异步迭代器采取*落地*分支（惯性宿主），并以 `iter.return()` 关闭，使 `finally` 块得以运行。`_reload` 在执行前还会让出一个微任务，因此被取代的加载永远不会开始。"],[4005,"**代码：** 实例化效应的逆操作设置 `uid = null`（立即从 runtime 中移除），把目标强制为 ⊥，然后等待转换链；最终状态为 `DISPOSED`。不存在持久的退役条目注册表。重新启用一个条目会创建一个**全新的纤程**（如论文所规定）。"],[4008,"**代码：** 显式的反向引用 `Impl.dependents: Set<Fiber>`，在提交时填充，在依赖方卸载结束时移除，外加唤醒用的 resolver（`impl.release`、`fiber._release`）。存在两层守卫：**纤程级**守卫（在提供者的*所有*提供项都空闲之前，它的任何撤销函数都不运行）与 `provide` 逆操作内部的**绑定级**守卫。这给出了论文按绑定的语义（`relied_n`），同时允许提供者撤回一个绑定而无需等待另一个。"],[4011,"**代码：** 纤程级撤销函数按逆序*发起*，但**并发**运行（`Promise.all`），每个都在一个微任务之后开始；错误被记录，且不会阻止其他撤销函数。顺序 LIFO 只在*单个* `ctx.effect` 内部成立。论文承认了这种并发（§5.1.3），定理 43（独立的逆操作可交换）为其提供了依据，但这意味着对顺序敏感的拆除必须组合进同一个效应。"],[4016,"**代码：** 遍历所有 runtime 的纤程，按声明的键与**领域符号**（或在领域迁移期间按自定义过滤器）筛选，只重新计算受影响的键（`_checkImpl`），然后调用 `_refresh`。它还会发出 `internal/service`。纤程提供项的通知只在进入或离开 `ACTIVE` 的转换上由 `_updateState` 发出。"],[2757,"**代表调用者创建效应。** 为调用者创建效应的服务方法把效应登记在 `svc.caller()` 上。这样效应属于调用者的纤程，在*调用者*卸载时撤销，这正是 Cordis 的追踪器借助 `this.ctx` 达到的效果。服务 crate 把这类方法实现为 **`Svc<S>` 上的扩展 trait**；由于 trait 是本地定义的，一致性规则允许这样做。计时器服务就是这样做的（已简化：实际的 `timeout` 在触发后还会撤销自己的效应）："],[1038,"**以 id 寻址的文档代替对象同一性**"],[457,"**余效应（coeffect）移动边界**：它把一个外部位置具体化到一组各自带有逆操作的操作之后。边界是*按位置*划定的，而不是按介质（私有的临时文件在内部；共享路径在外部）。"],[676,"**余效应**。判断形式 `Γ @ coeffect ⊢ t : T` 标注的是*上下文*。余单子 `(D, ε, δ)`（Uustalu 与 Vene）为依赖上下文的计算提供结构；Petricek 等人提出把余效应作为一种统一的静态分析；分级余效应使用预序半环来量化使用情况。"],[4064,"**使用点**（use site）"],[4083,"**使用点**上下文"],[1130,"**依赖**：`#[derive(Deserialize)]` 需要在 crate 自身的依赖中加入启用 `derive` 特性的 `serde`，即使 `kardia::prelude` 重新导出了该 derive。"],[2693,"**依赖环。** 插入纤程时，运行时检查其所在领域中各现存纤程声明的 `provide` 与 `inject` 集合是否经由它构成环。若构成环，运行时会记录一条指明该环的警告（`dependency cycle: a -> b -> a`），纤程停留在 `Pending`，而不是无声地等待。"],[1298,"**保持性**"],[3114,"**修改配置**。在 `examples/kardia.yml` 中，把 `console` 条目的 `disabled` 设为 `false`：控制台日志随即启动。改回 `true`，它就停止。"],[3116,"**停止应用**。按 Ctrl-C。关闭应用不会写入配置文件。"],[478,"**元编程**同时提供两者：*编译期元编程（例如 **Rust 过程宏**、Scala 宏、Zig comptime）为每个依赖生成一个带类型的声明以及一个访问器，从而无需通用的拦截原语。*"],[3131,"**共同主题：** 每个资源都通过*调用方*纤程（fiber）上的 `ctx.effect` 注册（经服务 tracker 找到调用方，见服务与可追溯性），因此在调用方卸载时被释放。服务中没有针对每个消费者的簿记。"],[536,"**关于 RAII 的 \\[Rust] 说明**：论文明确把 Rust 的所有权/RAII 定位为*静态作用域*的撤销：它是互补的，而不是替代品。因此 Rust 移植*不应*试图把组件的生命周期做成一个词法作用域；组件的生命周期是动态的，由纤程状态机管理，而 `Drop` 仍适用于单个效应内部的局部资源。"],[2650,"**关联服务。** Cordis 的 `foo.bar` 关联服务和 `ctx.mixin` 是 JavaScript 对象层面的便利功能。在 kardia 中，名为 `foo.bar` 的服务只是另一个键。要\"扩展\"另一个插件的类型，可以用扩展 trait（编译期，见 `Svc<T>` 与调用者），或用基于 `kardia_core::IdTable` 的注册表（registry）服务（运行期）。访问器或 mixin 层没有移植。"],[3205,"**关键性质：** 隔离（isolation）表与拦截表都是*原型链*。查找（`table[name]`）看到最近的覆盖；`Object.hasOwn(table, name)` 检测恰好在这一层引入的隔离边界（`locate` 使用了这一点）。"],[1597,"**关闭应用**（Ctrl-C）不会写入文件。"],[2430,"**冲突：以文件为准。** 运行时变化尚未写出时文件发生了变化，include 会做三方合并。冲突的运行时变化被丢弃，使树跟随文件，每次丢弃都记录为 `config conflict in <path>: entry <id> <reason>; file wins`，原因是以下之一："],[1596,"**冲突**：文件和应用同时修改时，以文件为准。"],[2939,"**出错的贡献**会被隔离：抛出异常的贡献（在 setup、渲染、钩子、侦听器或事件处理函数中）会被 `error` 插槽（`{ error, item, owner, retry }`）取代，没有该插槽时不渲染任何内容；其他贡献照常渲染，错误也不会传到应用。`retry()` 重新挂载它。`@error`（`{ error, item, owner }`）报告这次失败，例如用于显示是哪个插件出错；没有它时，失败由所属插件的日志器记录。所属插件继续运行：出错的视图只是该插件的一个贡献，停止插件还会移除它的服务和其他贡献。要停止它，可在 `@error` 中调用 `owner.fiber.dispose()`。"],[3629,"**分析（Analyze）**：反向边（不含来自宿主模块的边）。`accepted` = 变化的模块加上所有传递地导入它们的模块；`declined` = 宿主 ∪ 其余。*（论文的算法 8 是在正向导入上求不动点，环默认为 declined；代码则是更简单的反向可达工作表。）*"],[2276,"**分组**（group）是带 `group: true`、运行 `group` 插件的条目。它的 `config` 是一个条目列表，分组在每次更新时原地调和这个列表而不是重启：条目按 id 并发地创建、更新和移除，一个坏条目不会阻止其他条目。分组本身从不被禁用；它的 `disabled` 判定会传给其成员。"],[408,"**前置条件**：一个依赖不能被提供两次（扩展要求 `k ∉ dom(σ)`），也不能在不存在时被撤销（限制要求 `k ∈ dom(σ)`）。违反前置条件*会报告为错误，且不产生任何状态转移*（等价地，在 `Maybe` 单子中组合）。"],[2971,"**加入 TypeScript 一侧，例如 Tauri webview**：TypeScript 与 Tauri。"],[2255,"**加载器**（loader，`kardia-loader`）维护一棵由**条目**（entry，即插件名加上其配置）组成的树，并让它与运行中的纤程（fiber）双向保持一致：对条目的修改会被调和到运行中的纤程，插件自行更新或释放（dispose）时也会被回写到它的条目。**include**（配置文件引入）插件（`kardia-include`）把 YAML 或 JSON 文件中的条目嫁接到这棵树上，并让文件双向保持同步。"],[1119,"**动态代码**：先实现了静态目录；随后实现了 WASM、dylib 与进程后端（见动态模块）。"],[1923,"**动态库。** `DylibSource` 使用 C ABI，而不是传递 Rust 类型：`cdylib` 自带一份 `kardia-core` 和 tokio，静态变量各自独立，也没有运行时上下文。每次加载都会把库复制到一个新路径（位于临时目录下的 `kardia-dylib-<pid>` 目录中），因为平台加载器对已知路径会直接交出已加载的那个库。库永不卸载：一旦 Rust 代码注册了线程局部析构函数或交出了 `'static` 引用，卸载它就是不健全的。"],[639,"**动态组合演算**（§4）：组件是一个三元组 `(d, p, e)`（依赖、提供、效应迭代器）；它的实例是**纤程**（fiber）；九条规则（3 条编排规则、6 条生命周期规则）让纤程经历 `Inactive → Reloading → Active → Unloading`。元理论证明了保持性、恢复精确性、顺序性、解析一致性、进展性（无死锁且终止）以及**合流性**（静止状态等于从零开始静态加载最终配置所得的状态）。"],[2205,"**匹配。** 发生变化的模块是位于所报告的根或其下方的已加载模块；其中的宿主模块只做报告。"],[3628,"**匹配（Match）**：路径以某个根为祖先的已加载模块（按完整路径段匹配）。宿主模块与原生扩展 → `skippedHostModules`（仅报告）。"],[2415,"**匿名条目。** 文件中没有 id 的条目会在加载器看到它们之前得到 id，id 也会被回写。与上次读取中某个条目完全相同的匿名条目会保留那个 id（除非文件现在显式命名了它），所以编辑相邻条目不会让它重启。"],[288,"**协调**是增量的，其合理性来自：定理 80（终点是最终配置的函数）、定理 73（它会静止）、推论 69（重建一个条目不影响其邻居）以及定理 70（条目可以一起实例化，纤程会在 L-Begin 处等待，因此**模块是并发加载的**）。变更按字段分派："],[2209,"**单元。** 闭包（在旧图或新图中）共享某个被驱逐模块的插件组成一个**单元**，一起提交或一起放弃。含导入失败的单元被放弃：其中任何内容都不会应用，其模块的缓存条目会被恢复；其他单元不受影响。"],[418,"**原地**（in-place）：修改上下文并返回一个非平凡的逆操作；恢复时运行该逆操作。"],[3891,"**原地**重新挂接并替换表（为后代保持身份）；"],[2426,"**原子写入。** include 在同一目录中写一个临时文件（`.<name>.<pid>.<seq>.tmp`），再把它重命名覆盖原文件，因此读者永远不会看到被截断的文件。"],[1067,"**原子写入**：在同一目录中写临时文件，每次重命名前检查内容是否已过期，遇到 `PermissionDenied`/`ResourceBusy` 时进行有限次数的重试，只读时 → 把 journal 保留在内存中。"],[471,"**原生代码：显式的动态链接与卸载**（`dlopen`/`dlclose`、`LoadLibrary`/`FreeLibrary`）；"],[1334,"**参考实现**：Cordis 参考一节（TypeScript，Cordis v4）。"],[3630,"**发现（Discover）**：对 accepted 模块解包其导出，保留其中已注册的插件；**按 runtime 分组**（多个模块可以导出同一个插件）。"],[2715,"**受检访问**（论文的算法 6）按如下方式解析一个键："],[2942,"**只有 Rust 部分的扩展**无法携带 Vue 代码，但 Rust 插件可以暴露一个描述其界面的值（例如设置 schema），再由 TypeScript 插件为它注册一个通用组件。"],[2429,"**只读或缺失的文件。** 变化保留在内存中，并给出警告：`config file <path> is read-only, N pending change(s) kept in memory`（或 `is missing`）。写入失败时记录 `failed to write config file <path>, N pending change(s) kept in memory`。"],[636,"**可撤销效应**（§3.1）：每一次上下文变换都与一个由运行时持有的逆操作配对。追踪和恢复都是幺半群同态，因此组件被移除时上下文得以恢复，从而带来*局部时间可组合性*。"],[3896,"**可能的缺陷（已在源码中核实）：** 在领域回收监听器中（`config/isolate.ts:150-153`），当某个条目仍引用该领域时，内层循环使用了 `return`。这会退出整个监听器，跳过同一 `legacy.isolate` 中其余名称的回收；本意几乎可以肯定是（外层循环的）`continue`。后果：一个过时的全局领域可能一直存活到之后的某次 partial-dispose。"],[1313,"**合流性**"],[1746,"**同步：** `ctx.effect_sync(label, |scope| { … })` 立即运行效应体。若效应体失败（或 panic），它已收集的一切都会被释放，并返回该错误。"],[3304,"**同步迭代器不可中断**（没有守卫检查）；在单线程宿主中它们本来也无法被中断。每次 `collect` 都会做类型检查（`safeCollect`）。"],[2867,"**名称：** 若上下文有 `logger` 拦截元数据，取其中的 `name`；否则取该纤程（或其最近的有名祖先，都没有则为 `root`）的插件名，并连字符化（`fooBar` → `foo-bar`，`snake_case` → `snake-case`）。"],[2092,"**名称。** 每个导出和 dylib 符号也可以用 `kardia_*` 代替 `cordis_*` 命名（`kardia_meta`、`kardia_new` 等）。宿主对每一项都先查找 `kardia_*`，找不到时再查找 `cordis_*`，因此访客可以只导出其中一套、混用两套，或两套都导出：两者都存在时，宿主调用 `kardia_*` 的那个。WASM 宿主函数同时在 `kardia` 和 `cordis` 两个导入模块下提供，一个模块可以从其中任意一个或两个导入。kardia-hmr 0.2.0 及更早的宿主只认识 `cordis_*` 和 `cordis`，因此 `kardia-guest`（以及 pykardia 的导出工具）会以两套名称导出每一项，并从 `cordis` 导入宿主函数：这样构建的访客在新旧宿主上都能加载。"],[3423,"**名称解析：** 显式参数 → 拦截元数据 `{ name }` → *调用方*纤程的连字符化名称（`fiber.name` 向上找到第一个有名称的 runtime，否则为 `root`）。在服务方法内部，调用方是该服务的定义点，因此日志行归属于该服务（`logger.spec.ts` 回归测试）。"],[175,"**否**"],[2412,"**启动。** include 读取文件。若文件不存在且设置了 `initial`，它写入 `initial`（并分配 id）后再读取；没有 `initial` 时以 `config file not found: <path>` 失败。其他任何读取、解析或校验失败都会使插件失败，不支持的扩展名同样如此（`extension \"toml\" not supported`）。文件必须是由对象组成的顶层数组。"],[3774,"**启动**（`core/bin.js`）：创建根 `Context`，把 `baseUrl` 设为当前工作目录，`await ctx.plugin(Loader)`，然后执行 `ctx.loader.create({ name: '@cordisjs/plugin-include', config: { path: './cordis.yml' } })`。"],[637,"**响应式余效应**（§3.2）：组件声明它所需要的键（一份*规约*）；每一次上下文变化都依据规约被分类为*激活*、*停用*或*中性*，由此驱动激活与停用。这带来*局部空间可组合性*。"],[2355,"**回写。** 插件对自身的修改会到达它的条目："],[2969,"**围绕加载器构建自己的宿主（host）**：加载器。"],[611,"**在 kardia 中**：`ctx.effect(label, |scope| async { .. })` 与 `ctx.effect_sync(..)` 返回一个 `EffectHandle`，注册在当前纤程（fiber）的累加器中；`scope.adopt(handle)` 把一个嵌套效应移到外层效应之下。`Disposer` 包装一个 `FnOnce`，因此“至多一次”由类型系统保证。见效应与 API 设计。"],[537,"**在 kardia 中**：`EffectHandle` 在 `Drop` 时不会释放其效应；效应一直存在，直到其纤程卸载或它被显式释放，因此组件的生命周期从不绑定到某个 Rust 作用域。在效应内部，普通的 `Drop` 类型仍会清理局部资源。见效应与生命周期。"],[190,"**在 kardia 中**：`kardia_core::IdTable<T>` 就是这种注册表：`insert` 返回一个新的、永不复用的 id，`remove` 接收这个 id，条目保持插入顺序。服务作者应当在它之上构建自己的注册表（路由、监听器、命令）。见服务与 API 设计。"],[474,"**在 kardia 中**：`kardia-hmr` 通过三种后端加载访客模块，每种后端都通过一个桥插件运行访客插件：桥插件为每个纤程实例化一次访客，并在纤程被释放时丢弃该实例。`WasmSource` 在 Wasmtime 上运行核心 WebAssembly 模块（沙箱化，每个纤程一个 store）。`DylibSource` 加载动态库但从不卸载它们（不调用 `dlclose`）：一旦 Rust 代码注册了线程局部析构函数或交出了 `'static` 引用，卸载它就是不健全的，因此每个版本都从文件的一份新副本加载。`ProcessSource` 为每个纤程运行一个子进程，并在 `dispose` 之后将其终止。见访客插件与热重载。"],[479,"**在 kardia 中**：`Service` trait 把一个类型绑定到它的键（`#[derive(Service)]`），服务 crate 通过 `Svc<S>` 上的扩展 trait（例如为 `Svc<Timer>` 实现的 `TimerExt`）扩展消费者能做的事，由于该 trait 是本地定义的，一致性规则（coherence）允许这样做。访问在运行时由 `ctx.get::<S>()` 针对已提交视图（committed view）中介，无需代理。`#[plugin]` 宏提供编译期的那一半：接收 `Injected<(A, B)>` 的插件函数声明了 `A` 和 `B`，通过它访问其他任何东西都无法通过编译。见插件、服务与 API 设计。"],[309,"**在 kardia 中**：Rust 没有模块注册表，因此 `kardia-hmr` 自己维护一个 `ModuleGraph`，从 `ModuleSource`（WebAssembly、动态库或子进程）加载，并通过 `registry.replace` 替换变化模块所导出的插件。宿主模块的变化只会被报告、需要重启，而不会被应用。一次失败的导入只中止它自己的单元（与它共享模块的那些插件），该单元的缓存条目被恢复，其他单元照常应用。见热重载与加载器内部实现。"],[390,"**在 kardia 中**：依赖环在纤程插入时报告。注册表在存活纤程声明的 `provide`/`inject` 中搜索经过新纤程的环，并记录一条指明该环的警告（`dependency cycle: a -> b -> a`）；该纤程保持 `Pending`。声明的 `provide` 只是元数据，因此提供了未声明键的插件不受此检查约束。见生命周期。"],[329,"**在 kardia 中**：其中若干定理被写成了属性测试。`crates/kardia-core/tests/model.rs` 在带随机延迟的真实 tokio 调度下，对合成组件（写入一张共享表，每次写入都有精确的逆操作）运行随机的编排序列。它在每次运行期间检查顺序性（定理 70），并在静止时检查保持性（定理 64）、恢复精确性（定理 68 / 推论 69）和合流性（Active 纤程恰好是支撑集，定理 80）。见测试。"],[304,"**在 kardia 中**：声明式加载器是 `kardia-loader` crate（条目、分组、领域和插件 `Catalog`），带双向同步的文件式 include（配置文件引入）是 `kardia-include`。见加载器与加载器内部实现。"],[365,"**在 kardia 中**：失败的纤程处于 `FiberState::Failed`，并保留其错误（`Fiber::error()`）；只有 `update`、`restart` 或 `replace` 能使其恢复。见生命周期。"],[594,"**在 kardia 中**：效应体接收一个 `EffectScope`。`scope.defer(..)` 收集一个逆操作但不设边界；`scope.yield_(disposer)` 收集一个逆操作并标记一个迭代边界；`scope.checkpoint()` 只标记边界。效应被释放后，二者都返回 `Err(Interrupted)`，因此 `?` 会在边界处结束效应体，只保留已收集的逆操作。见效应。"],[465,"**在 kardia 中**：每个键在每个领域（realm）中只有一个提供者（第二次 `ctx.provide` 会以 `KardiaError::AlreadyProvided` 失败）。代理是一个普通服务，其注册表是一个 `IdTable`；后端提供者通过在自己的纤程（fiber）上创建的效应（`svc.caller().effect(..)`）向它注册，因此该提供者卸载时注册会被撤回。kardia 没有为访客插件（guest plugin）单独提供代理服务：每个访客纤程的 `GuestService` 就是它自己的 RPC 端点，其调用是同步的，而不是上文所说的异步契约，因此一个挂起的访客会阻塞其调用者。见服务与访客插件。"],[286,"**在 kardia 中**：没有代理。`ctx.get::<S>()` 针对已提交视图执行算法 6，失败时返回 `AccessError::Undeclared`、`AccessError::Inactive` 或 `AccessError::TypeMismatch`；`ctx.live::<S>()` 是对实时存储的反射式读取，对未声明的键也不会失败。编译期检查同样存在：接收 `Injected<(A, B)>` 的 `#[plugin]` 函数声明了 `A` 和 `B`，对未声明的 `S` 调用其 `get::<S, _>()` 无法通过编译。见服务与插件。"],[481,"**在 kardia 中**：注册表在纤程插入时报告依赖环：它在存活纤程声明的 `provide`/`inject` 中搜索，并记录一条指明该环的警告；该纤程保持 `Pending`。见生命周期。"],[62,"**在 kardia 中**：纤程的目标是 `Target::Inactive`（`⊥`）或 `Target::Epoch { revision, providers }`，后者按 `inject` 顺序列出各提供者的 `ImplId`；`ImplId` 和 `FiberId` 永不复用。已提交视图（`ω`）是一个在整个生命周期片段（episode）内固定的键 → `ImplId` 映射；每个绑定都记录其已提交视图指向它的纤程集合（`relied_n`），守卫就等待这个集合清空。在插件的 `apply` 中，`ctx.checkpoint()` 是一个迭代边界：一旦本次加载已被取代或纤程已退役，它返回 `Err(Interrupted)`，这就是 L-Divert 的中止选项。见生命周期。"],[279,"**在 kardia 中**：转移和异步效应体都被派生为 tokio 任务，因此无需调用者轮询也会推进，并且从不在中途被丢弃。所有生命周期簿记都在每个根一把状态锁下的短临界区中完成；持锁期间不运行任何用户代码。见并发。"],[363,"**在 kardia 中**：转移是惯性的。效应体或插件的 `apply` 被派生为任务（spawn），从不在中途被丢弃；释放时会等待它运行到结束或到达一个迭代边界（`ctx.checkpoint()`、`scope.checkpoint()`、`scope.yield_(..)`），并在那里以 `Interrupted` 停止。见并发与生命周期。"],[491,"**在 kardia 中**：键在所有地方都是字符串（`Service::NAME`），因为配置要按名称引用服务。绑定以 `dyn Any` 保存其值，类型化访问会对它做向下转型（downcast），类型不符时以 `AccessError::TypeMismatch` 失败，从而在单个二进制内检测互不相关类型之间的冲突。访客模块不与宿主共享 Rust 类型：它们按字符串键提供和读取服务，以 JSON 视图和 JSON 调用的形式，经由 JSON 访客 ABI 进行。该 ABI 不携带版本标签。见服务与访客插件。"],[443,"**在 kardia 中**：键是字符串 `Service::NAME`，通过 `Service` trait 绑定到一个 Rust 类型。`ctx.provide(value)` 是一个被追踪的效应，返回 `EffectHandle`；在同一领域中重复提供同一个键会以 `KardiaError::AlreadyProvided` 失败。`ctx.isolate(key)`（新的私有领域）、`ctx.isolate_in(key, realm)`（共享领域）和 `ctx.intercept(key, meta)` 返回一个派生的 `Context`。声明的元数据来自 `Inject::with_meta`，`Service::merge_intercept` 把它与上下文中的元数据由外向内合并，默认对 JSON 对象做右偏的浅合并。见服务。"],[1785,"**在一个效应内部**（一个 `effect_sync` 效应体、一个 `effect` 效应体，或一个作用域接管的逆操作），逆操作**按从新到旧的顺序依次**运行："],[3106,"**在仓库的克隆中运行**。"],[1345,"**在语义上忠实于演算**（论文 §4）：纤程（fiber）、目标视图与已提交视图（committed view）、卸载时的守卫、惯性（inertia）、失败结果、每个（键，领域（realm））只有单一来源、合流性。"],[1347,"**地道的 Rust**：带类型的服务键、以显式的调用者归属代替 `Proxy`、可在多线程 tokio 运行时中使用的 `Send + Sync` 句柄、核心中没有 `unsafe`。"],[466,"**基于能力的访问控制**。经代理中介的访问只允许已声明的依赖（未声明的访问是错误）。`inject` 充当能力请求，上下文代理充当能力中介。由于声明是静态的，编排器可以在加载时审查它们。"],[1125,"**声明**：`fn inject() -> Inject`（此处为 `Inject::of::<(Database,)>()`）代替 `type Inject`，`fn provide() -> Vec<Key>` 代替 `&'static [&'static str]` 切片。`#[derive(Service)]` 实现 `Service`（手写的 `impl Service for Database` 同样可用）。使用 `#[plugin]` 宏时，插件是一个接受 `Injected<(Database,)>` 的 `async fn`，这会把未声明的访问变成编译错误（见插件）。"],[3632,"**备份并逐出**每个要逐出的 URL（整个多槽位 ESM 条目 + CJS 模块）。"],[3805,"**外层纤程**承载条目级依赖；**内层纤程**才是真正的插件。若某个依赖在导入期间消失，异步迭代器的守卫会在 `yield` 处停止，插件永远不会启动（在迭代边界上的一次 L-Divert）。之后再失去依赖，会卸载外层纤程，而外层纤程会把内层纤程作为子效应释放；依赖恢复时，外层纤程重新加载并重新导入。"],[1924,"**子进程。** `ProcessSource` 把每个插件实例作为独立进程运行，通过 stdin 和 stdout 以 JSON 行的形式使用访客 ABI（见进程传输）。进程结束的访客只会让它自己的插件失败；破坏协议或超过调用截止时间的访客会被杀死。命令行参数、spawner、超时和退出报告见进程访客。替换可执行文件时，请把新文件重命名覆盖到原路径：正在运行的可执行文件不能被写入，而以写方式打开着的文件不能被启动。"],[147,"**定义 31：测试 / 不可区分性。** `𝒜` 上的一个*测试*是由操作的正向映射与其产出的逆操作组成的有限字；当每个测试在两者上都有定义或都无定义、且产生相同结果时，记 `v ≈_𝒜 v′`。`≃_k := ≈_{𝒜_k}`。"],[149,"**定义 33**：在键集 `S` 上相关的状态在 `S` 上有相同的定义域，且在每个键上的值相关。`≃`（`S = K`）最细；`≃_S` 忽略 `S` 以外的键。相关的状态在满足性和 `notify_d` 上一致，因此*响应性是 `Σ/≃` 的性质*。"],[150,"**定义 34**：`≃` 在函数、积和 `Maybe` 上的逻辑关系扩展，对迭代器按余归纳理解。一个映射与自身相关时，称它*保持* `≃`。"],[152,"**定义 36/37**：*在 `≃_S` 意义下带见证*的效应函数和迭代器：用 `g(δ) ≃_S γ` 代替相等。"],[156,"**定义 40**：`reach(i)` 是通过延续可达的迭代器集合；变换幺半群 `𝔐(i)` 由 `reach(i)` 中所有正向映射与产出的逆操作生成；`len(i)` 是最长的延续链。"],[158,"**定义 42：独立的迭代器** `i, j`："],[162,"**定义 44**：当两个操作 `a, a′` 的提升是独立的效应函数，*并且*任何一方都不干扰另一方的结果时，称它们独立。当一个键上任意两个操作（包括操作与自身）都独立时，称该键是**可交换的**。"],[164,"**定义 46：带见证的余效应**：余效应携带一个证明其键可交换的证据，作为第三个组成部分。与效应的见证一样，*这一义务落在提供该键的组件上*，而不是消费者。此后假定所有余效应都带见证。"],[54,"**定义 54：被依赖**：`relied_n(γ) := ∃m ≠ n, k ∈ d_m. installed_m(γ) ∧ ω_m(k) = n`"],[63,"**定义 55：约束于 `n`。** 若一个映射 (1) 只*写* `σ_n` 以及其他表在 `d_n` 的键上所存的值（对某个余效应进行操作的消费者会写提供者表中该键的值），从不写控制字段或注册表的定义域；并且 (2) 只*读* `σ_n` 和 `σ_m|_{d_n}`，则称它约束于 `n`。实例化是唯一的例外（它写入一个新条目；其逆操作写入一个 `τ`）。"],[64,"**定义 56：`n` 的上下文中介迭代器。** 包含单位元和三种迭代形式的最小集合：在 `d_n ∪ p_n` 的某个键上提升一个操作阶段；在 `p_n` 的某个键上提升一个提供阶段（落入 `σ_n`）；一次实例化。**每个纤程的效应函数都必须属于这个集合。**"],[338,"**定义 63：良构注册表**：(1) 父纤程存在（或为 `root`）；(2) 各提供两两不相交；(3) 已安装纤程的 `ω` 在 `d_n` 上是全函数，且指向存在的纤程；(4) 已安装的 `ω` 所指向的每个纤程都是已安装的。"],[340,"**定义 65**：当一个纤程的提供与另一个纤程的声明相交时，称纤程 `m, n` 是*纠缠的*。若每一对纤程要么独立，要么只通过可交换的共享键纠缠，则称一次运行是*两两独立的*。"],[351,"**定义 72**：优先关系 `n ≺ m := p_n ∩ d_m ≠ ∅`（`n` 可能提供 `m` 声明的某个键）。`≺` 无环是一个**假设**（声明了自己所提供键的组件会违反它）。"],[356,"**定义 74：支撑集 A**：`n ∈ A ⇔ ¬τ_n ∧ (π_n = root ∨ π_n ∈ A) ∧ ∀k ∈ d_n. ∃m ∈ A. k ∈ p_m`，它只是 `τ, π, d, p` 的函数。**引理 75**：支撑关系是良基的，且 `A` 唯一。"],[357,"**定义 76：在其提供上是全的**：一次完成的激活已经设置了 `p` 中的每个键。**引理 77**：在静止时（满足全性），`A` 就是 Active 纤程的集合。"],[287,"**定义 81：条目（entry）**：`id`（稳定的协调键）、`url`（组件模块）、`isolate`、`intercept`、`config`、`disabled`。条目是一份忠实的规约，因为它恰好记录了支撑集所读取的东西：`disabled` → `τ`，树中的父节点 → `π`，`url` → `(d, p)`。条目构成一棵**配置树**；`@cordisjs/group` 加载一组子条目；`@cordisjs/include` 嫁接一个外部 YAML 或 JSON 文件。绑定是**双向的**：组件修订自己的配置或禁用自身时，变更会被写回。"],[4067,"**定义点**（def site）"],[579,"**定理 10**：`(𝔈Γ, ⋄)` 是单位元为 `η(γ) = (γ, id)` 的幺半群；`(f,g) ↦ γ ↦ (f(γ), g)` 是同态 `𝔗Γ → 𝔈Γ`。"],[580,"**定理 11**：`𝔈Γ*` 是子幺半群（见证在组合下保持），且统一逆操作落在其中。"],[582,"**定理 13**：`effect(f) ⋄ effect(g) = effect(f ⋄ g)`。"],[583,"**定理 14**：投影可交换：提升后的正向映射与逆映射作用于状态的方式与 `f` 和 `g` 完全一致。"],[584,"**定理 15**：对带见证的 `e`：`g′(Δ) = (γ, φ ∘ g ∘ f)`。*状态*被精确恢复；*累加器*当且仅当 `g ∘ f = id` 时被恢复；无论如何 `(φ ∘ g ∘ f)(γ) = φ(γ)`，因此健全性不变量得以保持。所以 `effect` 一般**不会**把 `𝔈Γ*` 映到 `𝔈*∂Γ` 中，但撤销从不移动恢复目标。"],[586,"**定理 16**：从 `(γ₀, id)` 出发应用 `e₁…eₙ ∈ 𝔈Γ*`，再按**相反顺序**撤销，每次撤销都恢复其对应应用所面对的状态，且每个中间状态都满足健全性不变量。LIFO 不需要更多条件。"],[567,"**定理 4**：追踪不改变正向行为：`pr₁ ∘ track(f,g) = f ∘ pr₁`。"],[161,"**定理 43**：对两两独立的 `e₁…eₙ`，**以任意排列**应用它们产出的逆操作，都能到达 `γ₀`。无论顺序如何，每个逆操作都只撤回它自己的贡献。"],[163,"**定理 45**：**不同键**上的操作总是独立的（键局部的映射可交换）。"],[184,"**定理 47**：两个上下文中介迭代器，若满足 `P₁ ∩ S₂ = P₂ ∩ S₁ = ∅`（任何一方都不提供另一方触及的键），且共享的键都可交换，则它们独立。当所有余效应都带见证时，只剩这一不相交条件需要检查，而 §4（演算）从声明中直接读出它。"],[568,"**定理 5**：`track` 是幺半群同态 `𝔗Γ → (∂Γ → ∂Γ)`：逐对追踪等于追踪它们的扭转组合。"],[339,"**定理 64**：每条规则都保持良构性。L-Unload 上的守卫承担了条款 (3) 和 (4)：任何已提交视图都不会指向一个已被移除的纤程。推论：被 O-Remove 释放的名字可以被重新分配（不存在过期视图），并且纤程一旦变为 Inactive 就可以被移除，无需单独的依赖检查。"],[343,"**定理 68（恢复精确性）**：在 `n` 的生命周期片段中的任意时刻应用 `n` 的累加器，都会让每张表停留在仅由*其他*纤程的步骤从片段开始时所能到达的位置："],[570,"**定理 7**：若 `g(f(γ)) = γ`，则 `recover(track(f,g)(γ,φ)) = recover(γ,φ)`。一个逆操作能撤销自身的被追踪步骤不会移动恢复目标。状态的**健全性不变量**（soundness invariant）是 `φ(γ) = γ₀`；从 `(γ₀, id)` 出发经此类步骤到达的每个状态都满足它，而 `recover` 会把状态带回 `(γ₀, id)`。"],[347,"**定理 70（顺序性）**"],[350,"**定理 71（解析一致性）**：一次转移的每次迭代都针对同一个已提交解析 `ω` 运行。当纤程离开 Reloading 时，要么 L-Finish 让它针对 `ω` 落地为 Active，要么 L-Divert 把它带出，其生命周期片段以精确恢复关闭。一次转移从不跨越其余效应的两种解析（*转移内部*没有毛刺（glitch）；Cordis 没有 FRP 那样的全局“轮次”）。"],[352,"**定理 73（进展性）**：假设 `≺` 无环、迭代器长度不超过 `K`、名字有限。那么："],[359,"**定理 80（合流性）**：任何到达静止状态的运行都可以化归为一个**规范**运行：相同的编排步骤，然后按线性化支撑关系的顺序，为每个被支撑的纤程执行一个生命周期片段。具有相同编排输入的两次运行到达 `≃` 相关的状态（在重命名意义下）。*生命周期关系具有唯一的范式。*"],[2986,"**实时变更**：应用运行期间，可以重新配置、替换或热重载任意插件，应用的其余部分会随之调整。"],[3002,"**实现**"],[2093,"**宿主函数**（WASM 从模块 `cordis` 或 `kardia` 导入；dylib 则是 `host` 结构体 `{ host, read, write, log, provide, view, invoke }` 中的函数指针，每个都以 `host.host` 作为第一个参数）。指针是访客地址，长度是字节数："],[2073,"**导出**（状态 `0` 表示成功；失败时访客用 `write` 写出错误）："],[3426,"**导出器**通过 `logger.exporter(exp)` 以被追踪的效应注册，因此控制台导出器插件在卸载时会自行注销。一个内置导出器维护最近 1000 条消息的环形缓冲区（供后接入的控制台使用）。"],[3312,"**将其从纤程的顶层列表中移除**（`this._disposables.delete(dispose)`），即所有权转移（见下文），"],[415,"**局部空间可组合性**：组件只在满足其规约的状态下激活（从不读取不存在的绑定），并且每一次上下文变化都会依据规约进行分类（满足性的丧失在发生处即被检测到）。有两件事留给全局形式（§4.3.3，见元理论）：只在一个绑定所引起的停用全部完成*之后*才撤回该绑定，以及在激活运行期间保持其所读取的绑定不变。"],[186,"**局限**：把每个共享位置都绑定到一个键上是一种*纪律*，而不是该构造本身的性质。系统无法具体化为余效应的位置不在该定理的范围内（见讨论与相关工作中 §6.1 的系统边界）。"],[1042,"**带 `inject` 的条目使用两个纤程（fiber）**"],[2280,"**带 `inject` 的条目有两个纤程。** 声明了 `inject` 的条目运行一个外层纤程（标记为 `loader:outer`，即 `kardia_loader::OUTER_TAG`），它持有依赖、解析插件、通过一次 `ctx.checkpoint()?`，然后启动运行插件的内层纤程。没有 `inject` 的条目只有内层纤程。"],[1792,"**并发地**释放它们，记录每个失败和 panic；"],[1595,"**应用 → 文件**：运行时的修改（通过加载器 API，或插件更新、释放（dispose）自身）会写回给它的所有者：文件本身，或加载该文件的 `include` 的配置中的某个补丁（见 `include`）。生成的 id 也随之写入。"],[206,"**应用框架**，例如 Koishi（§5.3）。"],[1747,"**异步：** `ctx.effect(label, |scope| async move { … })` 以任务形式运行效应体。它绝不会中途被丢弃：释放会等待它运行到结尾或到达迭代边界。失败时会释放效应体已收集的内容、记录日志，并通过 `EffectHandle::ready()` 报告。返回 `Interrupted`（见下文）不算失败。"],[148,"**引理 32**：`≃_k` 是一个被 `𝒜_k` 中所有操作保持的等价关系，并且是此类关系中*最粗*的（证明原则：给出任意一个包含该对的、被保持的等价关系即可）。"],[151,"**引理 35**：在映射和迭代器上，`≃_S` 是部分等价关系。"],[153,"**引理 38**：把 §3.1 中所有等式的 `=` 换成 `≃` 后依然成立。"],[154,"**引理 39**：上下文中介迭代器属于 `ℑ^S_Σ`，其中 `S` 是任意包含其各阶段所触及键的集合。"],[157,"**引理 41**：交换性在生成元上即可判定；`⋄` 不会扩大该幺半群。"],[65,"**引理 57**：其成员约束于 `n`，并在 `≃_{d_n ∪ p_n}` 意义下带见证。"],[331,"**引理 59（表 1 中的查找）**："],[337,"**引理 60（≃ 不变性）**：规则无法区分 `≃` 相关的状态。**引理 61（等变性）**：结果在纤程名字重命名的意义下成立。**引理 62（残留条目）**：一个已退役、Inactive、为空且没有子纤程的条目对所有规则都不可见。"],[341,"**引理 66**：每次运行都是两两独立的（由带见证的余效应（coeffect）和定理 47 保证，见上下文范式）。"],[342,"**引理 67（纠缠的步骤）**：在 `n` 的生命周期片段打开期间，`n` 的提供者 `m` 只执行恒等状态映射（守卫阻止了它的 L-Unload）；消费者的步骤与 `g_n` 可交换；在 `n` 处于 Reloading 期间，与之纠缠的纤程只执行恒等映射。"],[358,"**引理 78（换位）**与**引理 79（删除）**：相邻的独立步骤可以交换，而一个已关闭的生命周期片段（连同其实例化）可以被删除而不改变终点。"],[1117,"**引用环**：没有 `Root` 类型，也没有 `shutdown()`。释放根纤程（`root.fiber().dispose().await`）会重启它，并撤销注册在它上面的一切，从而撤回所有绑定。"],[4096,"**影子**上下文（`symbols.shadow`）是一个二元组：对象本身是使用点（其纤程接收效应），其 `shadow` 属性是定义点（代理的 `get` 陷阱在 `locate` 时查询它）。因此，在服务方法内部："],[1301,"**恢复精确性**"],[3545,"**惯性（inertia）：** 过时的目标不会中止进行中的 `apply`。加载照常落地，纤程随后再卸载（异步宿主采取 L-Divert 中*落地*的那个分支）。执行前让出的那个微任务，使一连串 `update()` 调用能完全跳过被取代的加载（`update.spec.ts: 'skips superseded loads before executing the plugin'`）。"],[3107,"**或者从 crates.io 安装可执行文件**，并让它读取你自己的配置文件："],[301,"**托管领域。**`isolate: true` 给出一个条目私有的*局部*领域，以条目 id 标记，并在条目移动时随之移动；`isolate: \"name\"` 给出一个*全局*领域，由所有指明该字符串的条目共享。当不再有条目指明某个领域时，它被丢弃。"],[1046,"**托管领域（realm）**"],[1060,"**托管领域**：分界测试是在条目表为带标记的 `Overlay` 节点的上下文上调用 `Context::is_within(..)`；领域回收的修复已完成（`collect_realms` 使用 `continue`）。"],[3272,"**按领域符号隔离**实现了放宽后的演算规则“在领域内不相交”（§4.4，见元理论）。"],[2206,"**接受。** 发生变化的模块，以及导入了某个已接受模块的每个模块（宿主模块除外），都被接受。"],[483,"**接口漂移**：提供者在不同版本之间改变了 `k` 背后的接口；"],[345,"**推论 69（终态恢复）**：生命周期片段关闭之后，状态等于“只有其他纤程”的状态；特别地，`σ_n = ∅`（这正是 O-Remove 的前提）。"],[3229,"**提供者侧守卫**：`await` 直到 `impl.dependents` 为空（`impl.release` 由最后一个依赖方的卸载来 resolve）。它总会至少让出一次，使子级清理仍能访问继承来的服务；"],[3271,"**提供者身份**是 `Impl.uid`，一个新鲜的计数器值。它实现了已提交视图与目标视图中“看名称而非值”的原则。"],[143,"**提供阶段**：对 `k ∈ P` 执行 `set(k, v)`（这是任何操作都无法创建的键）。"],[2920,"**插件**是函数、类或带 `apply` 的对象，各自可带 `name`、`inject`、`provide` 和 `Config`（任意 Standard Schema 校验器）。`apply` 可以返回 promise，或返回一个在插件停止时运行的函数。"],[3044,"**插件作者**，用 Rust 或访客模块编写插件"],[3739,"**插入补丁** `{ id?, insert: [...] }` 把条目追加到某个分组（或根）中。"],[2103,"**握手。** 宿主的第一行以导出的形式提供版本 2：`{\"export\":\"hello\",\"input\":{\"protocol\":\"kardia-guest/2\"}}`。版本 2 的访客应答 `{\"ready\":\"kardia-guest/2\"}`。版本 1 的访客应答 `{\"done\":1}`（它对任何不认识的导出都这样应答），宿主随后按版本 1 为它服务。因此两种访客都能立即启动，版本 2 的访客在从不提供它的宿主上也能运行。在握手时限内没有应答的访客会被杀死。"],[2669,"**撤回会等待消费者。** 撤销提供会移除绑定并通知该领域，然后等待所有已提交到这个绑定的消费者完成各自的清理，最后才移除这项提供。"],[493,"**操作系统**：让声明的余效应规约成为组件所能触及的全部（类似 WASM 的导入），原生提供隔离（isolation）与拦截，并把操作系统资源（内存、文件描述符）作为余效应提供，使获取由分发资源的一方一次性记录；事务式或写时复制的存储可以使某些外发变得可撤销。"],[142,"**操作阶段**：对 `k ∈ S` 执行 `a ∈ 𝒜_k`，并根据结果选择延续；"],[2922,"**效应：** `ctx.effect(scope => ...)` 用 `scope.defer` 收集逆操作，或直接返回一个。异步的效应体不会被取消：效应被处置后，`scope.checkpoint()` 会结束它。"],[675,"**效应**。判断形式为 `Γ ⊢ t : T ! effect`。单子效应（Moggi、Wadler）把带效应的计算封装在 `T(A)` 中，带有单位 `η` 和乘法 `μ`。代数效应（Plotkin 与 Power）声明操作签名；效应处理器（Plotkin 与 Pretnar）用定界延续来解释它们（Koka、Eff、OCaml 5）。"],[2984,"**效应**（effect）：插件建立的一切（监听器、定时器、服务、子插件）都会被追踪，并在插件停止时撤销。"],[2914,"**效应从不跨越边界。** 每一侧各自撤销自己的效应。"],[1036,"**数据模型**"],[1057,"**数据模型**：`EntryOptions` 是一个带类型的视图，从已被 `validate_options` 接受的选项中读取（`EntryOptions::read`）；JSON 对象仍是唯一可信来源，因此未知键无需 `flatten` 映射即可在回写中保留。`IsolateLabel::{Private, Shared(String)}` 与 `Disabled::{Bool(bool), Expr(String)}` 与计划一致。"],[1594,"**文件 → 应用**：文件变化时，新条目按 `id` 与运行中的条目协调：变化的条目原地更新，新增的条目启动，删除的条目停止。"],[2413,"**文件编辑 → 树。** 每次读取都会调和进子树；只应用最新的目标树，较旧的被跳过。编辑过程中无法解析的文件（编辑时出现空文件或截断的文件很常见）会记录为警告，运行中的树保持不变，并且在之后某次读取成功之前不写入任何内容。"],[3005,"**方案**"],[353,"**无死锁**：非静止状态总是允许执行某条生命周期规则（被依赖的消费者所阻塞的 Unloading 纤程链沿 `≺` 递增，因此有限，并终止于一个未被阻塞的纤程）。"],[1129,"**日志**：`ctx.logger_named(\"greeter\")`，或 `ctx.logger()`，后者以插件名命名。"],[626,"**时间可组合性**（temporal composability）"],[469,"**时间方面的要求**：闭包（逆操作是一个被捕获的值），以及一种在运行时引入和撤回组件代码的方式："],[169,"**是**"],[633,"**智能体框架**：一个持续改写自身组件的框架无法承受每次修改都重启一次，而朴素的代码替换会悄无声息地破坏依赖者。"],[1272,"**暂停时间**（`start_paused = true`）"],[459,"**暂扣与补偿**。要恢复一次外发，要么暂扣它直到产生它的状态确定下来（输出提交问题），要么进行补偿（删除创建的文件、退还扣款），补偿只在应用提供的、更粗的等价意义下成立。补偿像逆操作一样按 LIFO 组合，但交换性元理论（元理论）必须针对这一更粗的关系重新建立。"],[2428,"**暂时性失败。** 以 `PermissionDenied` 或 `ResourceBusy` 失败的重命名（例如杀毒软件占用了文件）最多重试 10 次，每次多等待 20 ms。"],[313,"**有效性威胁**：单一生态、单一语言、观察性证据；开销与生产力的测量留待未来工作。"],[2985,"**服务**（service）：插件提供服务，并声明自己依赖的服务。插件在依赖可用后启动，在某个依赖被替换时重启，在某个依赖消失时停止。"],[2644,"**服务**（service）是由一个插件提供、被其他插件依赖的值。运行时（runtime）记录谁提供了什么、谁依赖什么：声明了某个服务的插件会在服务可用时启动，在服务被替换时重启，在服务消失时停止。本页介绍如何定义、提供和使用服务，调用如何归属到调用者，隔离（isolation）与拦截（interception）如何改变一个上下文（context）看到的内容，以及如何使用事件和日志器。"],[2921,"**服务**以字符串为键。`ctx.get(key)` 是带检查的访问：插件未声明的服务会失败。`ctx.live(key)` 不经检查读取实时存储。`Service` 返回的是一个视图，其 `caller` 是发起访问的上下文，对应 Kardia 的 `Svc::caller`。"],[462,"**服务代理**（service broker）：一个中心服务同时被后端提供者和消费者依赖声明（inject）；提供者通过可撤销效应*向代理注册*；后端提供者变化时，消费者看不到任何变化。"],[2915,"**服务的可用性会跨越边界。** 宿主暴露的服务恰在暴露期间出现在客户端，所以注入它的客户端插件恰在此时运行，并在它被重新暴露时重启。"],[2759,"**服务自身的依赖。** 服务通过构造时保存的 `Context`（它的定义点）解析自己的依赖，因此不需要影子上下文。由此产生两点与 Cordis 不同的行为（在 Cordis 中两者都跟随使用点）："],[2275,"**条目**是一个由选项组成的 JSON 对象。JSON 始终是事实来源，因此未知键会被容忍并在回写时保留。键保持稳定的顺序：`id`、`name`，其余按字母序，`config` 最后。"],[2281,"**条目何时运行。** 字面量 `disabled: true` 或被禁用的祖先分组会阻止条目运行。`disabled` 表达式在外层纤程的上下文（context）中求值（该上下文能看到条目的 `inject`）；求值失败时条目被禁用，并报告失败。接着对条目的 `intercept` 求值；`intercept` 无法求值时插件不会运行。`config` 中的表达式在每次加载时于插件的上下文中插值，源配置保留表达式本身；分组的 `config` 是其条目列表，不做插值。"],[1040,"**条目状态机**"],[1575,"**标识符**：一个名字读取同名服务的 JSON 值。条目必须在 `inject` 中声明该服务。只有具备 JSON 视图的服务才能这样读取（见编写插件）。"],[2277,"**树**（tree）是一组共用一个后端的分组，后端负责持久化它的变化。加载器自己的树位于内存中。插件可以创建子树（`loader.create_tree(ctx, backend)`）；include 为每个文件这样做。"],[2414,"**树的变化 → 文件。** 子树在运行时的变化（API 编辑、插件自行更新与自行释放）记录在一个日志（journal）中，并回写给拥有它们的一方：文件，或 include 自身配置中的某个补丁；后者通过 include 在父树中的条目持久化。关闭应用不会写入文件。"],[1052,"**校验**"],[204,"**核心库**：效应（effect）与余效应（coeffect）系统（§5.1）；"],[3626,"**根（Roots）**：`await callback()` → 绝对路径（经校验）。"],[1123,"**根**：`Context::new()` 创建根上下文；`root.fiber().dispose()` 代替 `root.shutdown()`。"],[1059,"**检查点**：同步的，`ctx.checkpoint()?`。"],[2181,"**模块**由 `ModuleId` 标识，即一个绝对路径（`/app/plugins/foo.wasm`）。其代码来自 `ModuleSource`："],[2101,"**模块的生命周期。** 加载模块时会实例化它一次以读取元数据（先 `meta`，再 `dispose`）；`deps` 中的依赖先加载。之后运行该插件的每个纤程都会得到一个新实例：以 `{ config, imports }` 调用 `apply`，任意次 `call`，以及纤程被释放时的 `dispose`，之后实例被丢弃。状态非零且没有写出任何内容时，以 `guest failed with status <n>` 失败。"],[2667,"**每个键在每个领域（realm）中只有一个绑定。** 同一领域中的第二个提供者（provider）会失败，错误为 `KardiaError::AlreadyProvided`，消息是 `service \"database\" has been registered at <db>`（尖括号内是提供它的插件名）。"],[468,"**沙箱化**不受信任的代码需要一个超越语言的执行边界（SFI、独立的运行时、沙箱进程、容器）；不受信任的组件通过一个*桥*访问宿主（host）的依赖，而这个桥本身是一个普通纤程，其能力可以被削减。"],[3273,"**没有编译期检查**：声明的键与访问的键只在运行时由代理检查（论文 §5.1.4 指出这本可以静态完成）。"],[419,"**派生**（derived）：保持输入不变，返回一个*从它派生出的新上下文*，逆操作为恒等；恢复时丢弃派生上下文。"],[3425,"**消息：** `{ sn, ts, name, type, level, args, fiber?: WeakRef<Fiber> }`。带 `cause` 的错误会记录其 cause；非空的 `AggregateError` 会被展平。"],[3627,"**清扫（Sweep）**：按类型槽位，从缓存中逐出*失败的* ModuleJob（Node 会保留它们，并在每次导入时重新抛出）。"],[2672,"**清理期间推迟移除。** 提供者卸载期间，它撤回的提供在清理结束前仍对其后代可见，这样后代在自己的清理中仍能使用继承来的服务。"],[411,"**满足谓词**：`σ ⊧ d := ∀k ∈ d. k ∈ dom(σ)`，由于 `dom(σ)` 有限，它是可判定的。"],[3115,"**热重载（hot reload）一个插件**。编辑 `examples/plugins/hello.wat` 中的问候语。`hmr` 条目会原地重新加载这个 WebAssembly 插件：旧实例先输出告别语，然后新实例输出你的问候语。"],[2104,"**版本 1：**"],[461,"**独占绑定**：同一时刻至多绑定一个；切换时卸载一个提供者再加载另一个，会扰动每个消费者。"],[2999,"**理论**"],[1333,"**理论**：概念一节（论文的定义、规则与定理）；"],[2923,"**生命周期：** 纤程依次经历 `pending`、`loading`、`active`、`unloading`、`failed` 和 `disposed`，与 Rust 一致。依赖被替换时插件重启，依赖离开时插件等待，提供者会一直运行到它的消费者完成清理。`fiber.update(config)`、`restart()`、`ctx.onUpdate(...)` 和 `ctx.registry.replace(old, new)`（热替换，用于 Vite HMR）的行为都与 Rust 相同。"],[3634,"**用并查集划分单元**：若两次尝试的**旧 ∪ 新**闭包共享某个被逐出的模块，它们就并入同一个单元（共享同一个变化依赖的两个插件，不能最终持有该依赖的不同实例）。"],[3042,"**用户**，用配置文件运行应用"],[2967,"**用配置文件运行应用**：配置文件，然后是热重载。"],[1044,"**目录（Catalog）**"],[1058,"**目录**：`Catalog::register::<P>()`、`register_def(name, def)` 与 `alias(alias, name)`（而不是 `register_alias`）；`kardia_loader::builtins()` 注册 `group` 并把 `@cordisjs/plugin-group` 设为它的别名，`kardia::catalog()` 再以名称及其 JavaScript 包名添加其他内置插件。"],[1276,"**真实时间**"],[3048,"**研究者**，关注其理论"],[735,"**移植规则：** TS 代码中的每个同步段都变成 `State` 上的**一个临界区**。持锁期间不做任何等待，并且**持锁期间不调用任何用户代码**（插件的 `apply`、撤销函数（disposer）、事件监听器、可用性检查）。"],[629,"**空间可组合性**（spatial composability）"],[475,"**空间方面的要求**：两个层面的依赖注入机制："],[3633,"**第 1 阶段，导入**，对每个过时插件依次执行：重新导入，并检查其导出是一个有效插件（`registry.resolve`）。*所有可能失败的校验都发生在这里，此时只有模块缓存被修改过*，因此后续阶段无需回滚。在所有插件都导入完成之前，不恢复任何缓存条目。"],[3636,"**第 2 阶段，替换（同步）**：对每个已提交的尝试执行 `ctx.registry.replace(oldPlugin, newPlugin)`。`replace` 把旧插件键作为新插件的别名（此后 `ctx.plugin(old)` 实例化新代码），并在每个纤程上调用 `fiber._replace(newRuntime, newInject)`：重新检查依赖、清除错误、递增修订号 ⇒ **同一个纤程对象原地卸载并重新加载**（身份、父级、配置与加载器条目均被保留）。"],[3637,"**第 3 阶段，稳定（并发）**：`await Promise.all(fibers.map(f => f.await().catch(noop)))`。**没有回滚**：新 `apply` 抛出的插件保持 FAILED（与冷启动时一样），并在下一次变化时重试。"],[1128,"**等待稳定**：只要没有正在进行的转换，`greeter.settled()` 就会立即完成，因此示例先等待 `db` 稳定；数据库被提供之后，greeter 的转换才会开始。"],[302,"**算法 7：借助定界符重新分配领域**。每个键有一个定界符 symbol `δ_k`；每个上下文在 `δ_k` 下存储一个标签，由后代继承，并在每次重新分配时重新生成，因此 `γ′[δ_k] = d₁ ⇔ γ′` 派生自该条目的上下文。"],[2279,"**类型化视图。** `EntryOptions::read(&options)` 把已校验的选项读成类型化视图（`id`、`name`、`config`、`group`、`disabled: Option<Disabled>`（其中 `Disabled::{Bool, Expr}`）、`inject`、`intercept`、`isolate: Vec<(String, IsolateLabel)>`（其中 `IsolateLabel::{Private, Shared(label)}`））；JSON 对象仍是事实来源。"],[476,"**类型层面**：类型正确的依赖访问；上下文类型必须记录每个键的余效应。*类型类（Haskell）和 **trait（Rust）** 让提供者可以在自己的模块中通过实例/`impl` 扩展上下文类型*；TypeScript 使用模块扩充（module augmentation）。"],[1120,"**类型级的键**：进程内的检查是访问时的向下转型（`AccessError::TypeMismatch`）。访客插件的服务以 JSON 值和 JSON 调用跨越模块边界（`GuestService`），因此没有任何 Rust 类型或 `TypeId` 跨越边界。"],[634,"**粗粒度的变通办法**：操作系统进程以进程为单位提供时间可组合性；容器编排器以服务为单位提供空间可组合性。二者在重启时都会丢弃进程内状态，也无法表达同一地址空间内的依赖；粒度是错的。"],[1796,"**纤程**是插件的一次实例化。实例化插件时，会在当前纤程上登记一个效应，其逆操作让新纤程退役："],[1789,"**纤程卸载时**，运行时："],[3547,"**纤程级**（`_unload` 中的循环）：只要还有任何提供项有依赖方，提供者纤程就不运行*任何*撤销函数。"],[3424,"**级别：** `exporter.levels[name] ?? exporter.levels.default ?? logger.level ?? INFO`；级别为 `ERROR=0, WARN=1, INFO=2, DEBUG=3`。"],[2868,"**级别：** 取 `logger` 拦截元数据中的 `level`（如有）。`logger.with_level(level)` 在副本上设置级别。"],[1064,"**纯模块**，几乎逐字移植并单独进行单元测试：`journal`（记录、合并、展平、应用、三方 `reconcile`；以文件为准）、`patch`（插入/覆盖补丁、`PatchIndex` 归属、`route_journal`）、匿名 id 分配。"],[205,"**组件加载器**：配置协调与 HMR（§5.2）；"],[2940,"**组合式函数：** `useContext()`；`usePlugin(plugin, config)` 在组件存续期间运行一个插件；`useService(key)` 是跟随某个服务的 ref（未被提供时为 `undefined`）；`useContributions(key)` 是用于自定义渲染（如导航菜单）的计算列表；`useFiberState(fiber)` 跟随一个纤程。"],[354,"**终止**：每个纤程至多执行 `(K + 3)(V(n) + 1)` 步，其中 `V(n)` 是目标变化的次数，它是有限的。"],[3548,"**绑定级**（`provide` 的逆操作，见 `provide`）：撤回一个绑定只等待该绑定的依赖方。这使一个提供者可以撤回绑定 A 而无需等待绑定 B 的消费者（`service-dispose.spec.ts: 'withdraws one binding without waiting for another binding from the same provider'`），也使一个绑定可以在某个消费者初始化期间被替换。"],[488,"**结构兼容性**谓词（宽度子类型容易；行为契约困难；有界量化不可判定）。"],[2970,"**编写无需重启应用即可重新加载的插件**：访客插件。"],[2968,"**编写编译进应用的插件**：编写插件、服务和效应。"],[677,"**缺口**。二者都是作用于词法固定作用域的静态工具。没有任何固定的词法作用域能界定一个在部署之后才加载的插件，也没有任何编译期上下文能预见由运行时配置产生的依赖。因此论文把这些结构*具体化*，使运行时能够操作它们，并在动态中确立这些系统在静态中所保证的东西。"],[741,"**考虑过的替代方案：** 一种 `!Send` 的设计（在 `LocalSet` 上使用 `Rc<RefCell<..>>`）最贴近 JS 的字面形态，有一轮分析曾针对加载器推荐过它。它在核心中被否决，因为它会迫使生态中的每个插件和服务都兼容 `!Send`（不能 `tokio::spawn`，与大多数异步库配合起来很别扭），而上面的“锁加动作”约束能以相当的复杂度保持同样的原子性。如果之后的性能分析显示访问热路径上存在锁竞争，可以通过 `arc-swap` 发布已提交视图（committed view，在每个生命周期片段（episode）内不可变），而不改变语义。"],[1048,"**自我释放 / 自我更新的回写**"],[1061,"**自我释放**：没有引入 `DisposeReason`。加载器在它自己的 `fiber.dispose()` 调用前后设置每个条目的 `disposing` 标志（`entry.rs`，`dispose_fiber`），与 TS 的 `_disposing` 标志是同一种模式。"],[458,"**获取与外发**。触及外部分两个阶段：*获取*（acquisition）在边界内设置一条记录（`open` → 描述符，`malloc` → 内存块，`fork` → 子进程），这是可撤销的；*外发*（emission）通过该通道推送数据（`write`、`send`）并跨越到外部，这是不可撤销的。"],[2616,"**获取资源后立即注册它的逆操作**，这样插件在启动过程中被停止时也不会泄漏任何东西。"],[1118,"**表达式**：决定采用一个无副作用的 JavaScript 子集（`kardia_loader::expr`），而不是 CEL；见状态与偏离。"],[1062,"**表达式**：实现为一个无副作用的 JavaScript 子集（`kardia_loader::expr`），而不是 CEL；标识符通过服务的 JSON 视图（`ctx.view(name)`，由 `provide_serialized_as` 提供）解析，而不是通过 `ExprValue` trait；见表达式。"],[1054,"**表达式**（`!!js`）"],[3740,"**覆盖补丁** `{ id, name?, ...keys }` 覆盖现有条目的键。若给出 `name`，它必须匹配（防止误给另一个插件打补丁）；覆盖分组的 `config` 会替换其子级列表。"],[1066,"**解析**：一个支持位置信息（span）和自定义标签的 YAML 解析器（`saphyr` 系列）：`!!js` → `Value::Expr`；错误**和**警告都是致命的；JSON 通过 `serde_json` 解析，并额外做一遍带位置信息的处理以获取位置。"],[1307,"**解析一致性**"],[2258,"**解析名称。** 加载器通过 `Resolver` 把条目的 `name` 转换成 `PluginDef`，相当于模块导入。解析可以是异步的："],[4001,"**论文：** `fiber.target` 是 `target(γ, n)`（键 → 提供者 uid 元组）的哈希，未满足时为 ⊥。"],[4015,"**论文：** `notify` 遍历所有纤程并调用 `refresh`。"],[4004,"**论文：** O-Retire（设置 τ）与 O-Remove（删除条目）是两条独立的规则；退役的条目可能残留（vestigial）。"],[4013,"**论文：** 每次迭代之前检查守卫；L-Divert 可以中止，也可以落地。"],[4010,"**论文：** 累加器是一个 LIFO 组合；算法 5 运行一次 `fiber.dispose()`。"],[4007,"**论文（算法 5）：** `unload` 等待被 `notify(...)` 的依赖方的 `await()`。"],[1890,"**访客插件**（guest plugin）是 `hmr` 插件可以原地重载的独立模块；编译进二进制的插件则不同，修改其代码需要重启。在 `kardia` 二进制加载的配置文件中，任何不是内置插件的条目名都是访客模块路径，相对于配置文件："],[3603,"**该实现与论文的算法 10 有实质性差异**（见论文与代码对照）。"],[1568,"**语法**：JavaScript 的一个无副作用子集："],[492,"**语言**：让上下文重新变得隐式（为了易用性，也为了防止组件通过闭包或全局变量触及另一个组件的上下文，那会把效应泄漏到其生命周期之外）；为效应提供编译器语法（把效应迭代器编译成一个在其栈帧中保存逆操作的状态机，而不是每一步一个闭包）；把余效应规约纳入类型系统（在编译期报告依赖环；类似行类型（row types）的结构化依赖比较）。"],[2916,"**调用是异步的**，两个方向都是。另一侧已不在时调用以 `unavailable` 失败，未按时应答时以 `timeout` 失败。"],[2937,"**贡献点**是 `Contributions<T>` 服务（`defineContributions(key)` 提供一个）。`register(item)` 是调用它的插件的效应；条目按 `order` 排序，`id` 唯一，`items` / `entries` 是 Vue 响应式的。"],[3046,"**贡献者**，参与 kardia 的开发"],[2941,"**路由：** `addRoute(ctx, router, route)` 以效应的形式添加 vue-router 路由：插件停止时路由被移除。"],[1126,"**边界**：`ctx.checkpoint()?` 与 `ctx.on_dispose(..)?` 是同步且可能失败的。"],[3631,"**过时插件（Stale plugins）**：对每个 runtime，取其导出者经由 accepted 模块的闭包。要重新导入的模块是**最外层的导出者**（保留入口模块的 `inject`/`Config` 元数据）。"],[2427,"**过期内容检查。** 每次重命名之前，它都检查文件是否仍是它上次读到的内容。若期间有人写过文件，它先读取并合并，然后再写。"],[2207,"**过期插件。** 模块闭包触及某个已接受模块的每个已注册插件都是过期的。由多个模块导出的插件（例如某个模块重新导出了它）从最外层的导出者取得替换，即没有被其他导出者导入的那个。"],[2671,"**过期的加载不能提供服务。** 已退役但加载仍在进行的纤程仍可登记逆操作（这样它获取的东西不会泄漏），但其 `provide` 调用会以 `KardiaError::InactiveEffect` 失败。"],[477,"**运行时层面**：访问必须被动态中介（JavaScript `Proxy`、Python 描述符，或以牺牲类型安全为代价的反射）。"],[1310,"**进展性**"],[1078,"**进程外插件**（重新派生进程 = 重新加载），采用论文 §6.2 的服务代理/RPC 模式。"],[2670,"**退役的提供者立即让出领域。** 释放（dispose）一个提供者会立即解除它的现存绑定，所以继任者可以在旧消费者仍在清理时于同一领域提供服务（旧消费者通过各自的已提交视图（committed view）继续读取旧绑定）。"],[2668,"**通知时机取决于提供者的状态。** 只有提供者纤程处于 `Active` 时才立即通知消费者（consumer）；否则在它进入 `Active` 时通知。提供者离开 `Active` 时，会先通知消费者，再运行它的任何逆操作。"],[467,"**通过拦截（interception）实现细粒度策略**：例如，一个文件系统依赖携带关于可读和可写路径的元数据，由提供者检查。它可以从上下文进行调整而无需修改提供者；它影响的是依赖如何被使用，而不是依赖是否被满足，因此可以在运行时改变而无需重新加载。"],[1127,"**配置**：`ctx.plugin::<P>(config)` 要求 `P::Config: Serialize`（该值会像其他任何配置一样被序列化再解码），因此只实现了 `Deserialize` 的配置要通过 `plugin_value` 以 JSON 传入。`db.update(value)?` 立即校验，并返回需要 await 的 future；`update_with(value, no_save)` 接受该标志。"],[1116,"**重入**：临界区把 `Action` 排入状态中（见并发）；在锁下释放的值在解锁之后才被丢弃。"],[1124,"**错误**：`Result<()>`（`kardia_core::Result`）代替 `Result<(), PluginError>` 与 `anyhow::Result`。"],[1068,"**错误**：使用结构化的 `ConfigFrame { id, file, line, col }` 链，而不是改写后的栈字符串。"],[484,"**键冲突**：互不相关的提供者选择了相同的键名。"],[486,"**键命名空间** `K × P`（按包划分；消除冲突，但与注册中心耦合）；"],[1063,"**键顺序**：选项是 `serde_json` 映射；只有开启 `preserve-order` 特性时，`sort_keys` 才能让回写得到稳定的顺序（`id`、`name`，其余按字母序，`config` 最后）。该特性开启 `serde_json/preserve_order`，默认开启。Cargo 会把这个特性统一到构建中的每个 `serde_json::Map`，所以它是可选的：关闭时，映射与回写都按字母序列出键。`kardia-include` 与 `kardia` 门面开启它；`kardia-hmr` 把它作为默认特性透传，因此关闭 `kardia-hmr`（以及 `kardia-loader`）默认特性的应用保留 serde_json 的默认映射。"],[306,"**阶段 1：分类（算法 8）**。输入是 `stashed`（发生变化的文件）和 `externals`（不可替换的模块，它们的变化需要完全重启）。在 `get_imports` 上求不动点：若一个待定模块的某个导入被接受，则它被*接受*；若其所有导入都被拒绝，则它被*拒绝*；剩下的（环）默认为拒绝。"],[2208,"**阶段 1：导入。** 驱逐过期插件的模块，并重新导入每个过期插件。这是唯一可能失败的步骤；有效性在这里检查，此时只有模块缓存发生了变化，所以后续阶段无需回滚。在所有插件都导入完之前不恢复任何内容，因此没有新模块会链接到被驱逐的旧模块。导入错误会被记录。"],[2210,"**阶段 2：替换。** 每个已提交的插件都通过 `registry.replace` 原地替换，并记录为 `reload plugin at <module>`。"],[307,"**阶段 2：过期条目检测（算法 9）**。对每个条目，收集 `entry.url` 的传递导入，遇到被拒绝的模块即停止；若这棵树与 `accepted` 相交，则该条目过期，其树被并入 `accepted`。"],[308,"**阶段 3：事务式重新加载（算法 10）**。使被接受模块的缓存失效（并备份），重新导入每个过期条目，并换入一个新纤程；一旦出现任何错误，就恢复缓存，用备份重建每个过期条目，然后重新抛出错误。系统从不进入半重载的状态。（在 Node.js 上，ESM 和 CJS 缓存都会被清除。）"],[2211,"**阶段 3：稳定。** 被替换的纤程并发地稳定下来。不做回滚：应用失败的插件保持失败，与冷启动时一样。"],[2925,"**隔离与拦截：** `ctx.isolate(key, realm?)`、`ctx.intercept(key, meta)`、`ctx.interceptMeta(key)`。"],[1304,"**顺序性**"],[844,"**首次 CI 发布。** 按上文递增版本并打标签。发布完成后，把每个包的 *Publishing access* 设为 \"Require two-factor authentication and disallow tokens\"，这样只有可信发布者（以及启用了双因素认证的维护者）可以发布。"],[4610,"*Bound:* tables are restored only up to each key's `≃_k`: a monotone allocator is not rewound, heap layout is not restored, a sent message stays sent."],[8327,"*effects*, *interception*, *isolation*"],[4449,"*Interface design rule (from Definition 31):* publishing fewer outcomes coarsens `≃_k`; withholding an outcome callers do not need can make a key commutative (cf. the scalable commutativity rule)."],[4608,"*Running an inverse withdraws the fiber's contribution and nothing else.*"],[8330,"*service resolution* (which `inject` declarations admit access)"],[7511,"*special* properties (symbols, `prototype`, `then`, numeric strings, names starting with `_`) bypass mediation;"],[1321,"*不*计划引入可选的 `loom`：单锁设计没有需要建模的无锁状态。"],[925,"*代表调用者*创建的效应使用 `svc.caller().effect(..)`：它们落在调用者的纤程中，这正是 Cordis 的 tracker 借助 `this.ctx` 所实现的效果。"],[183,"*接口设计规则（来自定义 31）*：公开更少的结果会使 `≃_k` 更粗；隐藏调用者不需要的结果可以使一个键变得可交换（参见可扩展交换性规则（scalable commutativity rule））。"],[4066,"*效应*、*拦截*、*隔离*"],[4069,"*服务解析*（哪些 `inject` 声明允许访问）"],[3250,"*特殊*属性（符号、`prototype`、`then`、数字字符串、以 `_` 开头的名称）绕过中介；"],[346,"*界限*：表只在每个键的 `≃_k` 意义下被恢复：单调分配器不会被回拨，堆布局不会被恢复，已发送的消息依然是已发送的。"],[344,"*运行一个逆操作只撤回该纤程的贡献，不多也不少。*"],[4171,"\\~1,210"],[8432,"\\~1,210"],[4159,"\\~1,430"],[8420,"\\~1,430"],[4195,"\\~140"],[8456,"\\~140"],[4189,"\\~150"],[8450,"\\~150"],[4183,"\\~170"],[8444,"\\~170"],[4153,"\\~2,030"],[8414,"\\~2,030"],[4201,"\\~240"],[8462,"\\~240"],[4213,"\\~400"],[8474,"\\~400"],[4177,"\\~790"],[8438,"\\~790"],[4207,"\\~960"],[8468,"\\~960"],[1354,"#"],[5615,"#"],[3505,"`_disposables`"],[7766,"`_disposables`"],[3795,"`_disposing`"],[8056,