],[5376,"How these were settled in the code:"],[7237,"How this documentation is organised"],[7217,"How to use kardia: config files, plugins, services, effects, the loader, hot reload and guest plugins."],[5006,"How to work on kardia: building and testing, the xtask commands, CI, releasing to crates.io and npm, and the documentation site."],[6716,"How values are located:"],[1148,"id、`Root`/`Context`/`Scope`、`IdTable`、效应（effect）引擎（`effect_sync`、`effect`、`EffectScope`、`EffectHandle`）、`provide`/`try_get_live`、isolate/intercept 叠加层；仅根纤程（fiber）"],[5259,"Identifiers (`key.rs`)"],[5258,"Identifiers, scope overlays, bindings, fibers, targets and committed views, IdTable and dependency-cycle detection in kardia-core."],[5803,"Identifies the entry across edits. Missing ids are generated, and written to the file with the next write-back."],[4385,"Identify providers by a **never-reused id**, so that \"replaced by an equal value\" still triggers a reload."],[7553,"identity effect (nothing to undo)"],[4822,"identity: `id_Γ` is the unit."],[7968,"ids invented for id-less file entries"],[5409,"ids, `Root`/`Context`/`Scope`, `IdTable`, effect engine (`effect_sync`, `effect`, `EffectScope`, `EffectHandle`), `provide`/`try_get_live`, isolate/intercept overlays; root fiber only"],[4613,"If `m` committed key `k` to provider `n`, then throughout `m`'s episode: `ω_m(k) = n`; `n`'s episode strictly contains `m`'s (`b < b′`, and `u′ < u` if `n` closes), so **a provider outlives its consumers**; the binding `k` stays in `σ_n` and moves only by operations at `k` of fibers declaring `k`."],[6953,"If a declared service goes away, it unloads and waits in `Pending`."],[6952,"If a declared service is replaced by another binding, it unloads and loads again against the new one."],[5840,"If it fails"],[7818,"if loaded, `waterfall(fiber, 'internal/update', resolved, restart)`: per-fiber `internal/update` listeners (registered by the plugin via `ctx.on('internal/update', …)`) may accept the new config *