ithms 2–3) and §5.1.4 (Algorithm 6), both in Implementation."],[7619,"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/events.ts` and `logger.ts`. In the paper, event listeners are the canonical *commutative key* (\"registration takes an entry of its own\", §3.4.2, see The context paradigm); the logger is an example of interception metadata."],[7545,"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/fiber.ts:60-363` and `utils.ts`. The paper counterpart is §3.1 and Algorithm 1; see Revertible effects."],[7711,"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/fiber.ts` and `registry.ts`. The paper counterparts are §4.1–4.2 (the calculus, see Calculus) and §5.1.3 (Algorithms 4–5, see Implementation)."],[8320,"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/service.ts` and `utils.ts:113-238`. The paper counterparts are §5.1.4 (context access, see Implementation) and §6.3 (capabilities, see Discussion and related work). The mechanism is mostly *implicit* in the paper, but it is essential for temporal composability in practice."],[7863,"This page covers `cordis/packages/hmr/src/index.ts` and `error.ts`, plus `core/src/registry.ts:185-209` and `core/src/fiber.ts:401-416` (see `registry.replace`). The paper counterpart is §5.2.2, Algorithms 8–10; see Implementation."],[7947,"This page covers `cordis/packages/include/src/{index,journal,patch}.ts` and `packages/group/src/index.ts`. The paper counterpart is §5.2.1 (\"`@cordisjs/include` loads an external configuration file (YAML or JSON) and grafts its entries in as a nested subtree\", see Implementation). The paper does not describe the synchronization machinery below; it is an implementation contribution."],[8033,"This page covers `cordis/packages/loader/src/**`. The paper counterparts are §5.2.1 *Declarative configuration* (see Implementation) and §4.4 *Configuration* (see Metatheory). File:line references on this page are relative to `packages/loader/src/`."],[5165,"This page covers the public API of `kardia-core` and the built-in plugin crates: