either a plugin nor a value exports nothing."],[4888,"When a component is removed, every modification it made to the shared environment is completely and safely reversed (resources, event registrations, state mutations), in an orderly way."],[6659,"When an entry's effective realms change (a new `isolate`, or a move to another group), a binding provided from inside the entry **migrates** to the new realm without restarting its provider, as long as the new realm is free; the consumers of both realms re-resolve. A shared realm is released once no entry uses its label for that service any more."],[5848,"When the entry starts or changes"],[5842,"When the entry starts or changes, in the entry's context (which sees its `inject`); the result's truthiness decides"],[6314,"When the guest instance itself fails, rather than the guest reporting an error, the call fails with a `kardia::hmr::GuestFailure`: its `kind` (a `GuestFailureKind`) says how, and its text is the error's message, unchanged. `GuestFailure::of(&error)` finds it in a `kardia_core::Error`, and so does `error.downcast_ref::<GuestFailure>()`. An error the guest reports itself (a failure status, or an error the SDK returns), a missing export, a disposed instance or a call that waited too long for another one to finish is not a `GuestFailure`; the instance keeps running."],[6006,"When the setup itself can fail, or registers several inverses, write it as an effect body. The body gets an `EffectScope` to collect inverses into."],[5106,"Where"],[5838,"Where"],[5317,"Where `kardia-loader` differs from the table:"],[6585,"where a value is written (see errors)"],[6653,"where char `offset` of the expression `expr` at `path` is written"],[7117,"Where Cordis uses waterfall events (`internal/config`, `internal/get`, `internal/update`), kardia has typed hooks. Each registration is an effect:"],[7187,"Where it differs from Kardia and Cordis is listed on Implementation status."],[7024,"Where metadata comes from, outermost first: