y it matters for a port"],[4326,"Why the guard does not deadlock: once a provider is marked (L-Leave or L-Divert) its table leaves `σ_γ`, so no target view can name it any longer, and every consumer committed to it is itself on its way out (Theorem 73, see Metatheory)."],[4990,"Why the model matters"],[6806,"With `Injected<D>`, `ctx.get::<S, _>()` compiles only if `S` is in `D` (the `_` is the inferred position of `S` in `D`). `Injected` dereferences to `Context`, so everything else on `Context` is available; `ctx.context()` gives the unchecked context."],[6438,"With `watch.enabled` and a non-empty `files` list, `hmr` logs `watching [..] in <base>` and starts a watch below itself that waits for `fs`. If `fs` is there, the watch is set up before `hmr` settles; a failure to set it up is logged."],[6308,"with limits, an export out of fuel or time traps, and the instance fails its later calls"],[4630,"With realms fixed at insertion, the relaxed calculus is the present one over keys `K × R`: a fiber under realm table `ρ` declares and provides `(k, ρ(k))`; disjointness becomes \"disjoint within a realm\". Reassigning a realm at runtime changes a fiber's interface, so it is handled as a *revision*. Interception needs no extension: metadata is consulted at access time and is in no fiber field."],[6760,"With the facade crate `kardia`, both macros take `crate = ::kardia`. The generated code refers to `::kardia_core` by default, which only works if you depend on `kardia-core` directly."],[6910,"Without `name`, the key is the type name hyphenated: `Database` → `database`, `FooBar` → `foo-bar`. `#[service(crate = …)]` points the generated code at `::kardia`; without it, it refers to `::kardia_core`."],[7369,"Without an argument, the binary reads `kardia.yml` from the working directory. See Installation for the requirements."],[4862,"Witness"],[5345,"Worked example"],[5043,"Workflow"],[5590,"Workspace layout"],[5406,"Workspace, crates, CI (fmt, clippy, test)"],[6134,"Write plugin